se},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"10bcba25600e51aba135f170b34aa6315c0f53d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/10bcba25600e51aba135f170b34aa6315c0f53d6","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/10bcba25600e51aba135f170b34aa6315c0f53d6"}]},{"sha":"10bcba25600e51aba135f170b34aa6315c0f53d6","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDEwYmNiYTI1NjAwZTUxYWJhMTM1ZjE3MGIzNGFhNjMxNWMwZjUzZDY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Colin Francis","email":"131073567+colifran@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-25T06:57:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T06:57:24Z"},"message":"feat(code,quickjs): dynamic subagents UI (#4221)\n\n### Summary\n\nThis PR implements a `dcode` ui for dynamic subagents (see attached\nimages). The implementation on the quickjs side adds code to emit\nsubagent events into a stream writer using the `custom` channel. `dcode`\nthen reads these events from the stream and is able to reliably classify\nsubagent events using the `subagent` stream event type.\n\n### Tests\nUnit tests and e2e testing with `dcode` to verify and validate quality +\nbehavior.\n\n### Dynamic Subagents UI\nCollapsed:\n<img width=\"1728\" height=\"1024\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-24 at 7 52\n56 AM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/34cece20-e072-40e2-a46d-20567583f252\"\n/>\n\nExpanded:\n<img width=\"1728\" height=\"1016\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-24 at 7 48\n42 AM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/01e83427-aeee-44f0-b29c-d9f1792db76f\"\n/>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Sydney Runkle <54324534+sydney-runkle@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","tree":{"sha":"f059017ffdc123f36455f932cb2facaeda64e441","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/f059017ffdc123f36455f932cb2facaeda64e441"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/10bcba25600e51aba135f170b34aa6315c0f53d6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPNFUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhZQQAFdbB2qfiQ10+7dvVdJ+lEJn\nqjHDBh5K2qfjvf/4b+GOWAca53DoHE2a5RQmHiO8kaywJpqcgyUtbTIpXnHPtq32\nXh8Jfbw3Vky+ybVtRMq+gMjpQcMXKE7eM4nsKfZ+EFIOpMZxoDwdo9KJ88iZWkW8\nNQ7XgRzjjSfII5FbY3obfScX06Ahp5PlhDN8Fuw5ChktLTCR83XkxidkVEE8Z0Im\n/wLfecnTa5ByyOCOdaV1wIhsQQ5a5ehEavGRP32PmVd8exuZAl4/4ybU21+W0kOG\nnE2SWlzxzubiNolKWITKSxXKrbWgW0BauFdHxDXhEPzraFuMRiJdLPtI/Uqta5PR\n6oVajCIre4gDcW1NgbpclSOR+YajcppSztdahQS4Ny/9ynboCf3upPwBR7LtxSqU\nc8UKE6Ebsovpa3wODdZ2KqUAblpThV7WfmZgliqV+w952IGxVJVdOr+nHaKsT99K\nLV6dpuUqgcM38JlqNQxbsZxtPfNcKxWb7IKNeXijDv6gRRKyGtEgXOksExTn8ZDZ\n6TQD5RADyVvfpEJCHxDekfmAzt6/gspnRMntLJUQgeiNN/CUosDoDffGhlYiu7ys\ndvT97+dV+JlfFUxZgY0aNZkxWplIKyS5JVOcw2rmiIAJ46hPW8dkKcVyXFrbY13A\nyirCD3RYFvve9yHJLMAV\n=VoXv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f059017ffdc123f36455f932cb2facaeda64e441\nparent cf536f339958d6726fa41f896c4a3e42df644c9f\nauthor Colin Francis <131073567+colifran@users.noreply.github.com> 1782370644 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782370644 -0400\n\nfeat(code,quickjs): dynamic subagents UI (#4221)\n\n### Summary\n\nThis PR implements a `dcode` ui for dynamic subagents (see attached\nimages). The implementation on the quickjs side adds code to emit\nsubagent events into a stream writer using the `custom` channel. `dcode`\nthen reads these events from the stream and is able to reliably classify\nsubagent events using the `subagent` stream event type.\n\n### Tests\nUnit tests and e2e testing with `dcode` to verify and validate quality +\nbehavior.\n\n### Dynamic Subagents UI\nCollapsed:\n<img width=\"1728\" height=\"1024\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-24 at 7 52\n56 AM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/34cece20-e072-40e2-a46d-20567583f252\"\n/>\n\nExpanded:\n<img width=\"1728\" height=\"1016\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-24 at 7 48\n42 AM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/01e83427-aeee-44f0-b29c-d9f1792db76f\"\n/>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Sydney Runkle <54324534+sydney-runkle@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","verified_at":"2026-06-25T06:57:25Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/10bcba25600e51aba135f170b34aa6315c0f53d6","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/10bcba25600e51aba135f170b34aa6315c0f53d6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/10bcba25600e51aba135f170b34aa6315c0f53d6/comments","author":{"login":"colifran","id":131073567,"node_id":"U_kgDOB9AGHw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131073567?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/colifran","html_url":"https://github.com/colifran","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colifran/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colifran/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colifran/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colifran/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colifran/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colifran/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colifran/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colifran/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colifran/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cf536f339958d6726fa41f896c4a3e42df644c9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cf536f339958d6726fa41f896c4a3e42df644c9f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cf536f339958d6726fa41f896c4a3e42df644c9f"}]},{"sha":"cf536f339958d6726fa41f896c4a3e42df644c9f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGNmNTM2ZjMzOTk1OGQ2NzI2ZmE0MWY4OTZjNGEzZTQyZGY2NDRjOWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-25T05:28:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T05:28:38Z"},"message":"fix(code): eager managed ripgrep install via `dcode tools install` (#4199)\n\n`dcode tools install` provisions the managed ripgrep binary; the install\nscript now sets it up by default (opt out with\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_RIPGREP_INSTALLER=system` or\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_OFFLINE=1`).\n\n---\n\nToday the pinned, SHA-256-verified ripgrep binary only lands on first\nrun (via `managed_tools.ensure_ripgrep`), so a fresh user pays a\none-time download the first time they launch. This makes the install\nscript provision it eagerly so `rg` is ready immediately, without\nreaching for `sudo` package managers by default.\n\nRather than re-encoding the pinned version + checksum table in bash\n(drift risk), a new `dcode tools install` verb reuses the existing\nmanaged-install code, and `scripts/install.sh` invokes the freshly\ninstalled binary. The verb is also handy on its own to repair a missing\nor stale `rg`.\n\nPower users can keep their own toolchain with\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_RIPGREP_INSTALLER=system`, which preserves the existing\nbrew/apt/cargo path in the install script and skips the managed download\nat runtime. A system `rg` already on `PATH` is reused under either\nsetting, and `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_OFFLINE` / `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_SKIP_OPTIONAL`\ncontinue to apply. The default eager install is announced and honors\nthose opt-outs, per the package's \"default shell-outs must announce +\noffer a documented opt-out\" rule.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"1a3c50645c00aed36a34cc3ccb5bb675b7fb0f30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/1a3c50645c00aed36a34cc3ccb5bb675b7fb0f30"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/cf536f339958d6726fa41f896c4a3e42df644c9f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPLyGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiLUQAFhD1YJeU/F4n68mxaFxyz0v\nWQvvQ+03J7zNhNirnQtWT1AFOg2NCnVIWm+DUcIhIUZZbfqU96Ib05jF6AqL9uFz\nQm9YruPpYAEbHEzi10p9RxHgeCejfYLDSLDlD1GDgeUmHUF4yCbF7BFTYg9GVZH/\nvMsBiZ8AeM8ApIrSC1fy9iTrXSTFg6w45RG4XwssszYCJ1YNFtlK4Ih8m9RBzItT\nEJ+BdfOyQdjvw052I0XAEaaFFUKtHhVJm9UVH2+r9vt06AuoAKV3RKw5J8TW17e/\n+SsrhogfFExzu/BW4lk4+E8yCuR6heY+eybniXTIxHJGbd1U4s7tu9j7WkHUd4pm\nTqHngfsjpFmzrd/xWJqyFMmXD5uB+WS1+Bnci8dRgXmxvoofgdy82kjDHc4pK5GI\nC5NRdZL3b1LN7upCH2gnmsd7QdIZmbm1+ifZnHt/uS2znjrVoxjXEXEixsZryWvB\nc/44jaadQQDX820tpe/ed6ZqTBjrTDLU1PnhgTS8s4CRw5RYxtCD80g1LBF5h/ck\n0xNSfqrdbsUfVuDOcUouPuQVkSOJjStxvRFuLaldXD+qi5S3vHfT08k1jCLqu4v/\nyhWZzTtvPJwHIHEtJh10luCWgZxqo0ct4gxovABps+y4YdIVnBQCm0gQmMPe9ZeO\neIsB71qIVzs0CZ7w+J6H\n=XdYf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1a3c50645c00aed36a34cc3ccb5bb675b7fb0f30\nparent 37c5fa23e621616836694bc59c1b0c38def81604\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782365318 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782365318 -0400\n\nfix(code): eager managed ripgrep install via `dcode tools install` (#4199)\n\n`dcode tools install` provisions the managed ripgrep binary; the install\nscript now sets it up by default (opt out with\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_RIPGREP_INSTALLER=system` or\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_OFFLINE=1`).\n\n---\n\nToday the pinned, SHA-256-verified ripgrep binary only lands on first\nrun (via `managed_tools.ensure_ripgrep`), so a fresh user pays a\none-time download the first time they launch. This makes the install\nscript provision it eagerly so `rg` is ready immediately, without\nreaching for `sudo` package managers by default.\n\nRather than re-encoding the pinned version + checksum table in bash\n(drift risk), a new `dcode tools install` verb reuses the existing\nmanaged-install code, and `scripts/install.sh` invokes the freshly\ninstalled binary. The verb is also handy on its own to repair a missing\nor stale `rg`.\n\nPower users can keep their own toolchain with\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_RIPGREP_INSTALLER=system`, which preserves the existing\nbrew/apt/cargo path in the install script and skips the managed download\nat runtime. A system `rg` already on `PATH` is reused under either\nsetting, and `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_OFFLINE` / `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_SKIP_OPTIONAL`\ncontinue to apply. The default eager install is announced and honors\nthose opt-outs, per the package's \"default shell-outs must announce +\noffer a documented opt-out\" rule.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-25T05:28:39Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cf536f339958d6726fa41f896c4a3e42df644c9f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cf536f339958d6726fa41f896c4a3e42df644c9f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cf536f339958d6726fa41f896c4a3e42df644c9f/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"37c5fa23e621616836694bc59c1b0c38def81604","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/37c5fa23e621616836694bc59c1b0c38def81604","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/37c5fa23e621616836694bc59c1b0c38def81604"}]},{"sha":"37c5fa23e621616836694bc59c1b0c38def81604","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDM3YzVmYTIzZTYyMTYxNjgzNjY5NGJjNTljMWIwYzM4ZGVmODE2MDQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nick Hollon","email":"nick.hollon@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-25T04:57:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T04:57:30Z"},"message":"fix(code): interrupt remote runs on chat cancellation (#4234)\n\nPressing Esc cancelled only the local Textual worker, so the LangGraph\nserver could keep remote/subgraph runs active until a later state-write\nconflict. Interrupt cleanup now explicitly cancels active remote runs\nbefore persisting recovery state, while keeping the cleanup best-effort\nfor local agents.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/d68b606b-4b3c-5278-0cab-51b79c3d5af4)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick Hollon <274035459+nick-hollon-lc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"c7fa8bf28c7c10e18acc1c1c09ab55da3154600d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c7fa8bf28c7c10e18acc1c1c09ab55da3154600d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/37c5fa23e621616836694bc59c1b0c38def81604","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPLU6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiawQAAQ64RNzlB8BoRdaaJOIOLR9\n27izZMhnYUSdC1CKL29OpZPDC73jhEQAxc9SK3LNxWx+RxlfpCVcUxmMA4uUs29O\nQCYZ9TTCG8CL2urm/nL2kcwZnORsMnZFoeqbOoeHG/NJvC6LupeNNcSaIVT522uh\nU1x9TUZacmXqYO124Rp5LZz64rhoGrsLLdBn+n2ssb4EoZypCOuyG0wtnadluF5z\nEkE6UukmNYSYfMXV4QtIeJRgs6oYlszMAbN34qu2FPVqTxQyhDOeD13w8aX8P/Ua\nKeu8snpwfB5LeVxUz9UXIj2sOYurewQU2j+DRENCYhtYMztvm8McABWX+7yhhoky\nub7ybZGy2+DCbTAXADEyKLhlAtrJfeXLz/BxiXzVb/m14L0Y2qyJ3mBh/GiwoWhz\nMCvpQbMPDwmtTM+tEy+3TKW0tk+sGIdOT9E3kMSz5ZXA44DbaBsYIV/lFqJLT/Zl\n4ohQzjPhq5rzNxiQcJlRWVMF48G6TUE+6nb3Iurmj9mbPjjxTp7M42jQTYEkO1ef\nAxZ0alw8PxeayDLGIilSmVOaD1YY4QnwMpQgU4+h5Y3s/sBRwr+JjVExpOOsayNo\nIM9kK86jYLPb7WO6xFHfy+ErtBjJycdpY1+Zys4+gBzggUjq7aaOCjh2V6elypEy\npXLJgKvnFKwqlWLx3fEU\n=gd7e\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c7fa8bf28c7c10e18acc1c1c09ab55da3154600d\nparent cc2b8d1d7546b0297bc0fac675e6e27e4935dd8c\nauthor Nick Hollon <nick.hollon@langchain.dev> 1782363450 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782363450 -0400\n\nfix(code): interrupt remote runs on chat cancellation (#4234)\n\nPressing Esc cancelled only the local Textual worker, so the LangGraph\nserver could keep remote/subgraph runs active until a later state-write\nconflict. Interrupt cleanup now explicitly cancels active remote runs\nbefore persisting recovery state, while keeping the cleanup best-effort\nfor local agents.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/d68b606b-4b3c-5278-0cab-51b79c3d5af4)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick Hollon <274035459+nick-hollon-lc@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-25T04:57:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/37c5fa23e621616836694bc59c1b0c38def81604","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/37c5fa23e621616836694bc59c1b0c38def81604","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/37c5fa23e621616836694bc59c1b0c38def81604/comments","author":{"login":"nick-hollon-lc","id":274035459,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFVzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274035459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc","html_url":"https://github.com/nick-hollon-lc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cc2b8d1d7546b0297bc0fac675e6e27e4935dd8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cc2b8d1d7546b0297bc0fac675e6e27e4935dd8c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cc2b8d1d7546b0297bc0fac675e6e27e4935dd8c"}]},{"sha":"cc2b8d1d7546b0297bc0fac675e6e27e4935dd8c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGNjMmI4ZDFkNzU0NmIwMjk3YmMwZmFjNjc1ZTZlMjdlNDkzNWRkOGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-25T04:33:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T04:33:10Z"},"message":"style(code): pointer cursor when hovering markdown links (#4240)\n\nHovering over links in assistant markdown now shows the pointer cursor.\n\n---\n\nHovering over URLs in rendered assistant markdown showed the plain text\ncursor. This detects link spans under the mouse (both OSC 8\n`Style(link=...)` and the `@click=link(...)` meta actions Textual's\n`Markdown` attaches to links/images) and switches the inner `Markdown`\nwidget's pointer to `pointer`, resetting it to `text` otherwise.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/957519a2-ca36-ca25-0858-04f366a8eb46)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"bafd5fc8f96d920a2d84f6c31c75d9b5a34f033e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/bafd5fc8f96d920a2d84f6c31c75d9b5a34f033e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/cc2b8d1d7546b0297bc0fac675e6e27e4935dd8c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPK+GCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUXkQADj+n/ebK1r5y1B3tdXpAu3W\nq33wLTAk+2vb+YMUZaPSWrLe/+eGPsYMIKtzs7NaOtBSRJnWtj1gQ6FG4Z2Bu/OV\n0pBYKi6hTJZgDzgQK5ekSjX9CU3lm48RjOnQ4dZA/FgPhj03FOZa+nsNSCaZ9pHc\nPjhC4gVIUZQd6UaeBSPJQk9zs7K3VKOjVg6EsMqrDhh0LEqTMOeQcTpeofVdIzj1\nSMQd2VnP32Y3PiiBKxrFOfB8XTfRQM7gol1tucHenZhyqR8guR9iC+xDGHjjDZae\nO72fokdBVlofu1i++LjPIOlVE4xPDRjFU6gMTsJ6O4UtEFBwIlFZJNLVy+rDxBxS\nwFX9Tr4SERqH9qVmAaaZHv6oDrCdqVRUOgB2QGz81F01NtTt7L8ED+S6l3m+TwTA\nUBsehQd5QWiabRc5adhta4iXK64YScPhMr8/6FGH1eJnXepBMKY2AqL/TsynM4D9\niaLcLGUMzKKpf2f1ifOw/YMrw0munC+kwQQ8l1r/LO8vPYxyLnz02krqy4m2oRyF\nRCOrNLinyHmDf+0o16eV0kGKNrIpGx8s579Kz7MCWQd79dlsvReQInbshjyNtGPu\n6U85wqFEg/0aqKc5x8uzgxomaXnXbxTM3v20Q37evfJwYPp0xAMTelXqE9xGyNP/\ntxtzAxWuUF6mX2cC23Ir\n=73Dr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree bafd5fc8f96d920a2d84f6c31c75d9b5a34f033e\nparent f11a76962c9d536a38e27ac05b32feca364b2424\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782361990 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782361990 -0400\n\nstyle(code): pointer cursor when hovering markdown links (#4240)\n\nHovering over links in assistant markdown now shows the pointer cursor.\n\n---\n\nHovering over URLs in rendered assistant markdown showed the plain text\ncursor. This detects link spans under the mouse (both OSC 8\n`Style(link=...)` and the `@click=link(...)` meta actions Textual's\n`Markdown` attaches to links/images) and switches the inner `Markdown`\nwidget's pointer to `pointer`, resetting it to `text` otherwise.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/957519a2-ca36-ca25-0858-04f366a8eb46)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-25T04:33:10Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cc2b8d1d7546b0297bc0fac675e6e27e4935dd8c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cc2b8d1d7546b0297bc0fac675e6e27e4935dd8c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cc2b8d1d7546b0297bc0fac675e6e27e4935dd8c/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f11a76962c9d536a38e27ac05b32feca364b2424","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f11a76962c9d536a38e27ac05b32feca364b2424","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f11a76962c9d536a38e27ac05b32feca364b2424"}]},{"sha":"f11a76962c9d536a38e27ac05b32feca364b2424","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGYxMWE3Njk2MmM5ZDUzNmEzOGUyN2FjMDViMzJmZWNhMzY0YjI0MjQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-25T04:20:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T04:20:16Z"},"message":"fix(code): clear stale live approval mode keys (#4242)\n\nWhen a user turns live approval mode on or off, the app keeps a session\nkey for the live approval-mode state so it can update or clean up that\nstate later. If the current agent cannot provide that live state writer,\nthe app should treat the write as failed and forget any old key instead\nof holding on to stale state.\n\nThe user story is: a user toggles live approval mode while a session is\nactive, but the active agent is one that can run without writing to the\nshared live approval-mode store. That can happen with local or\nin-process agents, older/custom agent wrappers, test doubles, or\npartially initialized agents that do not expose the remote store writer\nused for live approval-mode updates. In that situation, keeping an old\nkey would make the app think it still has a valid live approval-mode\nrecord even though the current agent cannot update it.\n\nThis change makes the no-writer case fail safely. The app clears the\nstale key, reports the write as unsuccessful, and falls back to the\nexisting approval behavior instead of carrying an outdated live\napproval-mode key into later tool approval checks.","tree":{"sha":"c5792c348f95ad33ac688443e3cfe6181a8ac679","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c5792c348f95ad33ac688443e3cfe6181a8ac679"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f11a76962c9d536a38e27ac05b32feca364b2424","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPKyACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfx4QAGD9g40yRQhAmBkUMhpvxIPZ\nec+ll/vBjqun4JBhpzdICw8szNHx4XAGkMEHgH2UJAFly5d8QiPTvIWO5aeX1o6j\nuzz43WenX5Iqt5VdbexxXK2C8M285IxxGhNnN4tmvIw06I6Y+vBjofwfPd0GIRTG\nzdRFjDbVpH/oC7drDzpMp0N1okm54xDp2kjlceBn9HthehD2Ydm6/JOQC1QM1MPG\nXVDgf69ZAL2U/NkB3aV6HfFw7oF4+6OhNL+Notbbmcx266cyZyTsmY0iUCxeeFb4\nCbijQliKCakxtvcDQ3YbueEMeXx6dfFAqGzbmNUiaWM8Td1ICE0MZzTILD89sv2I\n0Z1b+W5ZtI/m6Xx/U7W0t76KjWRHcQ0svuruMjIVC8aAt7WxBV+OHFBxDr2inznL\nVJXZ5hgw4SHt8P0rEWfRnHoKGnF/1s6v9Ksr0BD5pPeomorD7rqp7GM+bbT21sEH\n/dbEAezWD8yEnaPJnoHNmDie+VJwwA7E60tVcCvnEr1GE4z5ugUI4Jo+OtbMmWrj\nuCyZRfyWoKAop9UgrkbgRYtmQ16qkpSMgDFcVRxUr2fMfSCdIXBnINChWLoaQRRR\nSreoW9vQd8Dl/RHuJS0cJxKc9CApziqPPhq8gZMC/kePEnxtXcGTuxB7rZIF/SLR\n+TUPtsDqjtj+hinfXvvP\n=/bNR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c5792c348f95ad33ac688443e3cfe6181a8ac679\nparent 6c930c5e4502f572be554acc896c5fb6d061e0e5\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782361216 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782361216 -0400\n\nfix(code): clear stale live approval mode keys (#4242)\n\nWhen a user turns live approval mode on or off, the app keeps a session\nkey for the live approval-mode state so it can update or clean up that\nstate later. If the current agent cannot provide that live state writer,\nthe app should treat the write as failed and forget any old key instead\nof holding on to stale state.\n\nThe user story is: a user toggles live approval mode while a session is\nactive, but the active agent is one that can run without writing to the\nshared live approval-mode store. That can happen with local or\nin-process agents, older/custom agent wrappers, test doubles, or\npartially initialized agents that do not expose the remote store writer\nused for live approval-mode updates. In that situation, keeping an old\nkey would make the app think it still has a valid live approval-mode\nrecord even though the current agent cannot update it.\n\nThis change makes the no-writer case fail safely. The app clears the\nstale key, reports the write as unsuccessful, and falls back to the\nexisting approval behavior instead of carrying an outdated live\napproval-mode key into later tool approval checks.","verified_at":"2026-06-25T04:20:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f11a76962c9d536a38e27ac05b32feca364b2424","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f11a76962c9d536a38e27ac05b32feca364b2424","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f11a76962c9d536a38e27ac05b32feca364b2424/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6c930c5e4502f572be554acc896c5fb6d061e0e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6c930c5e4502f572be554acc896c5fb6d061e0e5","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6c930c5e4502f572be554acc896c5fb6d061e0e5"}]},{"sha":"6c930c5e4502f572be554acc896c5fb6d061e0e5","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDZjOTMwYzVlNDUwMmY1NzJiZTU1NGFjYzg5NmM1ZmI2ZDA2MWUwZTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-25T04:02:48Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T04:02:48Z"},"message":"feat(code): gate onboarding integrations modal behind opt-in flag (#4227)\n\nStreamlined first-run onboarding: the integrations summary screen is now\noff by default (model selection handles provider installs); re-enable it\nwith `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_ONBOARDING_INTEGRATIONS_SCREEN`.\n\n---\n\nThe onboarding \"Installed Integrations\" modal\n(`LaunchDependenciesScreen`) added a read-only step whose status glyphs\n(`○` / `[ ]`) read as clickable checkboxes but weren't, and it largely\nduplicated the model selector — which already surfaces uninstalled\nproviders as install-required rows and installs them on select. This\nskips it by default (onboarding goes name → model selector) while\nkeeping the screen in the repo, reachable via\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_ONBOARDING_INTEGRATIONS_SCREEN`. The curated\nmodel-selector description gains a one-line `/install` hint so sandboxes\nand other non-provider extras stay discoverable.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/03c9e178-0f75-11f1-b97b-2762e103489f)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4092e507442268ae9060a865614ee272072673f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/4092e507442268ae9060a865614ee272072673f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/6c930c5e4502f572be554acc896c5fb6d061e0e5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPKhoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPmwQAENbJV0gCIpDMEbaXkywADnX\n2gKV/e124KiIowoR88Vy1ZrKxwaQhxTmTCasyNwWyJPTJbG15cyjqXl626uCJKIS\nPF3/7DhCHMSqFroek9ltISKO43NFyxPnhMhTpIY08ag4niSm2gXYCGiBVewRBVt4\n98NGGUkkU7x8sfQH3tnUGauR7FXqGXXdGNd0ggzcKTz0cDJ4nq8bQzlo5NmpqhvU\nRi7JX64I/tmYvGCz021w39GBifg81E7QZw3RTpNj884PktIscZs3Y/fRPF6CAs+I\nYxaG3/8o2JI8Zm3u3QkkpP9POkh4cJCRE0ZdVIiZ0bpCZ2jJkcIVc6GWWbyAlcuR\nfavAEfLfnxb1qbG09Xq1eEANNId8kPmMygPG3fR1Be0B9AG6VFktuDYPDgbFjk9g\nWDyT4QjJ0iLndXah5SuDAk9waCJ7Oh6P0nBKcvfukfA5u3W40RP8utZVyyPHmIlH\nwnjSVWGGS87UxR9VUvFxCbPWuzO7gwlE3xk31KtgAbuoaCXajlW5uw6x6sDQjZvc\nH8aarIv8CgvQ1eWi99Jj6otRs4hJlxAbQ5kH7A/GjbnpzQxBWlZ5axLoW7YIK+gp\n9KAJAnSjAkYzRCthEEr0ACbkHGSeyHVaAcK1f9YSgfQAsTFtN0BcsX16ag6ts7GQ\ni0wmlPJ7z15NjObjsxFQ\n=R6RH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4092e507442268ae9060a865614ee272072673f9\nparent 4600365ea0b60c3e9113ecf59b5336be37d03428\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782360168 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782360168 -0400\n\nfeat(code): gate onboarding integrations modal behind opt-in flag (#4227)\n\nStreamlined first-run onboarding: the integrations summary screen is now\noff by default (model selection handles provider installs); re-enable it\nwith `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_ONBOARDING_INTEGRATIONS_SCREEN`.\n\n---\n\nThe onboarding \"Installed Integrations\" modal\n(`LaunchDependenciesScreen`) added a read-only step whose status glyphs\n(`○` / `[ ]`) read as clickable checkboxes but weren't, and it largely\nduplicated the model selector — which already surfaces uninstalled\nproviders as install-required rows and installs them on select. This\nskips it by default (onboarding goes name → model selector) while\nkeeping the screen in the repo, reachable via\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_ONBOARDING_INTEGRATIONS_SCREEN`. The curated\nmodel-selector description gains a one-line `/install` hint so sandboxes\nand other non-provider extras stay discoverable.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/03c9e178-0f75-11f1-b97b-2762e103489f)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-25T04:02:49Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6c930c5e4502f572be554acc896c5fb6d061e0e5","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6c930c5e4502f572be554acc896c5fb6d061e0e5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6c930c5e4502f572be554acc896c5fb6d061e0e5/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4600365ea0b60c3e9113ecf59b5336be37d03428","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4600365ea0b60c3e9113ecf59b5336be37d03428","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4600365ea0b60c3e9113ecf59b5336be37d03428"}]},{"sha":"4600365ea0b60c3e9113ecf59b5336be37d03428","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQ2MDAzNjVlYTBiNjBjM2U5MTEzZWNmNTliNTMzNmJlMzdkMDM0Mjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-25T03:12:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T03:12:40Z"},"message":"fix(code): sync approval toggles during active runs (#4239)\n\nApproval mode now has a live control path for remote `dcode` sessions\ninstead of relying only on the run-context snapshot captured at stream\nstart. That lets mid-run toggles take effect before the next gated tool\ncall, while failing closed to manual approval when the live state cannot\nbe synced or read.\n\n## Changes\n- **Live approval state:** Added `approval_mode_key`,\n`approval_mode_payload`, `read_approval_mode_from_store`, and\n`awrite_approval_mode` to store per-thread auto-approve state in the\nLangGraph Store under a deterministic hashed thread key.\n- **Interrupt decisions:** Updated `_should_interrupt_tool_call` to\nprefer the live store value over stale context, so toggling from\nauto-approve back to manual can interrupt subsequent gated tool calls in\nthe same active run.\n- **TUI synchronization:** Updated\n`DeepAgentsApp.action_toggle_auto_approve` and\n`_on_auto_approve_enabled` to write the live approval mode whenever the\nuser toggles approval behavior.\n- **Fail-closed behavior:** If manual approval cannot sync while an\nagent is running, the app warns the user and cancels the active run\nrather than allowing stale auto-approval to continue.\n- **Remote support:** Added `RemoteAgent.aput_store_item` so remote\nsessions can write unindexed LangGraph Store records used by the\nserver-side approval predicate.\n- **Context reconstruction:** Preserved `auto_approve` and\n`approval_mode_key` when dict-based runtime context is reconstructed\ninto `CLIContextSchema`.\n- **Stream propagation:** Updated `execute_task_textual` to write live\napproval state before each stream iteration and await async auto-approve\ncallbacks triggered from approval prompts.","tree":{"sha":"824e1c4a23b364d478a1ce309212dc0bb1a5b9e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/824e1c4a23b364d478a1ce309212dc0bb1a5b9e6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4600365ea0b60c3e9113ecf59b5336be37d03428","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPJyoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOFkQAGzBGcGOlbYf8AF3Vufv8DOS\n7K32G30kk0lJIiKS4wwZqxbxOSP+W9qZ88yRHLJjC+HYAUPHzjhGSktuHiBpfVOi\nxuBlp0ONLjQaUvNNkUyaF+GkS4PJz6ARw51XB2tVaOV+h6f6KtiBmegbKdNjkTFf\nE5hYHSk1LLJUg2+SdcthHpLSAqpDoGYXjOxNy3pgcVGryf4gbMhxy2EYVOhSYPyB\nJwtZEWykYJ09BLHHm9cHbYj1EM9yH0EwphuyDfEzybNU03K6dBYfaMIe7f9ojnlt\n0apyPubTrtPOCPZ6Mrii7ff0HEyXrn1Y20WcuBmbFYDiPxS+HWPSphlUvrbeEl3S\n0bjomF/zkhhHIlerpHaZ2k8kSoGwgGu8hFCypsH9u9YmlLRzGKd+JfD3pOQu+Tl+\nXaumlLk9bDNyU8YS/Vu0y94270M/WeiZcVHFSK/xvQLkMdWUpzheiHw4jyJkRe41\nmQYYZ3NbOgUt+v9fGTt5EuGCLlebXi3PsDgmv5HTXKoLUp8sbrNDZgzUBKYgG7ui\nTlI9kfAYRrDTptffLB47/61YYO45gnIfcZw9P7GM7VgBGIWVzXxpkq2ASdlZCfAR\nMhXpiREP9kC/M8qacqrDckmqD/Ce4sL1ViQPeMUCqBuDg/o3mo/UhNKmrRqDDp2K\nvhSyeBkBZAq8NLi/aF1L\n=5XBg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 824e1c4a23b364d478a1ce309212dc0bb1a5b9e6\nparent 649443a42601f48aa0cd9d4f947fdcaa0ff5e9ab\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782357160 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782357160 -0400\n\nfix(code): sync approval toggles during active runs (#4239)\n\nApproval mode now has a live control path for remote `dcode` sessions\ninstead of relying only on the run-context snapshot captured at stream\nstart. That lets mid-run toggles take effect before the next gated tool\ncall, while failing closed to manual approval when the live state cannot\nbe synced or read.\n\n## Changes\n- **Live approval state:** Added `approval_mode_key`,\n`approval_mode_payload`, `read_approval_mode_from_store`, and\n`awrite_approval_mode` to store per-thread auto-approve state in the\nLangGraph Store under a deterministic hashed thread key.\n- **Interrupt decisions:** Updated `_should_interrupt_tool_call` to\nprefer the live store value over stale context, so toggling from\nauto-approve back to manual can interrupt subsequent gated tool calls in\nthe same active run.\n- **TUI synchronization:** Updated\n`DeepAgentsApp.action_toggle_auto_approve` and\n`_on_auto_approve_enabled` to write the live approval mode whenever the\nuser toggles approval behavior.\n- **Fail-closed behavior:** If manual approval cannot sync while an\nagent is running, the app warns the user and cancels the active run\nrather than allowing stale auto-approval to continue.\n- **Remote support:** Added `RemoteAgent.aput_store_item` so remote\nsessions can write unindexed LangGraph Store records used by the\nserver-side approval predicate.\n- **Context reconstruction:** Preserved `auto_approve` and\n`approval_mode_key` when dict-based runtime context is reconstructed\ninto `CLIContextSchema`.\n- **Stream propagation:** Updated `execute_task_textual` to write live\napproval state before each stream iteration and await async auto-approve\ncallbacks triggered from approval prompts.","verified_at":"2026-06-25T03:12:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4600365ea0b60c3e9113ecf59b5336be37d03428","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4600365ea0b60c3e9113ecf59b5336be37d03428","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4600365ea0b60c3e9113ecf59b5336be37d03428/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"649443a42601f48aa0cd9d4f947fdcaa0ff5e9ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/649443a42601f48aa0cd9d4f947fdcaa0ff5e9ab","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/649443a42601f48aa0cd9d4f947fdcaa0ff5e9ab"}]},{"sha":"649443a42601f48aa0cd9d4f947fdcaa0ff5e9ab","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDY0OTQ0M2E0MjYwMWY0OGFhMGNkOWQ0Zjk0N2ZkY2FhMGZmNWU5YWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-25T01:55:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T01:55:13Z"},"message":"hotfix(code): remove obsolete empty filesystem result middleware (#4238)\n\nThe `deepagents-code` release failed because the published SDK now\nreturns `No files found` for empty filesystem listings. That means the\ntemporary `_FilesystemEmptyResultMiddleware` canary did its job: the\nupstream behavior changed and the compatibility middleware is no longer\nneeded for the release artifact.\\n\\nThis removes the obsolete\n`deepagents-code` middleware and its tests so the release check can pass\nagainst the current pinned published SDK behavior.\\n\\nVerified\nwith:\\n\\n- `make -C libs/code lint`\\n- `make -C libs/code test COV_ARGS=\nPYTEST_EXTRA=\"--no-cov -q\"`","tree":{"sha":"4af544cd752eee1959b01fea94f9b59617a51ae5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/4af544cd752eee1959b01fea94f9b59617a51ae5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/649443a42601f48aa0cd9d4f947fdcaa0ff5e9ab","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPIqBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjHUQAF4ekgsYf7SONNgr6Nz4x2Ll\nfokZ01he5B4E8qTnKYvixUzDCINHwPjTWk6P15Tvfruudo4etEur9W9KT53/8gAf\njx9eALWLGPxMq08WatAvMq2XVry9w08trr65nLGKsq39R2ZJf4zgvw4/uGHSIfGQ\nYEIM9LCd5BWQbvc6YAuGMqDNBc6AhusGNVW0pCVawzzoeRXs/fsZ7oFX1bgQcmxa\nmJVhZM0etwMFHwvxIoEViPPrljomdex962AO8udrUt+evrMHBurnmA7VGNVnWOPh\n/C/7H3jUdT7vKtwwQ84qVUpdppWTDxEqwtHp8E6Bbn6/T3dSp6X15UuypuNyjDPa\nQMm/3qDUU6U6xoxhI+U/UP//z9yTIk0CEVNss9jQWXrwg9tukrA7wywtlF9f8BCD\nK0pQIsVZ3+BwoGFM/lvEu5C6w85F37jEtHGEOxSzkjk0ip7jIV5zhg31QU4QttAy\nslWV6H1ip+DLb8Zw6W6gKEU29DdaigPqFznsuHZt/I9dro8B3vs6bXrkQ/qRy0na\nAuT3/uO5tje8Z2e1KH2AQRZUoPOI5Nf2n6lgOB3do0nkZr1Al2FyoMLpIt5FCfy1\ne3eE+bGX1MMi9Eb+f2zoSGe8tv0t6U9creKJql1b/gGp0wtDjI5Lt3qA5FT6u4EL\nvpWCI7jco9ZAcBUgu4S9\n=pYS9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4af544cd752eee1959b01fea94f9b59617a51ae5\nparent e65f4496dfafa8168fdb00f0880750d0a1bb9a4d\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782352513 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782352513 -0400\n\nhotfix(code): remove obsolete empty filesystem result middleware (#4238)\n\nThe `deepagents-code` release failed because the published SDK now\nreturns `No files found` for empty filesystem listings. That means the\ntemporary `_FilesystemEmptyResultMiddleware` canary did its job: the\nupstream behavior changed and the compatibility middleware is no longer\nneeded for the release artifact.\\n\\nThis removes the obsolete\n`deepagents-code` middleware and its tests so the release check can pass\nagainst the current pinned published SDK behavior.\\n\\nVerified\nwith:\\n\\n- `make -C libs/code lint`\\n- `make -C libs/code test COV_ARGS=\nPYTEST_EXTRA=\"--no-cov -q\"`","verified_at":"2026-06-25T01:55:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/649443a42601f48aa0cd9d4f947fdcaa0ff5e9ab","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/649443a42601f48aa0cd9d4f947fdcaa0ff5e9ab","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/649443a42601f48aa0cd9d4f947fdcaa0ff5e9ab/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e65f4496dfafa8168fdb00f0880750d0a1bb9a4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e65f4496dfafa8168fdb00f0880750d0a1bb9a4d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e65f4496dfafa8168fdb00f0880750d0a1bb9a4d"}]},{"sha":"e65f4496dfafa8168fdb00f0880750d0a1bb9a4d","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGU2NWY0NDk2ZGZhZmE4MTY4ZmRiMDBmMDg4MDc1MGQwYTFiYjlhNGQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"github-actions[bot]","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-25T01:35:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T01:35:38Z"},"message":"release(deepagents-code): 0.1.23 (#4208)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Everything below this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.23](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.22...deepagents-code==0.1.23)\n(2026-06-25)\n\n### Features\n\n* Collect Tavily key during onboarding\n([#4233](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4233))\n([e321cba](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e321cba5701313e974f979069186680f1a39587c))\n* Surface `/auth` in `/trace not-configured` hint\n([#4206](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4206))\n([392e410](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/392e410e48639a56fda5e35b6f7f85a5215cce9c))\n* Add Opus 4.8 to recommended models\n([#4204](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4204))\n([8faf2b0](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8faf2b025f8429481a41a3e65544d26614e53589))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* `--reinstall` on `/install` so upgrades rebuild a clean env\n([#4196](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4196))\n([5e152ac](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5e152ac0256d64376f96b293f8844bc8acc993ec))\n* Suppress auto-update migration notice on fresh installs\n([#4224](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4224))\n([eb8ff80](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/eb8ff809a1b3130a261083c66a193e532095c6db))\n* Bake release commit into `dcode doctor`\n([#4225](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4225))\n([6dc0246](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6dc0246f5c6e9170e05191e1c82fad6975ac945c))\n* Drop redundant version from \"already up to date\" message\n([#4223](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4223))\n([5d080df](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5d080df2776d380214bf20ae31266b9628e4e5b0))\n* Note subscription plans unusable for Anthropic in `/auth`\n([#4207](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4207))\n([28cd19d](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/28cd19db08bacf981ab2c91195638e66072816fe))\n\n---\n\n_Everything above this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"a34658f086de1ab7038007ac3d01bbed199e340d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a34658f086de1ab7038007ac3d01bbed199e340d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/e65f4496dfafa8168fdb00f0880750d0a1bb9a4d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPIXqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAv2MQAAawJEzqzx+R0PKBqq1qI4Uy\nhyzZvJRTSlBdl6WmOj85NcAbsBxGfbIX9SSMi9TNbbP0uVIuiNoyZq5C66FBhYy7\nYgbOfggNfkzVe/c7TiaXrlWLFzpXBKXDlrzHCTaPpuWrR8FOET0dWfu7wqIc9XOY\nzcf1S2B39nqNFv7M/sj0phaKP1iZbdpvHuZrwM90hzDn2pV+ZD8ZYzWbGaHCOMPu\nWJwi5FKv9jN1YgghhN15KYOdAXJO8Z5yM9UotAk8P7sTEznQY9FuAxN+X9/Rf6O3\n4SRdFTIukY/oASMof1kVaADdSMTNhD7CV3fqDKP+BGON+RgxOUrfMdMB/5VE08xh\nVr63O+ApvxBuqJABI3SLrhbKYhxb9qGdCPvYfc90a8PMGtQZsxYjA8tMf2FNR8ZV\n/jFhDHqjvUmIEuG9MX0noMWv29XYmRaCOcPlKWpD07JB5MuixdiC1y9QgzffWLN7\nD9+B4wyDXnCTPB1KlQ/WUT+J7LfuAzeHCcVJw1fdiLk6NHI3k3cy1sjJiu4dz2xj\nNtxsoar08W4KHhtUCH43iBhpHol+xuQANYe1O9Bdh5iIuAW5T05Pf0MEigWskyq4\noXopWXy1Eu0A4xa2zl0yCkCe77h8iqTgMg/LTYnYXXfiTRTpFq7D56cVQlKqB7h8\nY5PiaDSmqgTYeW7NCGjo\n=cpyB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a34658f086de1ab7038007ac3d01bbed199e340d\nparent e321cba5701313e974f979069186680f1a39587c\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1782351338 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782351338 -0400\n\nrelease(deepagents-code): 0.1.23 (#4208)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Everything below this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.23](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.22...deepagents-code==0.1.23)\n(2026-06-25)\n\n### Features\n\n* Collect Tavily key during onboarding\n([#4233](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4233))\n([e321cba](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e321cba5701313e974f979069186680f1a39587c))\n* Surface `/auth` in `/trace not-configured` hint\n([#4206](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4206))\n([392e410](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/392e410e48639a56fda5e35b6f7f85a5215cce9c))\n* Add Opus 4.8 to recommended models\n([#4204](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4204))\n([8faf2b0](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8faf2b025f8429481a41a3e65544d26614e53589))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* `--reinstall` on `/install` so upgrades rebuild a clean env\n([#4196](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4196))\n([5e152ac](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5e152ac0256d64376f96b293f8844bc8acc993ec))\n* Suppress auto-update migration notice on fresh installs\n([#4224](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4224))\n([eb8ff80](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/eb8ff809a1b3130a261083c66a193e532095c6db))\n* Bake release commit into `dcode doctor`\n([#4225](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4225))\n([6dc0246](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6dc0246f5c6e9170e05191e1c82fad6975ac945c))\n* Drop redundant version from \"already up to date\" message\n([#4223](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4223))\n([5d080df](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5d080df2776d380214bf20ae31266b9628e4e5b0))\n* Note subscription plans unusable for Anthropic in `/auth`\n([#4207](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4207))\n([28cd19d](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/28cd19db08bacf981ab2c91195638e66072816fe))\n\n---\n\n_Everything above this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-25T01:35:38Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e65f4496dfafa8168fdb00f0880750d0a1bb9a4d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e65f4496dfafa8168fdb00f0880750d0a1bb9a4d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e65f4496dfafa8168fdb00f0880750d0a1bb9a4d/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e321cba5701313e974f979069186680f1a39587c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e321cba5701313e974f979069186680f1a39587c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e321cba5701313e974f979069186680f1a39587c"}]},{"sha":"e321cba5701313e974f979069186680f1a39587c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGUzMjFjYmE1NzAxMzEzZTk3NGY5NzkwNjkxODY2ODBmMWEzOTU4N2M","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-25T00:11:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T00:11:54Z"},"message":"feat(code): collect Tavily key during onboarding (#4233)\n\nOnboarding now offers to store a Tavily web-search API key, and no\nlonger shows the \"web search disabled\" toast during first-run setup.\n\n---\n\nAdds an optional Tavily web-search key step to the first-run onboarding\nflow, mirroring the LangSmith `/auth` credential path (PR #4193): the\nkey is persisted via `auth_store` and bridged onto the env var, taking\nfull effect on next launch. The step is skipped when a Tavily key is\nalready configured (env or stored). Also suppresses missing-dependency\ntoasts (e.g. \"Web search disabled\") while onboarding runs, since the\nflow now handles integrations itself — the notices stay reachable via\nthe notification center (ctrl+n).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/36c09eb1-5a3d-e633-b8c7-7475b9557a8d)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"8c4fa7e4b8987e32d1f3c6299cc952e5f2cf2816","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/8c4fa7e4b8987e32d1f3c6299cc952e5f2cf2816"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/e321cba5701313e974f979069186680f1a39587c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPHJKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvXQQAIXnC+tNoz/88p0L0rLMzIcN\n09Uz1kwLxglb5MHtCGGJgZhW54wXRWLzIWHFl9xXbZ6EG5FTItTInkVZLVpYG//k\nHQepm0Ogm90GpZehk5TD/vw8KcArmhfkHOfYEjZGVaexEWMayNDMjG+8RHEz5mj4\n+rzVHqwQDRFfwz9XYO1WZa7s0geE7rkqfCk3rpaAfhvVB2ornKgqq62K8rfeUOaP\nAC5WjgNL7tfQg5+nsxq2D0T/QoPgqtOoVX/YDFOHi42KroA9KHq90w5/xzHVvewp\n64+Gj7sPXiG4ELJhJkZptgz1uRj/VuuQ+DvQDm4b9ekArTDFnT7N3PDo/kaLiw8r\nsBzVc6A9KjEiD6lBXkLKH9QViDiBywxYg6jPe7VniLDlJEjZ75sWOWostS4LrBW7\nrTY4esiuBZI7asvIg40ikC/ed/vnQvj+IGSJ54veJUVYXnFGsAxZk1nOYq7MkWtn\nl1DzfBWuAhUPJwVC1nCYL8qzzgJutK2Ru6ftWTvuo4aGgAjaiJNR3eHAmlJIDwH7\nQyQUE73ADJtT/+iRQf5pUq/VRemw7BIQYMluyNkhZkEzA66l2hexAjjKVMU+WPyy\nDyR4hpIlcRn6CEfoE8SAusLtHMLtR1aKYgHypLzyCotIl5IHPCNqI9QUyQIL10EQ\nP3PhFiTzF7s5FY2UYMVt\n=Fknq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8c4fa7e4b8987e32d1f3c6299cc952e5f2cf2816\nparent 5e152ac0256d64376f96b293f8844bc8acc993ec\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782346314 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782346314 -0400\n\nfeat(code): collect Tavily key during onboarding (#4233)\n\nOnboarding now offers to store a Tavily web-search API key, and no\nlonger shows the \"web search disabled\" toast during first-run setup.\n\n---\n\nAdds an optional Tavily web-search key step to the first-run onboarding\nflow, mirroring the LangSmith `/auth` credential path (PR #4193): the\nkey is persisted via `auth_store` and bridged onto the env var, taking\nfull effect on next launch. The step is skipped when a Tavily key is\nalready configured (env or stored). Also suppresses missing-dependency\ntoasts (e.g. \"Web search disabled\") while onboarding runs, since the\nflow now handles integrations itself — the notices stay reachable via\nthe notification center (ctrl+n).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/36c09eb1-5a3d-e633-b8c7-7475b9557a8d)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-25T00:11:54Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e321cba5701313e974f979069186680f1a39587c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e321cba5701313e974f979069186680f1a39587c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e321cba5701313e974f979069186680f1a39587c/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5e152ac0256d64376f96b293f8844bc8acc993ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5e152ac0256d64376f96b293f8844bc8acc993ec","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5e152ac0256d64376f96b293f8844bc8acc993ec"}]},{"sha":"5e152ac0256d64376f96b293f8844bc8acc993ec","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDVlMTUyYWMwMjU2ZDY0Mzc2Zjk2YjI5M2Y4ODQ0YmM4YWNjOTkzZWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-25T00:11:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-25T00:11:36Z"},"message":"fix(code): `--reinstall` on `/install` so upgrades rebuild a clean env (#4196)\n\n`/install` now reinstalls the dcode tool cleanly, fixing server-startup\n`ImportError`s caused by half-updated environments after adding an extra\nor package.\n\n---\n\nWhen you run `/install <extra>` (e.g. `/install fireworks`) or `/install\n<pkg> --package`, dcode runs `uv tool install -U\n'deepagents-code[...]'`. The `-U` upgrades the tool **in place**, on top\nof the copy that's currently running. An in-place upgrade can leave\nstale files behind — for example an old `tools.py` (or its cached\n`.pyc`) from the previous version. You then end up with a tool\nenvironment that's a mix of old and new files.\n\nThe next time the server starts (after `/restart`), the new\n`server_graph.py` tries to import something the stale `tools.py` doesn't\nhave, and the server dies on startup.\n\nThe fix is small: pass `--reinstall` so uv rebuilds the tool environment\nfrom scratch instead of patching it in place. Every file then matches\nthe freshly resolved version, so adding a model/extra can't leave the\ninstall in a broken state. This is the same thing the manual workaround\n(`uv tool install --reinstall -U ...`) does, now baked into the\n`/install` flows. The manual-command hints we show users are updated to\nmatch.\n\nPackage installs now use the same receipt-preserving reinstall path as\nextras, so adding a custom provider package keeps existing extras,\n`--with` packages, the uv-managed Python interpreter, and prerelease\nchannel instead of rebuilding a narrower tool environment.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/e196cb0c-bde5-c559-1675-3226784d7178)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"12e80038b4eb34033fb66752df6469bf37c90e2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/12e80038b4eb34033fb66752df6469bf37c90e2a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/5e152ac0256d64376f96b293f8844bc8acc993ec","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPHI4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZ9oQABsXbh0KButmwtDGcoTcsajN\n4kzckyzWReNroDopG4c6TSM/6BO2bNy2kTd15R3919QXYWcHj8JJ4BzZYbjeyuFC\nB/wip7/U1h+kSAbpXMnZjKysqwOWeUvUjBJMDGkbDuoQl48V6/KB+9Ssc675Lo4t\nvSGT9/Tu9iNI0XVZ7XquzcIXJ05t8d+puH+TcHx/08NvUrRLbNa5jHDh/O/bS927\nP9+MuLYt+upETyNeCs8dM0WOYm+6s3pVbhZZEYA9wJFE8Tr+rtgjehelEtzBmbfj\nt79L7/EdvE3TjZ9z/f842wzQLaUlXWoWkUKFRfpkuWdkrW5n6iRx4ATxgNZPURB0\naPSeggmPA4TuyBcg//7TKnVXwIKEBTdmzWyUppYX2XjQwRv6+Oki6BzvZkRRo0tz\nXpLzyvHljuoddPOnKLvTYpOwFspcE0l+lxEIZFTySPLf6LGrr2+ej4h9H+BvAONW\n6R2YVAtFH1T9fC6LlaB7AOGo+N4JYvXqQavL59VC90XM5KQxGUSZZSlblajEjhM+\nxj9ynZfrwyCLvwtG8QceKw1pMK+U3fqGmlIpnBKYT3JCqxerD1f7VKt8oSmm9WDZ\nE2SXj56BSFQG0hH46bsXWhsXmSL67NHhRdZADnzvSBXvvPFLNmIq2c2reSXUm7F3\nnQ2JIw9kWfGFWunQFhIb\n=lbJ5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 12e80038b4eb34033fb66752df6469bf37c90e2a\nparent 26ef927d6c4ddc27c2d3d912b716a718d5c72dd5\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782346296 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782346296 -0400\n\nfix(code): `--reinstall` on `/install` so upgrades rebuild a clean env (#4196)\n\n`/install` now reinstalls the dcode tool cleanly, fixing server-startup\n`ImportError`s caused by half-updated environments after adding an extra\nor package.\n\n---\n\nWhen you run `/install <extra>` (e.g. `/install fireworks`) or `/install\n<pkg> --package`, dcode runs `uv tool install -U\n'deepagents-code[...]'`. The `-U` upgrades the tool **in place**, on top\nof the copy that's currently running. An in-place upgrade can leave\nstale files behind — for example an old `tools.py` (or its cached\n`.pyc`) from the previous version. You then end up with a tool\nenvironment that's a mix of old and new files.\n\nThe next time the server starts (after `/restart`), the new\n`server_graph.py` tries to import something the stale `tools.py` doesn't\nhave, and the server dies on startup.\n\nThe fix is small: pass `--reinstall` so uv rebuilds the tool environment\nfrom scratch instead of patching it in place. Every file then matches\nthe freshly resolved version, so adding a model/extra can't leave the\ninstall in a broken state. This is the same thing the manual workaround\n(`uv tool install --reinstall -U ...`) does, now baked into the\n`/install` flows. The manual-command hints we show users are updated to\nmatch.\n\nPackage installs now use the same receipt-preserving reinstall path as\nextras, so adding a custom provider package keeps existing extras,\n`--with` packages, the uv-managed Python interpreter, and prerelease\nchannel instead of rebuilding a narrower tool environment.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/e196cb0c-bde5-c559-1675-3226784d7178)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-25T00:11:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5e152ac0256d64376f96b293f8844bc8acc993ec","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5e152ac0256d64376f96b293f8844bc8acc993ec","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5e152ac0256d64376f96b293f8844bc8acc993ec/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"26ef927d6c4ddc27c2d3d912b716a718d5c72dd5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/26ef927d6c4ddc27c2d3d912b716a718d5c72dd5","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/26ef927d6c4ddc27c2d3d912b716a718d5c72dd5"}]},{"sha":"26ef927d6c4ddc27c2d3d912b716a718d5c72dd5","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDI2ZWY5MjdkNmM0ZGRjMjdjMmQzZDkxMmI3MTZhNzE4ZDVjNzJkZDU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nick Hollon","email":"nick.hollon@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-24T22:16:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T22:16:29Z"},"message":"feat(evals): add tau3-bench dataset and conversational tau3 agent to Harbor (#4232)\n\n## What\n\nMakes [tau3-bench](https://github.com/sierra-research/tau3-bench)\nrunnable from the Harbor workflow, with a dedicated conversational\nagent.\n\n- **`harbor.yml`** — `dataset` becomes a dropdown\n(`terminal-bench/terminal-bench-2`, `terminal-bench/terminal-bench-2-1`,\n`sierra-research/tau3-bench`) plus a free-text `dataset_override`\n(mirrors the `models` / `models_override` pattern). Adds a `tau3`\n`agent_impl` that maps to the new `tau3_deepagent` graph.\n- **`langgraph_agent.py`** — `make_tau3_graph`, an async factory that\nattaches the task environment's MCP tools (`tau3-runtime`:\n`start_conversation`, `send_message_to_user`, domain tools) and uses a\nconversational system prompt, so the agent talks to the simulated user\ninstead of running autonomously like the terminal-bench graphs.\n- **`langgraph.json`** — registers `tau3_deepagent`; adds\n`langchain-mcp-adapters`.\n\n## Why a new graph\n\ntau3 is a conversation with a simulated user via MCP tools —\nstructurally unlike terminal-bench. The existing graphs (a) use a\n\"complete autonomously, no human operator\" prompt and (b) attach no MCP\ntools, so they cannot do tau3.\n\n## Dependency: Harbor must forward env-declared MCP servers\n\n`make_tau3_graph` reads `configurable[\"mcp_servers\"]`. Harbor's\ninstalled LangGraph agent currently stores `self.mcp_servers` but never\nforwards them to the runner (every other installed agent does). That fix\nlives in a Harbor branch (`nh/langgraph-forward-mcp-servers`). Without\nit, the graph raises a clear error rather than guessing a URL.\n\n## Verification\n\n1-task tau3-telecom rollout (bare `anthropic:claude-haiku-4-5`, docker,\n`tau3_deepagent`): **reward 1.0, 0 exceptions**, 35-step conversation,\n`termination_reason=user_stop`. The agent received the full tau3 toolset\nand resolved the case.\n\n## Running tau3 in CI (follow-ups, not in this PR)\n\n- The LangGraph agent dependency install needs `UV_PRERELEASE=allow`\n(the workflow sets it only for Fireworks today).\n- `tau3-runtime` user-simulator + verifier need working `OPENAI_API_KEY`\n+ `OPENAI_BASE_URL` + `TAU2_USER_MODEL` / `TAU2_NL_ASSERTIONS_MODEL`\nwired into the Harbor job env.","tree":{"sha":"e29464db808805b247d76e7c336adb0f8c49d8e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e29464db808805b247d76e7c336adb0f8c49d8e7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/26ef927d6c4ddc27c2d3d912b716a718d5c72dd5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPFc9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAq/MQAJxlEhmK9JPH+8ramEmZjVqa\nLmCGhzeYapts3JoHZ2ginByJgIAg3TIepggVIWQL3lxWXWeRnuamDrmTJbBzlD96\n2O4u+C5WmRZUG/FzcRpvs6YgYsILJUVTBs0g8TtucgopE+3WBrpqFmtDSWDFu+A7\naoXINTzdYncqVDcX0SLk5Mv1UWJDrxX8JC3P/ZcevTJR2iISiL0dbzEDMQRcaNsL\n8dwRiku5q3si3ypc8O2N9Dp8mwZMZr4UZQd1w1GWgv/QtgP+UbW2zNY3WAELDkCU\n38WcfQlKZS65/Hd/TmVTvgvd8o62fjfBHitmv0uqYNHJzYxW5wgm9EixVMYw6y5z\nZQxka3/5vlqsU9hYHWYxcxVAtNjiXjCxab0TId4sJtcH/RSNGYu8bpJpx8ZWtODu\nh7CnAkvpAtDZ92q9Swpt3N+McO2ThUBoPuLXRZnl8AskCZlhS0aS+eJGeiW95Iwx\nXHHWq0r1mPAu/p1S3ZbgMqnY74ud8x7THKz761sNQYSPbidl6yOpDJsIiBIRdWAW\nhP4C6TA7fbMmrZB984Cymua5L8gBwRMx1x5YBqxoE4f6zcP7yao807amNcymVEOi\n0FwuIUh8NIOyXUFTay/PyBkNX9YcTmI7qh2HF5WZVN3gDOc3BAMZH8iS71WBEs+o\n9Sj2sTcLCJ2NVyvtYs27\n=Yihp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e29464db808805b247d76e7c336adb0f8c49d8e7\nparent aef33b68862830af91761f162c4ca2919ebdc290\nauthor Nick Hollon <nick.hollon@langchain.dev> 1782339389 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782339389 -0400\n\nfeat(evals): add tau3-bench dataset and conversational tau3 agent to Harbor (#4232)\n\n## What\n\nMakes [tau3-bench](https://github.com/sierra-research/tau3-bench)\nrunnable from the Harbor workflow, with a dedicated conversational\nagent.\n\n- **`harbor.yml`** — `dataset` becomes a dropdown\n(`terminal-bench/terminal-bench-2`, `terminal-bench/terminal-bench-2-1`,\n`sierra-research/tau3-bench`) plus a free-text `dataset_override`\n(mirrors the `models` / `models_override` pattern). Adds a `tau3`\n`agent_impl` that maps to the new `tau3_deepagent` graph.\n- **`langgraph_agent.py`** — `make_tau3_graph`, an async factory that\nattaches the task environment's MCP tools (`tau3-runtime`:\n`start_conversation`, `send_message_to_user`, domain tools) and uses a\nconversational system prompt, so the agent talks to the simulated user\ninstead of running autonomously like the terminal-bench graphs.\n- **`langgraph.json`** — registers `tau3_deepagent`; adds\n`langchain-mcp-adapters`.\n\n## Why a new graph\n\ntau3 is a conversation with a simulated user via MCP tools —\nstructurally unlike terminal-bench. The existing graphs (a) use a\n\"complete autonomously, no human operator\" prompt and (b) attach no MCP\ntools, so they cannot do tau3.\n\n## Dependency: Harbor must forward env-declared MCP servers\n\n`make_tau3_graph` reads `configurable[\"mcp_servers\"]`. Harbor's\ninstalled LangGraph agent currently stores `self.mcp_servers` but never\nforwards them to the runner (every other installed agent does). That fix\nlives in a Harbor branch (`nh/langgraph-forward-mcp-servers`). Without\nit, the graph raises a clear error rather than guessing a URL.\n\n## Verification\n\n1-task tau3-telecom rollout (bare `anthropic:claude-haiku-4-5`, docker,\n`tau3_deepagent`): **reward 1.0, 0 exceptions**, 35-step conversation,\n`termination_reason=user_stop`. The agent received the full tau3 toolset\nand resolved the case.\n\n## Running tau3 in CI (follow-ups, not in this PR)\n\n- The LangGraph agent dependency install needs `UV_PRERELEASE=allow`\n(the workflow sets it only for Fireworks today).\n- `tau3-runtime` user-simulator + verifier need working `OPENAI_API_KEY`\n+ `OPENAI_BASE_URL` + `TAU2_USER_MODEL` / `TAU2_NL_ASSERTIONS_MODEL`\nwired into the Harbor job env.","verified_at":"2026-06-24T22:16:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/26ef927d6c4ddc27c2d3d912b716a718d5c72dd5","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/26ef927d6c4ddc27c2d3d912b716a718d5c72dd5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/26ef927d6c4ddc27c2d3d912b716a718d5c72dd5/comments","author":{"login":"nick-hollon-lc","id":274035459,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFVzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274035459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc","html_url":"https://github.com/nick-hollon-lc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"aef33b68862830af91761f162c4ca2919ebdc290","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aef33b68862830af91761f162c4ca2919ebdc290","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/aef33b68862830af91761f162c4ca2919ebdc290"}]},{"sha":"aef33b68862830af91761f162c4ca2919ebdc290","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGFlZjMzYjY4ODYyODMwYWY5MTc2MWYxNjJjNGNhMjkxOWViZGMyOTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nick Hollon","email":"nick.hollon@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-24T22:02:25Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T22:02:25Z"},"message":"feat(evals): run continual-learning-bench from the Harbor workflow (#4231)\n\n## Summary\n\nLets you run\n[continual-learning-bench](https://github.com/pgasawa/continual-learning-bench)\n(clbench) with the Deep Agents system, selected from the existing Harbor\neval workflow via `dataset=clbench`. clbench is **not** Harbor — it's a\nseparate, in-process, multi-episode harness — so this wires it in\nalongside Harbor rather than through it, mirroring how\n`deepagents_harbor/` is the deepagents-side integration for Harbor.\n\n## What's here\n\n**Adapter — `libs/evals/deepagents_clbench/`** (canonical source;\ndeployed into a clbench checkout by `sync_to_clbench.sh`):\n- `DeepAgentsSystem` implements clbench's `ContinualLearningSystem`. The\ncontinual-learning substrate is the agent's persistent memory\n(`MemoryMiddleware` via `create_deep_agent(memory=...)`), threaded\nacross `respond()` calls.\n- Memory is written by an explicit **reflection step** at each completed\ninstance (a one-shot decision agent won't reliably call `edit_file`\nmid-decision — verified). Per-turn structured output via a separate\n`with_structured_output` call.\n- In-state `StateBackend` only — the agent gets no host\nshell/filesystem, so no path to provider secrets.\n\n**Workflow — `.github/workflows/harbor.yml`:**\n- `dataset` moved to the top as the primary selector; `clbench` added.\nOther inputs are tagged `[Harbor only]` / `[Harbor + clbench]` since\nGitHub dispatch forms can't hide fields.\n- New `clbench` job (gated `dataset == 'clbench'`; Harbor job gated to\nthe negation) sharing the model matrix. It clones clbench (pinned SHA),\n`uv sync --all-extras`, installs the local Deep Agents SDK + provider\nintegration, deploys the adapter, and runs it. Runs on the runner (no\nLangSmith sandbox — clbench has no Harbor environment layer).\n- **`clbench_schedule`** input: `quick_test` (default, cheap — per-task\n`clbench run`) or `default` (leaderboard-comparable `run-all`, each\ntask's default schedule + 5 runs; warned as multi-hour / likely past the\njob timeout). Option mapping: `include_tasks`→tasks,\n`concurrency`→per-task-parallelism, model matrix→`--system.model`.\n- **Trace-level LangSmith**: enabled only when `LANGSMITH_API_KEY` is\npresent; groups each model's agent traces under\n`deepagents-clbench-<model>`. Experiment-level logging is intentionally\n**not** wired — clbench's `mean_gain`-over-a-sequence doesn't map onto\nLangSmith experiments.\n\n## Validation\n\nEnd-to-end CI run (`dataset=clbench`, `include_tasks=exploitable_poker`,\n`quick_test`, sonnet-4-6) **succeeded**: clone → sync → adapter deploy →\n`setup --all` → `clbench run` → real score, with traces confirmed in\nLangSmith (the deepagents middleware stack — `MemoryMiddleware`,\n`SubAgentMiddleware`, `ChatAnthropic` — shows up in the project). The\nHarbor job is correctly skipped for `dataset=clbench` and unchanged\notherwise. Input hardening: schedule/task names validated against\n`^[A-Za-z0-9_]+$`, pinned clbench commit SHA, all shell vars quoted, the\nAPI key never printed.\n\n## Caveats / follow-ups\n\n- clbench is cloned + installed at job runtime (pinned SHA), not\nvendored. Two tasks (`sales_prediction`, `codebase_adaptation`) need\nDocker + heavier deps.\n- Leaderboard mode (`clbench_schedule=default`) is genuinely day-scale\nfor a Deep Agents system and won't fit a single 360-min runner — it's\nthere for completeness, but real leaderboard runs want per-task\nsplitting or out-of-CI infra.\n- The adapter's model support is limited to `init_chat_model` providers.","tree":{"sha":"4ab0426e3c857631033b0edd21dfdc337061f76a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/4ab0426e3c857631033b0edd21dfdc337061f76a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/aef33b68862830af91761f162c4ca2919ebdc290","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPFPxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeBoQAAu2LU5dN3Ls2myK89sj02ch\n5a80/vW1tWUR9611UB95cyhgVU3SgUUQjBmLLMInKYch41jVowVbiOTlw2/O+hEu\nwlrbgJG/SbRapShXQClto+iPCAIXXiHPBFTdbnSndHj7FLH61Ze0ULcFU770OYPi\nO3ZUX3AjnTW+kho4t2JR3AgqyG93Q3UtcnFAOZCulRgQs2SdC7+35dO+edx391Sl\n5+42aBvMBul5MDTCmtFOEQFFLNCUzmYlEcXOwTiw7hmHA4nkpHiHKj54zggkGY6O\nc7fEgOY2GdEyxiPZtPZcG8hihSNn4Xly+TvHtrsFO7w6CBGKDAwoRpy6sBXezBjO\n0VasU9Fg7Kg9+z4747QolEtAl9i+R/6YD0Oc4mjJUQmHJHD1QSL6553mPjyb7V0z\ny63HxwwjzoljYZTPZb+OObrPXiXSC7p2CZFRf2oUuJpPWDT3lavzx6BArxkFuh3F\n6/jJGNLAhOFb3NwdXvWWGNh2X9HUdNEGF0INB63WfiW8GtUzkpw41CV/5BwQ+Kjt\nzCVM91Q9Ts9Ve1lwIkonpopIJd5Z+S0RhKVwOeK+T97Gny88K6a0FBXWLMralpxQ\nFdm995ejbVBQ+TTXDFJnpEb57yJfikbB4XsQX1dzKc/gdgapYc1VDm+VAPfq9c+7\njBroqdf+92RUCZMEtDBe\n=+PXk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4ab0426e3c857631033b0edd21dfdc337061f76a\nparent eb8ff809a1b3130a261083c66a193e532095c6db\nauthor Nick Hollon <nick.hollon@langchain.dev> 1782338545 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782338545 -0400\n\nfeat(evals): run continual-learning-bench from the Harbor workflow (#4231)\n\n## Summary\n\nLets you run\n[continual-learning-bench](https://github.com/pgasawa/continual-learning-bench)\n(clbench) with the Deep Agents system, selected from the existing Harbor\neval workflow via `dataset=clbench`. clbench is **not** Harbor — it's a\nseparate, in-process, multi-episode harness — so this wires it in\nalongside Harbor rather than through it, mirroring how\n`deepagents_harbor/` is the deepagents-side integration for Harbor.\n\n## What's here\n\n**Adapter — `libs/evals/deepagents_clbench/`** (canonical source;\ndeployed into a clbench checkout by `sync_to_clbench.sh`):\n- `DeepAgentsSystem` implements clbench's `ContinualLearningSystem`. The\ncontinual-learning substrate is the agent's persistent memory\n(`MemoryMiddleware` via `create_deep_agent(memory=...)`), threaded\nacross `respond()` calls.\n- Memory is written by an explicit **reflection step** at each completed\ninstance (a one-shot decision agent won't reliably call `edit_file`\nmid-decision — verified). Per-turn structured output via a separate\n`with_structured_output` call.\n- In-state `StateBackend` only — the agent gets no host\nshell/filesystem, so no path to provider secrets.\n\n**Workflow — `.github/workflows/harbor.yml`:**\n- `dataset` moved to the top as the primary selector; `clbench` added.\nOther inputs are tagged `[Harbor only]` / `[Harbor + clbench]` since\nGitHub dispatch forms can't hide fields.\n- New `clbench` job (gated `dataset == 'clbench'`; Harbor job gated to\nthe negation) sharing the model matrix. It clones clbench (pinned SHA),\n`uv sync --all-extras`, installs the local Deep Agents SDK + provider\nintegration, deploys the adapter, and runs it. Runs on the runner (no\nLangSmith sandbox — clbench has no Harbor environment layer).\n- **`clbench_schedule`** input: `quick_test` (default, cheap — per-task\n`clbench run`) or `default` (leaderboard-comparable `run-all`, each\ntask's default schedule + 5 runs; warned as multi-hour / likely past the\njob timeout). Option mapping: `include_tasks`→tasks,\n`concurrency`→per-task-parallelism, model matrix→`--system.model`.\n- **Trace-level LangSmith**: enabled only when `LANGSMITH_API_KEY` is\npresent; groups each model's agent traces under\n`deepagents-clbench-<model>`. Experiment-level logging is intentionally\n**not** wired — clbench's `mean_gain`-over-a-sequence doesn't map onto\nLangSmith experiments.\n\n## Validation\n\nEnd-to-end CI run (`dataset=clbench`, `include_tasks=exploitable_poker`,\n`quick_test`, sonnet-4-6) **succeeded**: clone → sync → adapter deploy →\n`setup --all` → `clbench run` → real score, with traces confirmed in\nLangSmith (the deepagents middleware stack — `MemoryMiddleware`,\n`SubAgentMiddleware`, `ChatAnthropic` — shows up in the project). The\nHarbor job is correctly skipped for `dataset=clbench` and unchanged\notherwise. Input hardening: schedule/task names validated against\n`^[A-Za-z0-9_]+$`, pinned clbench commit SHA, all shell vars quoted, the\nAPI key never printed.\n\n## Caveats / follow-ups\n\n- clbench is cloned + installed at job runtime (pinned SHA), not\nvendored. Two tasks (`sales_prediction`, `codebase_adaptation`) need\nDocker + heavier deps.\n- Leaderboard mode (`clbench_schedule=default`) is genuinely day-scale\nfor a Deep Agents system and won't fit a single 360-min runner — it's\nthere for completeness, but real leaderboard runs want per-task\nsplitting or out-of-CI infra.\n- The adapter's model support is limited to `init_chat_model` providers.","verified_at":"2026-06-24T22:02:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aef33b68862830af91761f162c4ca2919ebdc290","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/aef33b68862830af91761f162c4ca2919ebdc290","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aef33b68862830af91761f162c4ca2919ebdc290/comments","author":{"login":"nick-hollon-lc","id":274035459,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFVzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274035459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc","html_url":"https://github.com/nick-hollon-lc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"eb8ff809a1b3130a261083c66a193e532095c6db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/eb8ff809a1b3130a261083c66a193e532095c6db","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/eb8ff809a1b3130a261083c66a193e532095c6db"}]},{"sha":"eb8ff809a1b3130a261083c66a193e532095c6db","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGViOGZmODA5YTFiMzEzMGEyNjEwODNjNjZhMTkzZTUzMjA5NWM2ZGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-24T21:27:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T21:27:56Z"},"message":"fix(code): suppress auto-update migration notice on fresh installs (#4224)\n\nFresh `dcode` installs no longer show the \"now updates automatically by\ndefault\" migration notice, which only applies to users upgrading from a\npre-auto-update version.\n\n---\n\nThe one-time \"dcode now updates automatically by default. vX will be\ninstalled on the next launch\" notice\n(`should_announce_auto_update_default`, added in #3994) is meant only\nfor users who ran dcode *before* auto-update became the opt-out default.\nIt was leaking into brand-new installs, which never experienced the old\nbehavior. On a fresh install the version cache is cold on the first\nlaunch (so `_run_startup_auto_update` returns early), then the notice\nfires on a later launch — confusing, and it delays the actual update by\nan extra launch.\n\nThe fix pre-acknowledges the notice on the first launch ever — the\ncanonical fresh-install signal in `should_show_whats_new` (when no\n`seen_version` exists yet) — so new installs never see it, while\nexisting users upgrading into the auto-update era still get it exactly\nonce.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/7d20f2db-f40d-f031-7651-118a24f284ad)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"7f783d032fcd9e2229e4a45c6f99e2bfb4e5abc0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/7f783d032fcd9e2229e4a45c6f99e2bfb4e5abc0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/eb8ff809a1b3130a261083c66a193e532095c6db","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPEvcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAM20QAGDyUkxjpW6MAh4y6dP61pUG\nmqeJaV1jx1djqek8L+4JhGMk+5SP9bJ5YD/MPDGxdPCNmMwmVTVxPfwlWLjP5Nln\noJqwWGQh7q/soD2hf9iCnl/UJ2aNEdJLJ7a+j7CJGDYd5gRY0lwHKVVG79HM4Bcm\n82AD6I3SU8pI1AWjHxpaDVsO5WzmGV9F6v4Zt3+w7MUV1t2sXtGpRmxRhGFbCcre\nw2QMODVoMRW3orYf/D+o14JSGY7H9hswsJMhLuwhYswqjakZcHrXdLo0cUKBDom8\nQe4Vl187l/RsAeNVc0QuohrNmC0kv7F2bJ35Jc3vRx+weeoXfStYx6OCSskCgkmX\n2dLtzJhEGexxEA/2IVk9VmTu3sTq0thQUqqoIyjou2mjhyETyxmff+swBOwvExNN\nDfkp0HshOPHY3Hn7GR2S9RtA+RiBw+f+yDSlsU6CTYnv2J8HzqWxzsrTLceafFo7\ncNm3AyzdzQbJu+zSY0/VflQZ1H/bAStKpriUv9cyY47Pg6v/LgTcyb3otbmrq4me\nEIGpqXRTbVAU3diUlvA0uMqThJdRnJQIwdzkxXHDc32ouK9frAJbCQyEZdNB+kyt\nKnwN2lttCsWOOuIEn45Dpkk7iqkeqqE/zvkNLn/IEVCp26xRv0+7L3Z7wXfpKOHi\n4JPyeWX5Nyqcs6wEIKxZ\n=jREZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7f783d032fcd9e2229e4a45c6f99e2bfb4e5abc0\nparent 6dc0246f5c6e9170e05191e1c82fad6975ac945c\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782336476 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782336476 -0400\n\nfix(code): suppress auto-update migration notice on fresh installs (#4224)\n\nFresh `dcode` installs no longer show the \"now updates automatically by\ndefault\" migration notice, which only applies to users upgrading from a\npre-auto-update version.\n\n---\n\nThe one-time \"dcode now updates automatically by default. vX will be\ninstalled on the next launch\" notice\n(`should_announce_auto_update_default`, added in #3994) is meant only\nfor users who ran dcode *before* auto-update became the opt-out default.\nIt was leaking into brand-new installs, which never experienced the old\nbehavior. On a fresh install the version cache is cold on the first\nlaunch (so `_run_startup_auto_update` returns early), then the notice\nfires on a later launch — confusing, and it delays the actual update by\nan extra launch.\n\nThe fix pre-acknowledges the notice on the first launch ever — the\ncanonical fresh-install signal in `should_show_whats_new` (when no\n`seen_version` exists yet) — so new installs never see it, while\nexisting users upgrading into the auto-update era still get it exactly\nonce.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/7d20f2db-f40d-f031-7651-118a24f284ad)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-24T21:27:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/eb8ff809a1b3130a261083c66a193e532095c6db","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/eb8ff809a1b3130a261083c66a193e532095c6db","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/eb8ff809a1b3130a261083c66a193e532095c6db/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6dc0246f5c6e9170e05191e1c82fad6975ac945c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6dc0246f5c6e9170e05191e1c82fad6975ac945c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6dc0246f5c6e9170e05191e1c82fad6975ac945c"}]},{"sha":"6dc0246f5c6e9170e05191e1c82fad6975ac945c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDZkYzAyNDZmNWM2ZTkxNzBlMDUxOTFlMWM4MmZhZDY5NzVhYzk0NWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-24T21:11:21Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T21:11:21Z"},"message":"fix(code): bake release commit into `dcode doctor` (#4225)\n\n`dcode doctor` now reports the exact commit a released wheel was built\nfrom (once the release workflow sets `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_BUILD_COMMIT`).\n\n---\n\nReleased wheels and sdists ship no `.git` metadata, so `dcode doctor`\ncould only resolve a `Commit hash` for *editable* installs that probe a\nlive working tree — every normal pip/pipx/wheel install correctly showed\n`unknown`. This stamps the release commit into the package at build time\nso installed wheels report the real commit.\n\nA hatchling build hook (`hatch_build.py`) writes a generated\n`_build_info.py` with `BUILD_COMMIT` **only** when\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_BUILD_COMMIT` is set (CI release builds); it validates\nthe value is a hex SHA, registers the file as a build artifact, and\nremoves it afterward so the working tree stays clean. `doctor` now\nprefers that stamped commit and falls back to the existing live `git\nrev-parse` probe, so editable/dev installs keep reporting the live\nworking-tree commit (which reflects local changes).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/f53414ff-5e6b-da73-65d1-9091c5d31a94)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"470d90f6020f49b8d05afae8217049169821e4d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/470d90f6020f49b8d05afae8217049169821e4d4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/6dc0246f5c6e9170e05191e1c82fad6975ac945c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPEf5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADREQAHhoLg48Uj3rJ5u64GhOH8WO\nhuSomaFlS3mgrErhiv8jIFWYTPrdPKRcLK8f8hz4azNzPrY/RBvI+c2nhXaTZewV\ndEgQf7Bjs8Y11aJCRrD+3mlRg8SodTHFUQxvcMTkkL5JJDW2Pj3ZcfkmdWALQn4b\nTbNQ0NgG1Q8nYQpZFTcHad2PGedpWqGXGpk1KpelIMO9H4JqIgpqrDJtcUhjV8lA\nyijrEz/rmjCDANXC4yRMVJm4mIB7BkY6S4aInxRs54I5k2Mz325K5gsdWxrbeVs9\nPqDomr1bH1QNNht3IuH3tvXNtZBbYxSec1Sur+KO82Ggr6ySDzw8aPLRwyUvZJw0\n3qwRG5oaiCKj1oJ1FETadg067EjojIgkM4/5xPfEmIOSFUc+W/ob8OFIf52ClJOp\nLZ/dNu1NOvgdTTISmRftHx+v/4qcCJ0SgKGh9txxIizmMA0UcZFo7g9iVqLX1WJv\nZB9an7m7Ym2ue2ckTwu/DH7AGwGEq2WPPacYq/iYzgvQLeuAWnYFlAjq51ClmZkO\nqE+OYVGFQN5JANGXEnPLm7tfA++8uuE7FZtEWr5vVPTUt0ShYLbYm+vgXHkIOt+4\npq6HW7BE14aj5/V9pSazg3BuAJsTX6KesOOPMGzrBu+VU7HDiE7oCnLACC7LU9Ej\ndD5LvX9d+IlEZ/HsOroN\n=qKF7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 470d90f6020f49b8d05afae8217049169821e4d4\nparent ad4c16a517fb69e5fc952e2a48c54a0d5515fc61\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782335481 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782335481 -0400\n\nfix(code): bake release commit into `dcode doctor` (#4225)\n\n`dcode doctor` now reports the exact commit a released wheel was built\nfrom (once the release workflow sets `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_BUILD_COMMIT`).\n\n---\n\nReleased wheels and sdists ship no `.git` metadata, so `dcode doctor`\ncould only resolve a `Commit hash` for *editable* installs that probe a\nlive working tree — every normal pip/pipx/wheel install correctly showed\n`unknown`. This stamps the release commit into the package at build time\nso installed wheels report the real commit.\n\nA hatchling build hook (`hatch_build.py`) writes a generated\n`_build_info.py` with `BUILD_COMMIT` **only** when\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_BUILD_COMMIT` is set (CI release builds); it validates\nthe value is a hex SHA, registers the file as a build artifact, and\nremoves it afterward so the working tree stays clean. `doctor` now\nprefers that stamped commit and falls back to the existing live `git\nrev-parse` probe, so editable/dev installs keep reporting the live\nworking-tree commit (which reflects local changes).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/f53414ff-5e6b-da73-65d1-9091c5d31a94)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-24T21:11:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6dc0246f5c6e9170e05191e1c82fad6975ac945c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6dc0246f5c6e9170e05191e1c82fad6975ac945c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6dc0246f5c6e9170e05191e1c82fad6975ac945c/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-