://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0f3cb27cb38679bc6291bb03a9680829a40897ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0f3cb27cb38679bc6291bb03a9680829a40897ab","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0f3cb27cb38679bc6291bb03a9680829a40897ab"}]},{"sha":"0f3cb27cb38679bc6291bb03a9680829a40897ab","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDBmM2NiMjdjYjM4Njc5YmM2MjkxYmIwM2E5NjgwODI5YTQwODk3YWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"github-actions[bot]","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-24T06:34:32Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T06:34:32Z"},"message":"release(deepagents-code): 0.1.22 (#4191)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Everything below this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.22](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.21...deepagents-code==0.1.22)\n(2026-06-24)\n\n### Features\n\n* Add LangSmith tracing config to `/auth`\n([#4193](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4193))\n([8e62957](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8e6295791093c2ddfec7e6ac57f0df7f12048447))\n* Auto-retry credentials-blocked startup after `/auth`\n([#4176](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4176))\n([d10ba3d](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d10ba3dc162e47cc71df56b8e3d0000b6e0ed847))\n* Improve onboarding Installed Integrations screen\n([#4195](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4195))\n([0827bf1](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0827bf1b635b825121740ac8946dd6d98c815c7d))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* Exclude managed bin dir from agent picker\n([#4190](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4190))\n([d869d1e](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d869d1e1fa8558510fb48e71f78fb74c69ca4840))\n* Warn on `/trace` when thread has no messages\n([#4162](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4162))\n([c338fc9](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c338fc914fcd383beb4b97c13f53dfb2684f8c90))\n* Hide \"Recent\" section during onboarding model selection\n([#4198](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4198))\n([af882e4](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/af882e4f6c859878e350d8a37bb75b7bc01bb453))\n* Keep auth modal interactive after install-on-select\n([#4187](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4187))\n([afbc56a](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/afbc56a1d9dbe8a89015f4c2f90bb87547d5c1d4))\n* Generic \"missing credentials\" in model switcher\n([#4182](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4182))\n([456ce5c](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/456ce5c2f5487a754d1fea7046e32c03b7e27a17))\n* Hide chat input action buttons in same frame as empty draft\n([#4178](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4178))\n([f94d417](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f94d417d5ad9928db967777fe1d7bc2c37684fb9))\n* Preserve uv tool context when installing extras\n([#4201](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4201))\n([fcc616c](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/fcc616cf9bc2bbc7b2dc2574ae8649e2f270dc53))\n* Unpin uv self-updates and warn when a stale dcode shadows PATH\n([#4185](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4185))\n([8ca0a18](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8ca0a185a15f800267cc057178a348fb5063df1e))\n\n---\n\n_Everything above this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"ef35e25556ce47c92ee03533ccd2f736006ef685","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/ef35e25556ce47c92ee03533ccd2f736006ef685"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/0f3cb27cb38679bc6291bb03a9680829a40897ab","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqO3p4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyEcQAEZR0PB3Eq0s2bSxe/+T5qOe\nKsGfWTSlggEZQH2dILEb3J6eVM9xL9WQCQTkCqcdEohgqhsJ/wXBthYA5NmV7kZR\n1s7ctUuC+KgywL9h4mXN0vWfPeWuUZJklUvBuDxdYHdDy37k5B8cqJNWoXb1accW\nz0bxXxyAsE32kYnUrPi0aqaAbozE+Ru35i4PqKdMxDKlVpbbyu1yA6TLi9RBywaV\nL0Tzfgu2SW8sD6FBmR/TBiOkSLdOc8erG0zmwhVTvjPR3yh2v9V3JY+Ot0/6Ngfw\nXLaCZIwis7Dx47XIuX2KKiXA9uqryf8xjQtuBEz97xI0tBdav3Rw3/9nBnrNzQvp\n2Z66ZS+Gkui+P1byA2Ks54Mr5Pen1Iz4n/ss9nnlINwKNf4hxKsv0O+5kx+L3pi/\na3dSn4wuiChhTnbjEBUDHkg2XfBrASm25OIN8ghOYHzw5W7+R5nxyQ6T/lkqfQ1R\n0NYCRpjNW36+oU1w8uWR8AEKZDmg+xQAjLCWtxJJPWL0bk8Ntb+RcfXn6D46Wh1l\nF80J2HrdvSDg5zl/gk/vE55jPaQFVNaTxeLYNsQAd+lcWlSUTuFUH0YAEDcKsL88\nck8Um8BUXEoxiUv8ekt93KtM0jdfxr4UDgrsK4o+7AB8O3Xrbc2T2JKW42I23hJU\nQswtStSffW2WV+SdlrT/\n=jxKd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ef35e25556ce47c92ee03533ccd2f736006ef685\nparent fcc616cf9bc2bbc7b2dc2574ae8649e2f270dc53\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1782282872 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782282872 -0400\n\nrelease(deepagents-code): 0.1.22 (#4191)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Everything below this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.22](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.21...deepagents-code==0.1.22)\n(2026-06-24)\n\n### Features\n\n* Add LangSmith tracing config to `/auth`\n([#4193](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4193))\n([8e62957](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8e6295791093c2ddfec7e6ac57f0df7f12048447))\n* Auto-retry credentials-blocked startup after `/auth`\n([#4176](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4176))\n([d10ba3d](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d10ba3dc162e47cc71df56b8e3d0000b6e0ed847))\n* Improve onboarding Installed Integrations screen\n([#4195](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4195))\n([0827bf1](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0827bf1b635b825121740ac8946dd6d98c815c7d))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* Exclude managed bin dir from agent picker\n([#4190](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4190))\n([d869d1e](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d869d1e1fa8558510fb48e71f78fb74c69ca4840))\n* Warn on `/trace` when thread has no messages\n([#4162](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4162))\n([c338fc9](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c338fc914fcd383beb4b97c13f53dfb2684f8c90))\n* Hide \"Recent\" section during onboarding model selection\n([#4198](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4198))\n([af882e4](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/af882e4f6c859878e350d8a37bb75b7bc01bb453))\n* Keep auth modal interactive after install-on-select\n([#4187](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4187))\n([afbc56a](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/afbc56a1d9dbe8a89015f4c2f90bb87547d5c1d4))\n* Generic \"missing credentials\" in model switcher\n([#4182](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4182))\n([456ce5c](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/456ce5c2f5487a754d1fea7046e32c03b7e27a17))\n* Hide chat input action buttons in same frame as empty draft\n([#4178](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4178))\n([f94d417](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f94d417d5ad9928db967777fe1d7bc2c37684fb9))\n* Preserve uv tool context when installing extras\n([#4201](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4201))\n([fcc616c](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/fcc616cf9bc2bbc7b2dc2574ae8649e2f270dc53))\n* Unpin uv self-updates and warn when a stale dcode shadows PATH\n([#4185](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4185))\n([8ca0a18](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8ca0a185a15f800267cc057178a348fb5063df1e))\n\n---\n\n_Everything above this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-24T06:34:32Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0f3cb27cb38679bc6291bb03a9680829a40897ab","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0f3cb27cb38679bc6291bb03a9680829a40897ab","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0f3cb27cb38679bc6291bb03a9680829a40897ab/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fcc616cf9bc2bbc7b2dc2574ae8649e2f270dc53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/fcc616cf9bc2bbc7b2dc2574ae8649e2f270dc53","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/fcc616cf9bc2bbc7b2dc2574ae8649e2f270dc53"}]},{"sha":"fcc616cf9bc2bbc7b2dc2574ae8649e2f270dc53","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGZjYzYxNmNmOWJjMmJiYzdiMmRjMjU3NGFlODY0OWUyZjI3MGRjNTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-24T06:27:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T06:27:39Z"},"message":"fix(code): preserve uv tool context when installing extras (#4201)\n\nSplit extra installation into a display path and an execution path so\nuser-facing recovery instructions match the public install script, while\nthe in-app uv flow still preserves the existing tool environment. This\navoids dropping the recorded Python interpreter or `--with` packages\nwhen `/install <extra>` rewrites the uv-managed `dcode` tool.\n\n## Changes\n- Add `INSTALL_SCRIPT_COMMAND` and make `install_extras_command` /\n`install_extra_command` display the promoted `curl -LsSf\nhttps://langch.in/dcode | DEEPAGENTS_CODE_EXTRAS=... bash` reinstall\nflow instead of raw `uv tool install`\n- Add `_install_extra_uv_tool_command` for the actual uv-managed\nexecution path, merging the requested extra with installed extras\nthrough `_uv_tool_install_command`\n- Extend `_uv_tool_install_command` with `extras_to_add`, preserving the\nuv receipt’s `--python` interpreter and existing `--with` packages while\nadding the new extra\n- Update `perform_install_extra` to use `_install_extra_uv_tool_command`\nfor uv-managed installs and report `ToolRequirementIntrospectionError`\nwhen the receipt cannot be safely preserved\n- Keep unsupported install guidance in `perform_install_extra`\nreceipt-free, so Homebrew/unknown installs get the install-script\nrecovery command without failing on uv receipt parsing\n- Update `DeepAgentsApp._install_extra` and the `--install` CLI fallback\npath to surface the install-script command in user-facing manual\nrecovery messages","tree":{"sha":"ed9f9281c3b62629ffaf525e8b53aed4491a7371","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/ed9f9281c3b62629ffaf525e8b53aed4491a7371"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/fcc616cf9bc2bbc7b2dc2574ae8649e2f270dc53","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqO3jbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvH0QADLU3uPv2SAiPkyhWhbn7qqw\nbwZ4bg1/O7S910TFkqDdtIgFbWt6touMsLwi7Cpwk/p+Li+sUUcJJ+JAHjLScIBb\n6R7g9szEiai6AXx11GKgbBQZ/Nu2qN0LqDdtGyQLctNQ5Tk3mhcQ9QIAFSvAF/Al\nYL6UU85EktDGpTgM2lxLyVK4Yz2VMwkfPlWrQlr69K7K/kW64/CAf5r46Jv9qSh5\nskRQGp5Bsgg8rrF1LOViAyN2+XosFuxG0wzSfyV6fTj/u2g2C4KBPiPuFUPeyW8c\neTL8BQHj7d1aL+3y7uNBmTWkUnx1TZkhi8vyD5+JagHRAf+tfS5dVovXiMBLO98A\nE5lS27aIemBxt5z09d+eui0TxlByxgAUt1ZjvQy1T4VKofpbu0RP7kiA5Ya+M+Zh\nxiHWcgmZMUYq/Gdqs/oFgcTMINtgXwHTD7jac7BY8OoE9cGEePuL0s7zhbmm9Edl\n5HP3ozIEVBoySgbyAI06OIfIHq1kD8YnHzsnfWHsSHZ/vNZDU+yatWj5PXW6Whs0\nzZWsAewi9bBk4guevQpFPWkupKq3qIEb6Qj5jIvC+gcB3rwuDX/PXIzIRCpHnol8\nHaglncnoz2B7pNrMt5njXKyvaLV/rGeHeM5ZaczLw9pGRsoczJAZxoyb4nOHrGHM\nrkSbr2/bOhRRUK1IOpBl\n=3oKI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ed9f9281c3b62629ffaf525e8b53aed4491a7371\nparent 8e6295791093c2ddfec7e6ac57f0df7f12048447\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782282459 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782282459 -0400\n\nfix(code): preserve uv tool context when installing extras (#4201)\n\nSplit extra installation into a display path and an execution path so\nuser-facing recovery instructions match the public install script, while\nthe in-app uv flow still preserves the existing tool environment. This\navoids dropping the recorded Python interpreter or `--with` packages\nwhen `/install <extra>` rewrites the uv-managed `dcode` tool.\n\n## Changes\n- Add `INSTALL_SCRIPT_COMMAND` and make `install_extras_command` /\n`install_extra_command` display the promoted `curl -LsSf\nhttps://langch.in/dcode | DEEPAGENTS_CODE_EXTRAS=... bash` reinstall\nflow instead of raw `uv tool install`\n- Add `_install_extra_uv_tool_command` for the actual uv-managed\nexecution path, merging the requested extra with installed extras\nthrough `_uv_tool_install_command`\n- Extend `_uv_tool_install_command` with `extras_to_add`, preserving the\nuv receipt’s `--python` interpreter and existing `--with` packages while\nadding the new extra\n- Update `perform_install_extra` to use `_install_extra_uv_tool_command`\nfor uv-managed installs and report `ToolRequirementIntrospectionError`\nwhen the receipt cannot be safely preserved\n- Keep unsupported install guidance in `perform_install_extra`\nreceipt-free, so Homebrew/unknown installs get the install-script\nrecovery command without failing on uv receipt parsing\n- Update `DeepAgentsApp._install_extra` and the `--install` CLI fallback\npath to surface the install-script command in user-facing manual\nrecovery messages","verified_at":"2026-06-24T06:27:39Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/fcc616cf9bc2bbc7b2dc2574ae8649e2f270dc53","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/fcc616cf9bc2bbc7b2dc2574ae8649e2f270dc53","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/fcc616cf9bc2bbc7b2dc2574ae8649e2f270dc53/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8e6295791093c2ddfec7e6ac57f0df7f12048447","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8e6295791093c2ddfec7e6ac57f0df7f12048447","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8e6295791093c2ddfec7e6ac57f0df7f12048447"}]},{"sha":"8e6295791093c2ddfec7e6ac57f0df7f12048447","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDhlNjI5NTc5MTA5M2MyZGRmZWM3ZTZhYzU3ZjBkZjdmMTIwNDg0NDc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-24T06:24:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T06:24:50Z"},"message":"feat(code): add LangSmith tracing config to `/auth` (#4193)\n\nLangSmith tracing can now be configured directly from `/auth` (and\n`dcode auth set langsmith`), including enabling tracing, a temporary\nopt-out via `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGSMITH_TRACING=false`, and a custom\nproject name.\n\n---\n\nWires LangSmith tracing into the `/auth` surface as a configurable\nservice, mirroring how Tavily is already handled. Storing a LangSmith\nkey via `/auth` persists it to the credential store, bridges it onto\n`LANGSMITH_API_KEY`, and opts the user into tracing — so configuring\ntracing no longer requires exporting environment variables before\nlaunch.\n\nKey behaviors:\n- A stored key turns tracing on by default. An explicit falsy tracing\nflag (most simply `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGSMITH_TRACING=false`) is honored\nas a non-destructive, session-scoped opt-out — pause tracing without\ndeleting the key. The TUI prompt surfaces this path.\n- An optional project name (advanced field in the TUI prompt,\n`--project` on `dcode auth set`) routes traces to a custom\n`LANGSMITH_PROJECT`; the default stays `deepagents-code`.\n- Services are now surfaced in `dcode auth list`/`status` (this also\nfixes a pre-existing gap where Tavily was invisible to the CLI).\n- Bootstrap reordered so a `/auth`-stored key is applied before\norphaned-tracing detection, keeping tracing alive instead of being\ndisabled.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/2ba1485c-7c70-59b6-82bf-18302c214c6c)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"3e3ca7fbc1f85c3b78b4c64bb63c1f6dec723a56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/3e3ca7fbc1f85c3b78b4c64bb63c1f6dec723a56"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/8e6295791093c2ddfec7e6ac57f0df7f12048447","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqO3gyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACzYQAJ9AsYFlUqVvq22gJn5Sl6+9\nbC2Si9Hc/RUTazzLEQRghvZz3RHVdsbegVZ51q2YgJDjAYLNMY2KZuAi757kYlly\nku5JYkhDLtO6ydfjJo4rAAkedtQXRWqP/DTgFhg3LXDdbJe95cG4Csn2wuQca4m1\nnzeo0x8AALGrcL0WGtBmZKjEXzFFB0L038iqiwqe7iPKX0guI7c9Kj5ld37ez45I\n5WvpcMrHvF9JbpcA8W7Q2+uCa1zW0n1mBS27E8IO0r8PbNWamWILyn0IDalJRko5\n5D0FDO5+yrbR0/kZVJODkaY0Rlb5aGgiXeySTYBBZCay6himkpA6KCgGSt4y+uRm\nUJIth6QUPsfZzh2aMN6TINR1Ik9BmKBiQNAZxAnLirZzwLU+Xn/oSO38WdAapvC0\naYOqh8l9QB3bQn3SE1c+84rXek4IM9fYl8a9oWAwD62+buRIHhaO0xBRYecxdTxp\nnlTHgMQWoMKPK49pP1IBbAnjc4qx2qw+ecyL3Qm6pmd+OKZ3AkPC1CqDiL4bdSPk\nQhUf8ATyK9/fjz4Biv/1T/lBVGWk9xjDKr9SiXZDztR/mRHDLdH2Gd6yP5EUO6kK\n13ZqRSVf+GGFMAwTGW19BMrg2sJ9NbSUi6wj6gKKM32K5LxLnpGK/ddoHtZ4lJjB\nkveA+ExCQoxvMlvgCIRp\n=kakT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3e3ca7fbc1f85c3b78b4c64bb63c1f6dec723a56\nparent 23f52054e1bd9fd3cdf7cdbab466255031545653\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782282290 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782282290 -0400\n\nfeat(code): add LangSmith tracing config to `/auth` (#4193)\n\nLangSmith tracing can now be configured directly from `/auth` (and\n`dcode auth set langsmith`), including enabling tracing, a temporary\nopt-out via `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGSMITH_TRACING=false`, and a custom\nproject name.\n\n---\n\nWires LangSmith tracing into the `/auth` surface as a configurable\nservice, mirroring how Tavily is already handled. Storing a LangSmith\nkey via `/auth` persists it to the credential store, bridges it onto\n`LANGSMITH_API_KEY`, and opts the user into tracing — so configuring\ntracing no longer requires exporting environment variables before\nlaunch.\n\nKey behaviors:\n- A stored key turns tracing on by default. An explicit falsy tracing\nflag (most simply `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGSMITH_TRACING=false`) is honored\nas a non-destructive, session-scoped opt-out — pause tracing without\ndeleting the key. The TUI prompt surfaces this path.\n- An optional project name (advanced field in the TUI prompt,\n`--project` on `dcode auth set`) routes traces to a custom\n`LANGSMITH_PROJECT`; the default stays `deepagents-code`.\n- Services are now surfaced in `dcode auth list`/`status` (this also\nfixes a pre-existing gap where Tavily was invisible to the CLI).\n- Bootstrap reordered so a `/auth`-stored key is applied before\norphaned-tracing detection, keeping tracing alive instead of being\ndisabled.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/2ba1485c-7c70-59b6-82bf-18302c214c6c)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-24T06:24:50Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8e6295791093c2ddfec7e6ac57f0df7f12048447","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8e6295791093c2ddfec7e6ac57f0df7f12048447","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8e6295791093c2ddfec7e6ac57f0df7f12048447/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"23f52054e1bd9fd3cdf7cdbab466255031545653","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/23f52054e1bd9fd3cdf7cdbab466255031545653","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/23f52054e1bd9fd3cdf7cdbab466255031545653"}]},{"sha":"23f52054e1bd9fd3cdf7cdbab466255031545653","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDIzZjUyMDU0ZTFiZDlmZDNjZGY3Y2RiYWI0NjYyNTUwMzE1NDU2NTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-24T06:03:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T06:03:03Z"},"message":"style(code): sort credentialed providers to top of `/auth` modal (#4197)\n\nThe `/auth` modal now floats providers and services that already have\ncredentials configured to the top of the list.\n\n---\n\nThe `/auth` manager listed every entry strictly alphabetically, which\nburied the credentials a user is actively using beneath providers\nthey've never configured. This sorts entries whose credential resolves\nto `CONFIGURED` (a stored key or a resolvable env var) ahead of the\nrest, so the keys in active use are easiest to find.\n\nModel providers and non-model services (e.g. Tavily web search) are\nordered together in a single pass rather than as separate blocks, so a\nconfigured service can float above an unconfigured model provider.\nAlphabetical order is preserved within the configured block and within\nthe unconfigured block.\n\nUninstalled install-on-select rows intentionally stay at the bottom,\nsince selecting one installs a package rather than managing a key.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/50a27fa0-1aa1-208a-647b-aa9003321d93)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"aaf102ee79fb8e958e325a21357c6c8d668d7d8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/aaf102ee79fb8e958e325a21357c6c8d668d7d8f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/23f52054e1bd9fd3cdf7cdbab466255031545653","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqO3MXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzD0QAH6msoOjMirtUrWs/K069I6u\nAmoBM0AGY+o+7C01ORxtV9e/IYeiuQH9F4taisT4GH7jgD43srMJAQcVzk7mXK92\nKShJnBOt9XmJoCLm0EGFMIYEvCY1gN/R5Tx07LpQZXt/gqW+cdmlowoiBB3YEFJy\n1HWm1XhnjpVTW2HYYKko90nZlfmIxzuxIbcL66+xaqQqlKGN+XXtB8rqKIu8mQzr\n+2MJNkJHMTvrlaOQuW1ek46cmUzLSeCkDjWO8e2KtSwCeG7kvBCh2dPAfRA38Oq+\nLk3MBRzoWTj51jzhvVPVfR9lYYjTu/XNavaN5rCerWJ1TgU8lD6QHtbGgGbL5djh\nJ8JcSZ4rV/3ihQ2ICH5//PjCndAmINietUqekb1hhqdwr+VcGg1bGWP26b6Pawzz\nRthgZZOkmFTX5khgzO/2OGSY/utz2Xlofkb6NWf0hEa6IdYfA0VLDf4YyPLeVclR\n7nHo3SUDECDzKiKlfSDHDPY66QngJ2ZWBEvLP0Xp+seNKn91q9A3EGN+NQgnHQ5R\nTWMvFwcc1WZT5Osc1Kt5DF2Jopak8OsKo3fV68Tn7cO0Jev/OmnEsEhbvcMHcE4C\n3+pr1AZExCLyIXMJr4r7198TSdA8c7qZpcFGKQBvAGFASqDs6O4e8+bi+nUU6rJZ\njGDzpTdcv6jaSwTR3r0W\n=6Qw7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree aaf102ee79fb8e958e325a21357c6c8d668d7d8f\nparent af882e4f6c859878e350d8a37bb75b7bc01bb453\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782280983 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782280983 -0400\n\nstyle(code): sort credentialed providers to top of `/auth` modal (#4197)\n\nThe `/auth` modal now floats providers and services that already have\ncredentials configured to the top of the list.\n\n---\n\nThe `/auth` manager listed every entry strictly alphabetically, which\nburied the credentials a user is actively using beneath providers\nthey've never configured. This sorts entries whose credential resolves\nto `CONFIGURED` (a stored key or a resolvable env var) ahead of the\nrest, so the keys in active use are easiest to find.\n\nModel providers and non-model services (e.g. Tavily web search) are\nordered together in a single pass rather than as separate blocks, so a\nconfigured service can float above an unconfigured model provider.\nAlphabetical order is preserved within the configured block and within\nthe unconfigured block.\n\nUninstalled install-on-select rows intentionally stay at the bottom,\nsince selecting one installs a package rather than managing a key.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/50a27fa0-1aa1-208a-647b-aa9003321d93)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-24T06:03:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/23f52054e1bd9fd3cdf7cdbab466255031545653","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/23f52054e1bd9fd3cdf7cdbab466255031545653","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/23f52054e1bd9fd3cdf7cdbab466255031545653/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"af882e4f6c859878e350d8a37bb75b7bc01bb453","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/af882e4f6c859878e350d8a37bb75b7bc01bb453","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/af882e4f6c859878e350d8a37bb75b7bc01bb453"}]},{"sha":"af882e4f6c859878e350d8a37bb75b7bc01bb453","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGFmODgyZTRmNmM4NTk4NzhlMzUwZDhhMzdiYjc1YjdiYzAxYmI0NTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-24T05:38:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T05:38:22Z"},"message":"fix(code): hide \"Recent\" section during onboarding model selection (#4198)\n\nOnboarding model selection no longer shows a spurious \"Recent\" model on\na fresh install.\n\n---\n\nOn a fresh install, the onboarding \"Choose a Recommended Model\" screen\nshowed a \"Recent\" entry for a model the user never picked. The startup\ndefault-fallback resolution auto-detects a provider and persists it to\nthe recent-models MRU (`save_recent_model` / `touch_recent_model`),\nwhich the curated onboarding picker then surfaced as \"Recent\". The fix\nskips loading recents in curated (onboarding) mode, so the section only\nappears once a user has genuinely switched models.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/1188b11f-a113-c648-0ba7-b0a91b2f5c0c)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"d007af8245479bfb69de82e0fadbaf55bd55bd25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/d007af8245479bfb69de82e0fadbaf55bd55bd25"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/af882e4f6c859878e350d8a37bb75b7bc01bb453","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqO21OCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFooQAEDtJSJSHIWEeaZgPFxCRD1u\nN+H9kZvlTjMed4A8W4wv7wcX5wiAs841PajCVGL+CRmcyaTfDsoDgc3cQhNLDmDx\nXc2YFu2pVLOFZ00c3SIn9RyS84P8/4rlx/PttDmdvk15nGGFePVzRxdK2XJPU409\ne4S/Fp3/WXmHejrvy8r24gmey6k6ZaKTFB2R2e3eLvUMyMiArsh6Nu1cfaa86zwb\npwuAVJxLtJySOSY00c7PNqb0YxayGT7oox7dtVjODM56RkcXi+3iJKWAd+Kump+M\nd+BaWogQw8aeNNGe9tej6IBI9pV48odULKq4yH24BGh8J7oJnpw1c0PuJUS+kEmr\nHfhRhozDHhRkQbzx7xFv6d3IlUYnALk9+8JfMMVooprDogGkk1QC91BjQrKkd48H\nxjGQ84C9VL7KSFkZue+KeRYqzP25wjxL7IcqjzACX3O1Yzg1zIsR8/hZ3D/CRlO2\ngnh4aLRtszLyymgc6WIzr7qabgH2FhnE2vea37lcvikK45tU2gpd5vt/wjYygtZD\n7yTteu6Z6fnONOpSQgwp5YnvdxJ1lUKs8x6yS0I8Co9hqGvwnW0T7v+lNB99NhZp\nLj7BvlZZ9gbULU/JZ8NH6drXlALX5JxD7Gmm6P40huI8epGq0fEyH5TVMuvcglZu\nyDw+4AJMMWl6vV77+qpp\n=lkCf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d007af8245479bfb69de82e0fadbaf55bd55bd25\nparent 0827bf1b635b825121740ac8946dd6d98c815c7d\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782279502 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782279502 -0400\n\nfix(code): hide \"Recent\" section during onboarding model selection (#4198)\n\nOnboarding model selection no longer shows a spurious \"Recent\" model on\na fresh install.\n\n---\n\nOn a fresh install, the onboarding \"Choose a Recommended Model\" screen\nshowed a \"Recent\" entry for a model the user never picked. The startup\ndefault-fallback resolution auto-detects a provider and persists it to\nthe recent-models MRU (`save_recent_model` / `touch_recent_model`),\nwhich the curated onboarding picker then surfaced as \"Recent\". The fix\nskips loading recents in curated (onboarding) mode, so the section only\nappears once a user has genuinely switched models.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/1188b11f-a113-c648-0ba7-b0a91b2f5c0c)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-24T05:38:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/af882e4f6c859878e350d8a37bb75b7bc01bb453","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/af882e4f6c859878e350d8a37bb75b7bc01bb453","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/af882e4f6c859878e350d8a37bb75b7bc01bb453/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0827bf1b635b825121740ac8946dd6d98c815c7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0827bf1b635b825121740ac8946dd6d98c815c7d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0827bf1b635b825121740ac8946dd6d98c815c7d"}]},{"sha":"0827bf1b635b825121740ac8946dd6d98c815c7d","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDA4MjdiZjFiNjM1YjgyNTEyMTc0MGFjODk0NmRkNmQ5OGM4MTVjN2Q","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-24T04:59:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T04:59:49Z"},"message":"feat(code): improve onboarding Installed Integrations screen (#4195)\n\nOnboarding's Installed Integrations screen now lists all available\nintegrations (no \"+N more\" truncation) with clearer per-category rows\nand guidance on how to add them.\n\n---\n\nThe first-run \"Installed Integrations\" onboarding screen truncated the\n\"Available to add\" list at 8 names with \"+N more\" - which hid most\naddable extras since a fresh install has almost everything in that\nsection. This reworks the screen to list every extra as per-category\nrows with status glyphs and counts (no truncation), adds the\npreviously-dropped Other/standalone category (`quickjs`), makes the body\nscrollable, and adds copy pointing at the existing install paths (the\nmodel selector that follows installs your provider; `/install <name>`\nfor anything else) so the info is actionable without blocking\nonboarding.\n\nThe onboarding/default recommended selector intentionally favors the\ncurated recommendation set over the full installed-model list. This\nkeeps first-run setup narrow and predictable, even when users already\nhave custom or non-recommended providers installed.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/f342522b-99b6-17d0-756d-87cf23066279)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a0f21fe13e60fd1389715f3c3195d2261827ac5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a0f21fe13e60fd1389715f3c3195d2261827ac5b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/0827bf1b635b825121740ac8946dd6d98c815c7d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqO2RFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeegQACKHu78mpSnAKPvUvrX+zWPq\nn0vfGbu7+r/9Opw+noGBigMGgQ8bcBWwjPtlHTgyKx5uaJj/P/u+lXVvVRwAX++Z\nZ8iPzAFqafxazFBlxzFoq701u/S1966ZcD8Z1JqdwkbVvy7xMuV8YxAIoxKzh6UK\nqWYMnQBrCiGxPoKVyURvg9+LnguAwfb6ApdPKC2HlM1uuoQ9qTOXOePXjm73Td63\n77jwJuza0e1JNW9U1y9LRRIMbxL6i/tZQXr9TlykoMMp6wgiYVXmDVDXc9fcy3jV\nf8AdrzLueAYCJ0Kv7VMgpH/WpMMSGDFKRyxf3lDDYgpoWskWwyMgvZdexSG7+Hmu\neMrFYWH9O/Ga5pu4lDwxiRYV/l4PZ19nfZFJ9sVgxQJks5LOiXZwyZE2TKHlHBVp\nlagJOxlyaWjAsUYuhMY24tsCq0l84ELFPre6gFSxMdH1GCkBnZ4zABYXrsOcLpgK\nwPk8AfFslK/Chl4XXJpYSogoYckGS/hiH4eX+uJFtqsuyrb+pgCiAko9pLfEw0nd\nQAa7qWoszHJ27wU2ftdZP3dp7jMuf2xorau5T0Pu4GRC1hGW3BstVNAdOT+jGrlv\nK8AN5iWpfSTe9qfzFtSgh4MATRHaNweZd6Fz34Mn6u+L0gDOaSyp5f0x0e6L2m7f\nkWNZq5+Tq7E5LWaDMUAd\n=eZlg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a0f21fe13e60fd1389715f3c3195d2261827ac5b\nparent 249ae5cdbf0301feea9d7dab2d0893accbb75c7b\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782277189 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782277189 -0400\n\nfeat(code): improve onboarding Installed Integrations screen (#4195)\n\nOnboarding's Installed Integrations screen now lists all available\nintegrations (no \"+N more\" truncation) with clearer per-category rows\nand guidance on how to add them.\n\n---\n\nThe first-run \"Installed Integrations\" onboarding screen truncated the\n\"Available to add\" list at 8 names with \"+N more\" - which hid most\naddable extras since a fresh install has almost everything in that\nsection. This reworks the screen to list every extra as per-category\nrows with status glyphs and counts (no truncation), adds the\npreviously-dropped Other/standalone category (`quickjs`), makes the body\nscrollable, and adds copy pointing at the existing install paths (the\nmodel selector that follows installs your provider; `/install <name>`\nfor anything else) so the info is actionable without blocking\nonboarding.\n\nThe onboarding/default recommended selector intentionally favors the\ncurated recommendation set over the full installed-model list. This\nkeeps first-run setup narrow and predictable, even when users already\nhave custom or non-recommended providers installed.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/f342522b-99b6-17d0-756d-87cf23066279)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-24T04:59:50Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0827bf1b635b825121740ac8946dd6d98c815c7d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0827bf1b635b825121740ac8946dd6d98c815c7d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0827bf1b635b825121740ac8946dd6d98c815c7d/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"249ae5cdbf0301feea9d7dab2d0893accbb75c7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/249ae5cdbf0301feea9d7dab2d0893accbb75c7b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/249ae5cdbf0301feea9d7dab2d0893accbb75c7b"}]},{"sha":"249ae5cdbf0301feea9d7dab2d0893accbb75c7b","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDI0OWFlNWNkYmYwMzAxZmVlYTlkN2RhYjJkMDg5M2FjY2JiNzVjN2I","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-24T02:04:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T02:04:08Z"},"message":"style(code): hide Esc skip-setup hint in onboarding modals (#4194)\n\nKeeps Escape bound on the onboarding modals (name, dependency summary,\nand curated model selection) but stops advertising the `Esc skip setup`\nhint in their footers. The escape hatch still works for anyone who\npresses Escape — it's just no longer surfaced as a prompt, per\ndiscussion. Standard `/model` keeps its `Esc cancel` label.\n\nThe `escape` `Binding`s and the dismiss/skip logic are untouched, so\nexisting `test_escape_skips` coverage continues to assert the binding\nstays functional.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/68bbbc5d-5b24-1de8-eb78-67627981a639)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"9ef1002cebe668a88928c6b42dc0a9dc6db52152","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/9ef1002cebe668a88928c6b42dc0a9dc6db52152"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/249ae5cdbf0301feea9d7dab2d0893accbb75c7b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOzsYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfOcQAEmf1YPHBHuo4vVbZ54rIKbx\n/+MXUIo4/2UIoKR+xFMMqLSmLWWLS7jry7QkasRZDki9bvZyjT8i735zEjm1714u\nvaQ/3MSSbXw0yHST85p2otwSLu7InjqKtN2JbVinzM3kzAGaqjvtscJjuQlGja0m\nwbw6f0tAlVI7B6afqvVuxMrbb7sLyNLEvt17PBAaSXw/GDx1xG43DlM+jKkMsvEm\nVywNUpkVkNJZKt9oO1Mu+sQeKbTiN4FPMqjm1Xi62Q6vUfx+GPRnbuAfWDh+icSG\n6IMPvjZFkkeutLe1g/PqfsKbeg3ADuHa2mU5Pomem+sXT+22h/HU+BYyNsYz7an2\npxwIZyX3nCos7qIF4ToXOvnolyWFMV5UC7AVPORcWam7NyfKoE3nnPPgSaHeo2PP\nB+90mumsdCdCiEwy+3+RtpacptVn393UcGzyt+hobaOW7Kg0rRRKEcMdjchqB13E\niO2SMJZieG8kNZUem9YrGRP4lwq08YMyR7hzBKK/bp7QdPk8aMOEBGhzZPY3JA9O\n1QAOoHEOJ+wGvxzILBjRkwp7FD0B6xmam2axX9a2xRu6TuKi3rxQpHaqFwTqkExf\nfkT6qtdjqM0AyNylmhN8lpT27i5VXmqpUho9wwFKx/IOnl/nDezzCakuVsIm/xpK\n9y9TfM91IJ2ju4uCpi8g\n=Hvt1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9ef1002cebe668a88928c6b42dc0a9dc6db52152\nparent d10ba3dc162e47cc71df56b8e3d0000b6e0ed847\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782266648 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782266648 -0400\n\nstyle(code): hide Esc skip-setup hint in onboarding modals (#4194)\n\nKeeps Escape bound on the onboarding modals (name, dependency summary,\nand curated model selection) but stops advertising the `Esc skip setup`\nhint in their footers. The escape hatch still works for anyone who\npresses Escape — it's just no longer surfaced as a prompt, per\ndiscussion. Standard `/model` keeps its `Esc cancel` label.\n\nThe `escape` `Binding`s and the dismiss/skip logic are untouched, so\nexisting `test_escape_skips` coverage continues to assert the binding\nstays functional.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/68bbbc5d-5b24-1de8-eb78-67627981a639)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-24T02:04:09Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/249ae5cdbf0301feea9d7dab2d0893accbb75c7b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/249ae5cdbf0301feea9d7dab2d0893accbb75c7b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/249ae5cdbf0301feea9d7dab2d0893accbb75c7b/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d10ba3dc162e47cc71df56b8e3d0000b6e0ed847","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d10ba3dc162e47cc71df56b8e3d0000b6e0ed847","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d10ba3dc162e47cc71df56b8e3d0000b6e0ed847"}]},{"sha":"d10ba3dc162e47cc71df56b8e3d0000b6e0ed847","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQxMGJhM2RjMTYyZTQ3Y2M3MWRmNTZiOGUzZDAwMDBiNmUwZWQ4NDc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-24T01:18:25Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T01:18:25Z"},"message":"feat(code): auto-retry credentials-blocked startup after `/auth` (#4176)\n\nThe interactive coding agent now restarts automatically after you add a\nmissing provider API key via `/auth`, instead of requiring a manual\n`/restart`.\n\n---\n\nWhen the langgraph server fails to start with a\n`MissingCredentialsError` (e.g. a missing `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`), `/auth`\nis the natural place to supply the key. Previously the user then had to\ntype `/restart` (or `/model`) to actually bring the server up — closing\nthe `/auth` modal did nothing. Now closing `/auth` auto-retries startup\nonce the blocking provider's credentials resolve, mirroring the existing\ndeferred first-launch behavior. The retry reuses\n`_retry_startup_with_model` and is a no-op when no credentials-blocked\nfailure is pending or the key is still missing (so it can't loop back\ninto the same failure).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/038952da-70d6-65f8-2237-6b4828df49a5)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"315d630822ee0d5c80620caa18ee6139c557fdb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/315d630822ee0d5c80620caa18ee6139c557fdb9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d10ba3dc162e47cc71df56b8e3d0000b6e0ed847","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOzBhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/o8QAARqOqbEXeHaLKnTKIXlI0vW\nVKzzVT1UJGWndBnp72GmobSKoDmRKnpGcJsSWPItVx+gsaj9BmvCvTcW2f6NEmNV\nltVlzPb2h89vJv/BkHuV5gR3rWLxE1Jc+9Rm+C2BHUMM31wPVrk0GJf7I590OMTB\nop/VVJJdsiq7LaTNEfrUP7gQNWS3xodhrVBATr+228OwGbaJjqQ5ApUrRSpjO3Np\niEFAsEWDn0o6qJ/jgwqqh4WcAi7ukBOAHI5VPizATIfUnAQacYoJxJU9mZ5MKUS4\n3auP0RuI/HCpKi6SB3COwC5MbuNmhWVbbJ1PopNBF84xHhizoaJFmD0tLqeehWP3\n91tnOeVE4op/yIjkCg4mDcWDZFq4FDZj699TLYF2PvOkEL1MW5v6Oam+OxnFl2z5\nve9g8x4Au8AbyF0HIbofa3ax1XcIurV1dlg9OVEhTEek7GWXDFdzScUpBdVsdg8S\nJIBVb5JNdunXmp9T4SELl+ZHbOS8s5Lt33JQqv86uy/9e+DRM92q7nJEnT7NS4A1\n1CURVChango4sXqSTNftPgjsu665/jbKMxhvIWkTmo/4jlxBjunppWh8SKuD/NTm\nCRL14zr9CHWC2tEj/Wdvmuglvy9TQmELagNT6QboMtsU9KdXKvJsRzhc7DgbhHo5\nK+oydeWYaqtUTFWrjL+3\n=V0v3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 315d630822ee0d5c80620caa18ee6139c557fdb9\nparent 785c8d0061114f8f3c457d4afc35a83bd405fc1b\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782263905 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782263905 -0400\n\nfeat(code): auto-retry credentials-blocked startup after `/auth` (#4176)\n\nThe interactive coding agent now restarts automatically after you add a\nmissing provider API key via `/auth`, instead of requiring a manual\n`/restart`.\n\n---\n\nWhen the langgraph server fails to start with a\n`MissingCredentialsError` (e.g. a missing `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`), `/auth`\nis the natural place to supply the key. Previously the user then had to\ntype `/restart` (or `/model`) to actually bring the server up — closing\nthe `/auth` modal did nothing. Now closing `/auth` auto-retries startup\nonce the blocking provider's credentials resolve, mirroring the existing\ndeferred first-launch behavior. The retry reuses\n`_retry_startup_with_model` and is a no-op when no credentials-blocked\nfailure is pending or the key is still missing (so it can't loop back\ninto the same failure).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/038952da-70d6-65f8-2237-6b4828df49a5)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-24T01:18:25Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d10ba3dc162e47cc71df56b8e3d0000b6e0ed847","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d10ba3dc162e47cc71df56b8e3d0000b6e0ed847","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d10ba3dc162e47cc71df56b8e3d0000b6e0ed847/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"785c8d0061114f8f3c457d4afc35a83bd405fc1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/785c8d0061114f8f3c457d4afc35a83bd405fc1b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/785c8d0061114f8f3c457d4afc35a83bd405fc1b"}]},{"sha":"785c8d0061114f8f3c457d4afc35a83bd405fc1b","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDc4NWM4ZDAwNjExMTRmOGYzYzQ1N2Q0YWZjMzVhODNiZDQwNWZjMWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-24T01:17:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T01:17:50Z"},"message":"fix(code): quiet uv installer output and require Xcode CLT on macOS (#4180)\n\nThe install script now hides the uv installer's output by default and\nexits early on macOS when Xcode Command Line Tools are not installed.\n\n---\n\nThe uv installer's verbose download/PATH output cluttered a fresh\n`dcode` install; it's now hidden by default and shown only with\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_VERBOSE=1` or on failure. On macOS, the installer now\nfails fast with an actionable message when the Xcode Command Line Tools\nare missing, instead of letting a downstream tool (uv interpreter\ndiscovery / git) trigger the blocking macOS \"install developer tools\"\nGUI popup mid-install.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] On a fresh macOS without CLT, run the installer and confirm it\nexits with the `xcode-select --install` message instead of showing the\nGUI popup.\n- [ ] On a machine without uv, run the installer and confirm the uv\ninstaller's output is hidden unless `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_VERBOSE=1`.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/c4c6c178-52dd-957a-68b7-dcba7f3223e0)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"9f9b4a2e1d107cde01e38c001d705138b6195776","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/9f9b4a2e1d107cde01e38c001d705138b6195776"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/785c8d0061114f8f3c457d4afc35a83bd405fc1b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOzA+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJtEQABsToNY6G+y/FropPDOMQNGo\nkYwh/ZTzlGr6qBfxQicQQDw0DNalFzZxs6Qgw9Jx+h24TDHGinrivXO3rgyeEsj7\n0/0an+WL0DHdDbdQiy9mrI84Ksq6/W4a+h6CP0FGgb0crFVx6xl9wUmKSr7I/uzk\nZ5rTezjL/GTbEz4fE7j/xRrthyhEnCMU8PuNJ2h9ZpKcuz9jWkTp8ID1j3n6XJeW\nTmFZilOPZk65qd2HM7xXr2Ith7E9OBtqmsUaxj/bLnBp0Uw6hhI9q42fDTsgmoC8\nycErAh3+/89s9tckcbW6gDAaord5sCdQcc0A+GY9cS3rDudCudfyit3MK3+g35rE\n16dmqSQPI+M7N+uZHsiva9cBWc79rEX/Y1tMQoh2ZVQy84RFmNpa5crHTUpBiLxH\n/RgTZeuVnIeRkrOyZGK3Ub8fVWihZPSMfLjU1t2Epq77nAh487G5qGwQ2F0eJZ0W\nVNU62iKFvlguDzME1ugsIckScdkLIfk05/uYAr/0bF3026CYsEUXxyaQ8sPhv1GF\nXD3s1XLMek2h92Fn2fYAiSj1uZnXwi1c9KlCFjgwjFl94859YjALlp3Pee0EnVOp\nMFL33xhix9hU29Ciy166nV0kRYW2FdzZ7B5EaSf6eUA79A31IC4WFSt71C9NfIx6\njYIrwLcpzuRdR9uRV6vX\n=LufL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9f9b4a2e1d107cde01e38c001d705138b6195776\nparent c338fc914fcd383beb4b97c13f53dfb2684f8c90\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782263870 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782263870 -0400\n\nfix(code): quiet uv installer output and require Xcode CLT on macOS (#4180)\n\nThe install script now hides the uv installer's output by default and\nexits early on macOS when Xcode Command Line Tools are not installed.\n\n---\n\nThe uv installer's verbose download/PATH output cluttered a fresh\n`dcode` install; it's now hidden by default and shown only with\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_VERBOSE=1` or on failure. On macOS, the installer now\nfails fast with an actionable message when the Xcode Command Line Tools\nare missing, instead of letting a downstream tool (uv interpreter\ndiscovery / git) trigger the blocking macOS \"install developer tools\"\nGUI popup mid-install.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] On a fresh macOS without CLT, run the installer and confirm it\nexits with the `xcode-select --install` message instead of showing the\nGUI popup.\n- [ ] On a machine without uv, run the installer and confirm the uv\ninstaller's output is hidden unless `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_VERBOSE=1`.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/c4c6c178-52dd-957a-68b7-dcba7f3223e0)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-24T01:17:51Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/785c8d0061114f8f3c457d4afc35a83bd405fc1b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/785c8d0061114f8f3c457d4afc35a83bd405fc1b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/785c8d0061114f8f3c457d4afc35a83bd405fc1b/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c338fc914fcd383beb4b97c13f53dfb2684f8c90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c338fc914fcd383beb4b97c13f53dfb2684f8c90","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c338fc914fcd383beb4b97c13f53dfb2684f8c90"}]},{"sha":"c338fc914fcd383beb4b97c13f53dfb2684f8c90","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGMzMzhmYzkxNGZjZDM4M2JlYjRiOTdjMTNmNTNkZmIyNjg0ZjhjOTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-24T00:21:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T00:21:26Z"},"message":"fix(code): warn on `/trace` when thread has no messages (#4162)\n\n`/trace` now warns when the current thread has no messages yet, since\nthe LangSmith view is empty until the first message is sent.\n\n---\n\nWhen a user runs `/trace`, dcode opens the LangSmith thread view. That\nview stays empty until the first message is sent in the thread, which is\nconfusing — the user clicks through expecting to see something. This\nappends a short note after the URL when the current thread has no\nmessages yet, warning that the trace will be empty until they send their\nfirst message.\n\nThe empty-thread check reuses the existing `_has_conversation_messages`\nhelper, so it covers both deferred (busy) and immediate output paths and\ndegrades safely (no warning shown on lookup errors).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/3a51b629-ea5a-3486-ef49-8ebc226646be)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"3d8ff9043293a72859f4388ba3403026bfa074f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/3d8ff9043293a72859f4388ba3403026bfa074f4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/c338fc914fcd383beb4b97c13f53dfb2684f8c90","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOyMGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmFoQAIOVy7hpmOWu//tVSic1YHch\nR3T27yZZWpYNoPo+EmFRKMAbQ5oK4Vc+qV6RM/cbDnxAm44BcNY3/MayENGrlmKL\nlKdVMlPHM+a2K6abmdNLKMyoVR4GWrNd2bYQ03IKCW3fThxnJ9pZE8CXZ4ULPljY\nl4AdNC/+iuR1pn0rA1/cLefKfSP94WvbRAQ5LPWWjI73CYe4Hk2k+x4ZPoDMYE3C\nXA50bNuAYxtj6wOHhW6MdnFUaQ7C1RL9AXNe+z2U226773mPv/3i8CUVrs3T/x6D\nNjfubxu9syMNyuSkkhY8Pjcbx71clOKcdgPozkkYFJXuLWvoXZdmn5mwY1NjlWdH\nbk1gOvJso2HEkkvyiwrqdk1nteRr88GIeERs+jD9AF0+PbDK2KZ0m2lWiy5HNrtO\nbu8GQNfevnBxpl5T5uMomQ0nbAg40u4A9AoS5Fq3wSZxRzRoiWsPE4jLdCnORx+Y\nhQ01b5b2ly7XWOm0BP4FfrXHWobMTaOekSUyz+0UrIIAVLheo6fu4q1O83V1zpH0\nxmBW0NoDF8InmFSm/M8OlFOU/LeAw1HMvEdhNBmf+IWol3QvdmkUIM6GlD8sSSpd\nMblvYHE5iI0nStuR0TOTfTSH3LlptQrQaaJmEhEjbgUQ1e56ulEqcgkPXRfyd54Z\n88WEcwfQWJZUvKd/8byF\n=o17V\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3d8ff9043293a72859f4388ba3403026bfa074f4\nparent 456ce5c2f5487a754d1fea7046e32c03b7e27a17\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782260486 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782260486 -0400\n\nfix(code): warn on `/trace` when thread has no messages (#4162)\n\n`/trace` now warns when the current thread has no messages yet, since\nthe LangSmith view is empty until the first message is sent.\n\n---\n\nWhen a user runs `/trace`, dcode opens the LangSmith thread view. That\nview stays empty until the first message is sent in the thread, which is\nconfusing — the user clicks through expecting to see something. This\nappends a short note after the URL when the current thread has no\nmessages yet, warning that the trace will be empty until they send their\nfirst message.\n\nThe empty-thread check reuses the existing `_has_conversation_messages`\nhelper, so it covers both deferred (busy) and immediate output paths and\ndegrades safely (no warning shown on lookup errors).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/3a51b629-ea5a-3486-ef49-8ebc226646be)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-24T00:21:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c338fc914fcd383beb4b97c13f53dfb2684f8c90","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c338fc914fcd383beb4b97c13f53dfb2684f8c90","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c338fc914fcd383beb4b97c13f53dfb2684f8c90/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"456ce5c2f5487a754d1fea7046e32c03b7e27a17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/456ce5c2f5487a754d1fea7046e32c03b7e27a17","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/456ce5c2f5487a754d1fea7046e32c03b7e27a17"}]},{"sha":"456ce5c2f5487a754d1fea7046e32c03b7e27a17","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQ1NmNlNWMyZjU0ODdhNzU0ZDFmZWE3MDQ2ZTMyYzAzYjdlMjdhMTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-24T00:21:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T00:21:11Z"},"message":"fix(code): generic \"missing credentials\" in model switcher (#4182)\n\nThe model switcher now shows a generic \"missing credentials\" indicator\ninstead of the specific environment variable name.\n\n---\n\nThe `/model` switcher provider header — in both the regular selector and\nthe onboarding flow — rendered the literal env var name as helper text\n(e.g. `missing ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`). This switches the `MISSING` auth\nindicator to the generic `missing credentials` label already used for\nproviders without a named env var (e.g. `openai_codex`), keeping the\nindicator consistent and avoiding surfacing internal env var names.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/b2361e5f-76b9-ddc3-a948-49b8495c5b3a)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"dfd76103242271b4348b4b7e661f704808c3ce29","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/dfd76103242271b4348b4b7e661f704808c3ce29"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/456ce5c2f5487a754d1fea7046e32c03b7e27a17","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOyL3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKdMQAEgHNOqQ9fNbV5gAdBEnoxOb\nTh20FyqJwjDVXqHNkzY7h7JZNYTVwq7W7W2gqEH/mtrpJ3C/MFc2wXu5EYYtlHDx\nv+N3FDDlh2uxhIgm41IJypXR8NsXUG90ASTL0skeRyQFu+KkaHyZ2puH498bxQrT\np9L/63VnQWkL/jvFnsSDVKbYvBMR5Hx67kpGT58+Xy0lamojtI7JanXGdkoA4Ut5\nZxRnwOQJChKq0Dj5PHu06URgWu2j5WhrD6snP+J3Wdz/wXhl8j6ZhjC0wYBFB2pi\nOZEfHYjThuw5RNpCEFRLcfSykTSkNapOcG33LhKT065YF70F/39j3KwEdyZwF+tY\n9cMM2R9YnImlHW4D4EKE5jGBYkrjhYQMGL6Wn5rx7y31N3BGq/7BH7se7f90y6Ek\nEExMBte3pNm8gn6EzDjynb9PyZAnLcO4HACh5+qlVkKZZjOC1zANZIoW92WIDGTV\nUdJ4PymgPdsliEqsUN3msmKTT1XlGxrLcrIgZIHl1fPYwycCswGES3KI9KvRFYhm\nL39ReLBS3mbPSpRBUceQ90bv7yyqh9qLuAV1C7Xx6wcOjKOrw7QLiQu/seOilKLi\nUySMCi4YgZSBWiuswCGijAVzSOlHyxDL9Pzr/wVUQA444fGEQku+aBVZ72HoFwUz\nYXW3qaId50LZw9w+lJay\n=j+NF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree dfd76103242271b4348b4b7e661f704808c3ce29\nparent f94d417d5ad9928db967777fe1d7bc2c37684fb9\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782260471 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782260471 -0400\n\nfix(code): generic \"missing credentials\" in model switcher (#4182)\n\nThe model switcher now shows a generic \"missing credentials\" indicator\ninstead of the specific environment variable name.\n\n---\n\nThe `/model` switcher provider header — in both the regular selector and\nthe onboarding flow — rendered the literal env var name as helper text\n(e.g. `missing ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`). This switches the `MISSING` auth\nindicator to the generic `missing credentials` label already used for\nproviders without a named env var (e.g. `openai_codex`), keeping the\nindicator consistent and avoiding surfacing internal env var names.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/b2361e5f-76b9-ddc3-a948-49b8495c5b3a)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-24T00:21:11Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/456ce5c2f5487a754d1fea7046e32c03b7e27a17","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/456ce5c2f5487a754d1fea7046e32c03b7e27a17","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/456ce5c2f5487a754d1fea7046e32c03b7e27a17/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f94d417d5ad9928db967777fe1d7bc2c37684fb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f94d417d5ad9928db967777fe1d7bc2c37684fb9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f94d417d5ad9928db967777fe1d7bc2c37684fb9"}]},{"sha":"f94d417d5ad9928db967777fe1d7bc2c37684fb9","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGY5NGQ0MTdkNWFkOTkyOGRiOTY3Nzc3ZmUxZDdiYzJjMzc2ODRmYjk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-24T00:14:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T00:14:52Z"},"message":"fix(code): hide chat input action buttons in same frame as empty draft (#4178)\n\nThe floating `[ X ]`/`[ COPY ]` buttons on the chat input border only\ntoggled on the deferred `TextArea.Changed` event. History navigation and\nclear set the draft text programmatically and suppress that event, so\nwhen a draft emptied (notably tabbing through input history), the\nbuttons lingered for an extra frame. This syncs button visibility\nsynchronously when text is set programmatically so they hide/show in\nlockstep with the draft.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/89f7c717-fc07-c517-89f1-df142c799d2f)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"278c0d9035aa480ceb0ac2e1034071568e7ed3f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/278c0d9035aa480ceb0ac2e1034071568e7ed3f3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f94d417d5ad9928db967777fe1d7bc2c37684fb9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOyF8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlq4QAKntT5CgbsFBRHbRIOFQX8m5\n85a1CvQnzm6fEIcNFsZVfLLHSePs79s80KoIVbE+zHf6xi5l03kQ18BKqf/o0D/1\nBCvHNT+/MTMWzak1IixdC0PTjZ8wexbcqw3xgOd5U0maqRBVtcfa21c7BGsWQwsh\nT6xhuQdjBrEI/wUlKvoboFY7tkoZB3yf8xGYSJ7B/MmR0L5EPZ1gD4V3vhvnNOM/\ntEjKF2SYNQEzLypkeOfQwq4IDakm5TJe8rmrVIvqVJvaZhHbNwMZaQq/1L5TgY54\nsRH7K0Eg0aujUCZuXI/Fl8VypwCYDvP/B/rM5W+U8WcTGQHRO4ujBQvIh+TRqOtf\n9GhZRD4XWR8aSarxODfSi/qjmqtoipA3dHVJZpELSVqa8U1VthEqQHJyzrXMODq1\nfKD0KjBH0elYQMnDokoCVkOZkMG/0qRefiFQCfocAZXkoU2OeyeiBIGbJ1jM1KLy\nTyVXg9ofC8W0zaLh0GrCH354fOYPgXC9GI1E8YseTyE6b21FJZFUqAoJKwW+ZNHw\nJNUEU4ztLza8M2fAwZUmP+TPO5VL5ln0EFDjj7w0D98QnGSZwa47LVK+eIM2WmHP\nvr2uZ0SbV0eTZPeXQ1oictrDNdzesu3VodMmzgYdvl77elnWR59bFSMZ+kZ+CcAJ\nyhjrWM/aUg8d2bknbJSi\n=3fJz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 278c0d9035aa480ceb0ac2e1034071568e7ed3f3\nparent 8ca0a185a15f800267cc057178a348fb5063df1e\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782260092 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782260092 -0400\n\nfix(code): hide chat input action buttons in same frame as empty draft (#4178)\n\nThe floating `[ X ]`/`[ COPY ]` buttons on the chat input border only\ntoggled on the deferred `TextArea.Changed` event. History navigation and\nclear set the draft text programmatically and suppress that event, so\nwhen a draft emptied (notably tabbing through input history), the\nbuttons lingered for an extra frame. This syncs button visibility\nsynchronously when text is set programmatically so they hide/show in\nlockstep with the draft.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/89f7c717-fc07-c517-89f1-df142c799d2f)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-24T00:14:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f94d417d5ad9928db967777fe1d7bc2c37684fb9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f94d417d5ad9928db967777fe1d7bc2c37684fb9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f94d417d5ad9928db967777fe1d7bc2c37684fb9/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8ca0a185a15f800267cc057178a348fb5063df1e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8ca0a185a15f800267cc057178a348fb5063df1e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8ca0a185a15f800267cc057178a348fb5063df1e"}]},{"sha":"8ca0a185a15f800267cc057178a348fb5063df1e","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDhjYTBhMTg1YTE1ZjgwMDI2N2NjMDU3MTc4YTM0OGZiNTA2M2RmMWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-23T23:55:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T23:55:43Z"},"message":"fix(code): unpin uv self-updates and warn when a stale dcode shadows PATH (#4185)\n\n`uv tool upgrade` honors the requirement string baked into the uv tool\nreceipt, so a self-update could report success while silently\nre-resolving the same pinned version — and even a genuine upgrade has no\neffect if an older `dcode` sits earlier on the user's PATH. The update\npath now forces an unpinned `uv tool install -U` and checks for a\nshadowing binary after every upgrade, surfacing a copy-pasteable PATH\nfix instead of a misleading \"relaunch to use the new version.\"\n\n## Changes\n\n- **Unpinned uv upgrades.** `/update` and auto-update run `uv tool\ninstall -U deepagents-code` instead of `uv tool upgrade`, clearing any\n`==<version>` pin left in the receipt (from an original pinned install\nor a prior dependency refresh) that would otherwise keep re-resolving\nthe same version. `upgrade_install_command` rebuilds the requirement\nreceipt-aware so installed extras, `--with` packages, and the recorded\n`--python` survive; on receipt-introspection failure it falls back to\nthe bare command and emits a progress note that extras may not carry\nover.\n- **Shadowed-`dcode` detection.** `detect_shadowed_dcode` compares\n`shutil.which(\"dcode\")` against uv's documented executable directory\n(`_uv_tool_bin_dir`, following the `UV_TOOL_BIN_DIR → XDG_BIN_HOME →\n$XDG_DATA_HOME/../bin → ~/.local/bin` precedence). When a different\nbinary wins on PATH, `/update`, the \"Install now\" notification action,\nand startup auto-update surface a warning naming both paths plus a\nsession-scoped `export PATH=…` fix from\n`format_shadowed_dcode_fix_command`. The comparison is deliberately\nagainst the un-followed PATH entry so healthy uv symlink shims aren't\nflagged.\n- **Startup auto-update skips the re-exec when shadowed.** Re-exec'ing\nwould relaunch the old binary and trip the no-op restart guard, so the\npre-launch path prints the warning and continues on the current version.\n- **Detection can't sink a good upgrade.** All three call sites route\nthrough `detect_shadowed_dcode_safe`, which logs and returns `None` on\nany unexpected error, so a detector defect never turns a successful\nupgrade into a user-facing failure.\n- **Warning completion state for the progress modal.**\n`UpdateProgressScreen.mark_warning` adds a third terminal state —\nwarning glyph, durable status, `c` to copy the fix command — distinct\nfrom success/failure, and the \"Install now\" modal enters it instead of\nthe success state when the upgraded shim is shadowed.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Shadow detection is covered branch-by-branch: the paired symlink cases\n(uv's own shim must not flag; a symlink in another PATH dir must), the\nlegacy `deepagents-code` name fallback, and `OSError` fault injection on\npath resolution. `detect_shadowed_dcode_safe` is pinned to swallow an\nunexpected raise.\n- `upgrade_install_command` gets direct coverage of the `--python`\nquoting and `--with` assembly that the `perform_upgrade` tests stub out,\nand the modal's warning state asserts the durable status, glyph, and\ncopy-fix-command behavior.","tree":{"sha":"aedee2c760db679d38ee31d4171e62d7325e20fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/aedee2c760db679d38ee31d4171e62d7325e20fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/8ca0a185a15f800267cc057178a348fb5063df1e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOxz/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVLYQACw+cMNK6DDhPmeoAnMM7eDz\nenKkgAAknVjf/4tPR6eLMqH3lh9CRUEohmbqZvG0pKih9LNzxL1RELBz1a7kKjt3\nyQ3RKgXvtAAln1NjZWGbg+/yB7Tz4dGYTtrhZCLdU0mA0dOOmUhzarnK2raDpm7z\n05tDWmncXztSaL/99IxM/MeIoGZJg20QThGfhP9L6fQ9NP7lo7HFheBAegzM+LLR\njLrkAgp/KRCsRwN+aZkW7qOFMIXfLIy1/dBkzcbHeRo9H+SKlNEB6K5aBJfopg1t\nK3k8TvU6LwDg/XQzLoslZ590lvJVrEk4OkQnGmNPx/rdWAdD1zLkXsIjhsc4YPAv\nRWZVANsmq1veoZdFZu8cVCDP4LWrb6FiY1/FPNCJkvMtuK1Zul5ZJHrPeitKKYvt\nBYGt/wmyyqC8cdDYpUPgU7O2/Rka7ijiAPJv5p22KLgXFuKYt/GQl7AOFNMaVU7x\n5G2hgYnKm+IwU8/c2x1moF1G5YRPfadA1lxk6/VbgOQsFJv3CnYYYtfYw/XSneEr\ntFX5C30Q7KKE+s2CQhlrYsUvoAy5lEbsOHiuWSWDmnZ2BDjuPA+6mBM50o3mlAXX\nlPki85ON+C0rxcF90IIlG+XYRy3QobsZQBl4If80aoqv0IwPRpuZaanRTUYUC1ny\n7tghD427PEPCMg1gl0mf\n=9MaF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree aedee2c760db679d38ee31d4171e62d7325e20fe\nparent 2a30c0618c90a3b910865037e2666b7b3e7a2ce3\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782258943 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782258943 -0400\n\nfix(code): unpin uv self-updates and warn when a stale dcode shadows PATH (#4185)\n\n`uv tool upgrade` honors the requirement string baked into the uv tool\nreceipt, so a self-update could report success while silently\nre-resolving the same pinned version — and even a genuine upgrade has no\neffect if an older `dcode` sits earlier on the user's PATH. The update\npath now forces an unpinned `uv tool install -U` and checks for a\nshadowing binary after every upgrade, surfacing a copy-pasteable PATH\nfix instead of a misleading \"relaunch to use the new version.\"\n\n## Changes\n\n- **Unpinned uv upgrades.** `/update` and auto-update run `uv tool\ninstall -U deepagents-code` instead of `uv tool upgrade`, clearing any\n`==<version>` pin left in the receipt (from an original pinned install\nor a prior dependency refresh) that would otherwise keep re-resolving\nthe same version. `upgrade_install_command` rebuilds the requirement\nreceipt-aware so installed extras, `--with` packages, and the recorded\n`--python` survive; on receipt-introspection failure it falls back to\nthe bare command and emits a progress note that extras may not carry\nover.\n- **Shadowed-`dcode` detection.** `detect_shadowed_dcode` compares\n`shutil.which(\"dcode\")` against uv's documented executable directory\n(`_uv_tool_bin_dir`, following the `UV_TOOL_BIN_DIR → XDG_BIN_HOME →\n$XDG_DATA_HOME/../bin → ~/.local/bin` precedence). When a different\nbinary wins on PATH, `/update`, the \"Install now\" notification action,\nand startup auto-update surface a warning naming both paths plus a\nsession-scoped `export PATH=…` fix from\n`format_shadowed_dcode_fix_command`. The comparison is deliberately\nagainst the un-followed PATH entry so healthy uv symlink shims aren't\nflagged.\n- **Startup auto-update skips the re-exec when shadowed.** Re-exec'ing\nwould relaunch the old binary and trip the no-op restart guard, so the\npre-launch path prints the warning and continues on the current version.\n- **Detection can't sink a good upgrade.** All three call sites route\nthrough `detect_shadowed_dcode_safe`, which logs and returns `None` on\nany unexpected error, so a detector defect never turns a successful\nupgrade into a user-facing failure.\n- **Warning completion state for the progress modal.**\n`UpdateProgressScreen.mark_warning` adds a third terminal state —\nwarning glyph, durable status, `c` to copy the fix command — distinct\nfrom success/failure, and the \"Install now\" modal enters it instead of\nthe success state when the upgraded shim is shadowed.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Shadow detection is covered branch-by-branch: the paired symlink cases\n(uv's own shim must not flag; a symlink in another PATH dir must), the\nlegacy `deepagents-code` name fallback, and `OSError` fault injection on\npath resolution. `detect_shadowed_dcode_safe` is pinned to swallow an\nunexpected raise.\n- `upgrade_install_command` gets direct coverage of the `--python`\nquoting and `--with` assembly that the `perform_upgrade` tests stub out,\nand the modal's warning state asserts the durable status, glyph, and\ncopy-fix-command behavior.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T23:55:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8ca0a185a15f800267cc057178a348fb5063df1e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8ca0a185a15f800267cc057178a348fb5063df1e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8ca0a185a15f800267cc057178a348fb5063df1e/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"htt