165)\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","verified_at":"2026-06-23T05:52:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c1be66e76cae7fdd0b9224647d2826968dc473bb","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c1be66e76cae7fdd0b9224647d2826968dc473bb","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c1be66e76cae7fdd0b9224647d2826968dc473bb/comments","author":{"login":"hntrl","id":40191806,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMTkxODA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40191806?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl","html_url":"https://github.com/hntrl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2bb3e44243553a5f2954a0f3ec42364563842a87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2bb3e44243553a5f2954a0f3ec42364563842a87","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2bb3e44243553a5f2954a0f3ec42364563842a87"}]},{"sha":"2bb3e44243553a5f2954a0f3ec42364563842a87","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDJiYjNlNDQyNDM1NTNhNWYyOTU0YTBmM2VjNDIzNjQ1NjM4NDJhODc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-23T05:47:32Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T05:47:32Z"},"message":"feat(code): surface tracing in `doctor` and `config show` (#4163)\n\n`dcode doctor` now reports a tracing summary, and `dcode config\nshow`/`list` group tracing options under a dedicated `Tracing` section.\n\n---\n\nMakes LangSmith tracing configuration easy to inspect from the CLI\nwithout digging through env vars.\n\n`dcode doctor` gains a brief `Tracing` section reporting whether tracing\nis enabled, whether credentials are configured (presence only — the API\nkey value is never read or printed), the resolved project, and any\ncustom endpoint or replica project. It stays fully offline and flags a\nproblem only when tracing is enabled without a key *and* without a\ncustom endpoint, mirroring the existing orphaned-tracing guard (a\nkeyless self-hosted endpoint is a valid, healthy setup). The detection\nlives in a new offline `get_tracing_status` helper so it is\nindependently testable.\n\nThe `tracing.*` options move into their own `Tracing` group so `config\nshow` and `config list` render them as a dedicated section instead of\nburying them under `Models`. Grouping is first-seen order, so the new\nsection appears right after `Models` with no other changes.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] `dcode doctor` shows a `Tracing` section; with\n`LANGSMITH_TRACING=true` but no key/endpoint, the `Credentials` item is\nflagged unhealthy.\n- [ ] `dcode config show` lists a `Tracing` group.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/b0ab8323-a16c-9185-e910-a4de6bdc11ae)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4162c22ee7e21fbe0c11741ea3875acd6219ed91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/4162c22ee7e21fbe0c11741ea3875acd6219ed91"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/2bb3e44243553a5f2954a0f3ec42364563842a87","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOh30CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwy4QAJVnNa9uaSoX0xQIUg+Z1pdS\n/TD/PL1nR3bPA5yL0z0/MyUJ5PIFB6svk03AFSUh8lZ8ZFt5T49nXVLAMEu6iYUu\n/RZR7wdEuRgEv63dQXgtUjIQskV6djq1vfqlAgDXXw+nGpXYpuwY+aKmBG5n26Gq\nYNTGbcYquNQ5+xKCOI8pZalur4GbBBOJ9WWkeSIY4EMeWLTnqDzlIAeYk48bEoM4\n65dxzucjjhofTjKuM0G2IZoMzRZFpBKPO7HAscATf3IBJ7jzKMXgbJjM/bb0nTEE\nven+/UdvNegK1bxd9PDoZlGrOI7YmZydNALvzCcESJSd45EwAmzcGy3uDFQlglRL\n3iYqPj/5r2i8H5D7B+Ob8r7EnNezrNooq53tBzPumppnbHfXLpLnJ5pYM1ihW6er\nVQJsIammMt08oSf6HRykxraVOhhNRnalikm2UPIAfbGF5vgLSJwXCOfmgCoA+QyN\n+HBw3fa/o+8u5sh8kzxrx/BlQEaStaR9St+AP3wH/8SaMAA+/Xcpd6N2GMxVHsPx\nt51d7CMHuppvOA/oM7RcW0oMt/wKUI4MyNg1g4DGHzfY+gV3k35VJEVq/0A8iHbe\nuEzikBtSnNlCVTndP3T1K0EkE71fmsumnPMSFKtQMObQ3oikFqVM5ou/rihUPbYR\nKY5IA8sjYwpvE4jnJD/o\n=PfqP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4162c22ee7e21fbe0c11741ea3875acd6219ed91\nparent 9e21c346a6eb8ad25b9cc671f24527b07732e2b7\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782193652 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782193652 -0400\n\nfeat(code): surface tracing in `doctor` and `config show` (#4163)\n\n`dcode doctor` now reports a tracing summary, and `dcode config\nshow`/`list` group tracing options under a dedicated `Tracing` section.\n\n---\n\nMakes LangSmith tracing configuration easy to inspect from the CLI\nwithout digging through env vars.\n\n`dcode doctor` gains a brief `Tracing` section reporting whether tracing\nis enabled, whether credentials are configured (presence only — the API\nkey value is never read or printed), the resolved project, and any\ncustom endpoint or replica project. It stays fully offline and flags a\nproblem only when tracing is enabled without a key *and* without a\ncustom endpoint, mirroring the existing orphaned-tracing guard (a\nkeyless self-hosted endpoint is a valid, healthy setup). The detection\nlives in a new offline `get_tracing_status` helper so it is\nindependently testable.\n\nThe `tracing.*` options move into their own `Tracing` group so `config\nshow` and `config list` render them as a dedicated section instead of\nburying them under `Models`. Grouping is first-seen order, so the new\nsection appears right after `Models` with no other changes.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] `dcode doctor` shows a `Tracing` section; with\n`LANGSMITH_TRACING=true` but no key/endpoint, the `Credentials` item is\nflagged unhealthy.\n- [ ] `dcode config show` lists a `Tracing` group.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/b0ab8323-a16c-9185-e910-a4de6bdc11ae)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-23T05:47:32Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2bb3e44243553a5f2954a0f3ec42364563842a87","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2bb3e44243553a5f2954a0f3ec42364563842a87","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2bb3e44243553a5f2954a0f3ec42364563842a87/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9e21c346a6eb8ad25b9cc671f24527b07732e2b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9e21c346a6eb8ad25b9cc671f24527b07732e2b7","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9e21c346a6eb8ad25b9cc671f24527b07732e2b7"}]},{"sha":"9e21c346a6eb8ad25b9cc671f24527b07732e2b7","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDllMjFjMzQ2YTZlYjhhZDI1YjljYzY3MWYyNDUyN2IwNzczMmUyYjc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-23T05:32:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T05:32:44Z"},"message":"fix(code): skip tool interrupts once auto-approve is set (#4092)\n\nDeep Agents Code no longer splits a turn into many runs when \"approve\nalways\" is enabled; gated tool interrupts are now suppressed at the\nsource.\n\n---\n\nWhen a user enables \"approve always\" in Deep Agents Code,\n`HumanInTheLoopMiddleware` kept interrupting on every gated tool call\nand the client auto-resolved each one. Each interrupt/resume cycle\nstarts a fresh agent run, so a single turn fragmented into many runs and\nproduced noisy, hard-to-parse traces.\n\nThe fix carries the auto-approve decision in run-scoped CLI context\n(`CLIContext` / `CLIContextSchema.auto_approve`) rather than graph\nstate, and each `interrupt_on` config gains a `when` predicate\n(`_should_interrupt_tool_call`) that reads `request.runtime.context`.\nOnce approve-always is in effect the predicate returns `False`, so the\nmiddleware skips the interrupt entirely instead of pausing and being\npatched on the client. The initial turn seeds the flag from session\nsettings (`app.py`), and `textual_adapter.py` refreshes it into context\non every stream iteration — so choosing \"auto-approve all\" mid-turn\npropagates to the resuming stream and the remaining tool calls in that\nsame run also stop interrupting.\n\nAuto-approve is sourced from run context rather than graph state for two\nreasons: seeding state would require a first-turn `Command(update=...)`,\nwhich the LangGraph API server rebuilds with `goto=None` and crashes\n`_control_branch` on a fresh thread; and context is safer because the\nmodel cannot self-approve by writing state. The predicate is fail-closed\n— missing or malformed context still interrupts — and consumers accept\nboth a coerced `CLIContextSchema` (in-process) and a plain dict (over\nthe LangGraph API / RemoteGraph).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4b76ff9f-a307-5834-5471-a0d441f2a147)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Sydney Runkle <54324534+sydney-runkle@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"92affb3f973208ae9890888e5a8b0cb13390f872","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/92affb3f973208ae9890888e5a8b0cb13390f872"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/9e21c346a6eb8ad25b9cc671f24527b07732e2b7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOhp8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdG8QACTd55cNEPuiE6NOquSFgVes\nfWTKafG/Ft615Nl+DT0xDkgP9K+d302pSZMXPL5dY1P2122FlDFAXs+aC7xvta4O\nNhCKsoZMivrieymc/zoQdSP4MfO917xt+ognOTNg3ZRWS7TeKWrNAE837NnCNLP3\n0YJR7SC/nbiP9945ZEUYJjrZVCp9THNCd2fxQbFrh/7Qei6G1KMcfmiVo10w8JO/\nT1PItQfqLOPXw6B1DWQYJDyg5Xquss7ERxB99oSs3mJ/I8MsYunva2WxZIOOkBYY\ncuVWe7D+vj6B5Mgep5qv4auULKTs49rSi7zLQ87npigpGUWyeq4KcOJYW0SE7bKC\nCQR0a+GkD41HeqJYi1cHCVfv6arv8nJi/CI5CgKYDJ+KKj6UknyVbWjO+8my1WbY\ngNhjko6VSqLdGxBj98pwFvKZvedhtLgdcWi9JNSCchjH+SumphMciqaywBaRSgYt\nrv5zh+M8XSipUBm7/+N/fcH2VWnrfwlvRZaQQySVpMISR5qZ+bSIQQz0EWshOGmm\nwYrrzYA08I9tK0s4Kuc1RAGFoXQBXOTtChp2Ya1+GvLWeGzvbGADU8BrySxvVa0p\nnTnxAez1/xErTB8MevPirNPz5J0anRIUYwv0OOi9UdpgOH7iSv2VRWVCmLjUPaUt\nn7w82LTFCJ+MZ2KbC2KL\n=+L/o\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 92affb3f973208ae9890888e5a8b0cb13390f872\nparent 7beb97a2b02e2fd238baf3b6f05d43a4accf3f42\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782192764 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782192764 -0400\n\nfix(code): skip tool interrupts once auto-approve is set (#4092)\n\nDeep Agents Code no longer splits a turn into many runs when \"approve\nalways\" is enabled; gated tool interrupts are now suppressed at the\nsource.\n\n---\n\nWhen a user enables \"approve always\" in Deep Agents Code,\n`HumanInTheLoopMiddleware` kept interrupting on every gated tool call\nand the client auto-resolved each one. Each interrupt/resume cycle\nstarts a fresh agent run, so a single turn fragmented into many runs and\nproduced noisy, hard-to-parse traces.\n\nThe fix carries the auto-approve decision in run-scoped CLI context\n(`CLIContext` / `CLIContextSchema.auto_approve`) rather than graph\nstate, and each `interrupt_on` config gains a `when` predicate\n(`_should_interrupt_tool_call`) that reads `request.runtime.context`.\nOnce approve-always is in effect the predicate returns `False`, so the\nmiddleware skips the interrupt entirely instead of pausing and being\npatched on the client. The initial turn seeds the flag from session\nsettings (`app.py`), and `textual_adapter.py` refreshes it into context\non every stream iteration — so choosing \"auto-approve all\" mid-turn\npropagates to the resuming stream and the remaining tool calls in that\nsame run also stop interrupting.\n\nAuto-approve is sourced from run context rather than graph state for two\nreasons: seeding state would require a first-turn `Command(update=...)`,\nwhich the LangGraph API server rebuilds with `goto=None` and crashes\n`_control_branch` on a fresh thread; and context is safer because the\nmodel cannot self-approve by writing state. The predicate is fail-closed\n— missing or malformed context still interrupts — and consumers accept\nboth a coerced `CLIContextSchema` (in-process) and a plain dict (over\nthe LangGraph API / RemoteGraph).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4b76ff9f-a307-5834-5471-a0d441f2a147)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Sydney Runkle <54324534+sydney-runkle@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-23T05:32:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9e21c346a6eb8ad25b9cc671f24527b07732e2b7","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9e21c346a6eb8ad25b9cc671f24527b07732e2b7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9e21c346a6eb8ad25b9cc671f24527b07732e2b7/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7beb97a2b02e2fd238baf3b6f05d43a4accf3f42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7beb97a2b02e2fd238baf3b6f05d43a4accf3f42","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7beb97a2b02e2fd238baf3b6f05d43a4accf3f42"}]},{"sha":"7beb97a2b02e2fd238baf3b6f05d43a4accf3f42","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDdiZWI5N2EyYjAyZTJmZDIzOGJhZjNiNmYwNWQ0M2E0YWNjZjNmNDI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-23T05:16:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T05:16:24Z"},"message":"feat(code): allow dependency updates without requiring release (#4157)\n\n`/update --deps` (and a prompt on `/update` when already current)\nrefreshes dependencies to their newest in-range versions without waiting\nfor a new release.\n\n---\n\nDependencies are range-pinned, so newer in-range releases (e.g. a fresh\n`langchain-openai`) are already permitted by a published\n`deepagents-code` — but `/update` only ever checked the dcode version on\nPyPI and dead-ended at \"Already on the latest version\", so users had to\ndrop to raw `uv` to pull them in.\n\nThis makes the refresh first-class in the TUI:\n- `/update --deps` re-resolves the tool environment via `uv tool install\n-U deepagents-code==<current>` (`perform_dependency_refresh`), so\ncompatible dependency releases are picked up without crossing to a newer\napp version. If a dcode update also happens to be available, `/update\n--deps` first asks (via `UpdateBeforeDependenciesConfirmScreen`) whether\nto take the app update instead; declining continues with the deps-only\nrefresh.\n- Plain `/update`, when dcode is already current, computes a preflight\ndry-run plan first and only then offers the refresh through a\nconfirmation modal (`RefreshDependenciesConfirmScreen`, which previews\nthe planned changes) instead of dead-ending.\n- Both paths parse uv's environment diff and report exactly which\ndependencies moved; a normal version bump also surfaces any dependency\nchanges that rode along.\n\nEditable (and other non-uv) installs are still refused, and a dep\nrefresh stays explicit/confirmed (it is not folded into silent\nbackground auto-update), consistent with the \"announce before running\nshell\" rule. `uv tool install`/`upgrade` has no `--dry-run`, so the\npreflight plan is computed against the running tool environment with `uv\npip install --dry-run --python <sys.executable>`\n(`perform_dependency_refresh_dry_run`), using the same pinned\nrequirement, extras, and preserved `--with` packages as the real\nrefresh.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/d64c7415-11cc-947f-f5f3-67aca0ec21ed)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"d3de6bfa960b35e41354272a4abfb16d3caa25b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/d3de6bfa960b35e41354272a4abfb16d3caa25b8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/7beb97a2b02e2fd238baf3b6f05d43a4accf3f42","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOhaoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/iYQADH2YRLNHXeN29Fk7oqehUpv\nWeSVvHbRHGmsUpWaTt/R3m52qoQU2MZxF1XPFR9ROUKIxQR3UPhzYEs2xHF99Q6Z\nvP4x24msN/ucxwn+ZbXt3Jp1eHNXKW8lexMXwqiToI7JLMnxDfSUvURN5TDkRjAM\nTmG4MeebaeEIke4BSZ3ZgxpS1rty6QegIaaWECIBrmzTUYTBINgoOMliwGY/7rW4\nL4Fmw9BUq0m77XRlSh2G674CAwHvYnbI4OhH1SywXOyPZ5IUlsvxqyNVtk48DOqN\nYWaBZ/Dlj5EJLqNJ+MAJiaShNT3WeXg5OA7/SaswZS4MLFzIixmlwUSzKc15YaAU\nSCk+eMkEwqd2IVU8e4gUM6gxTVoNu+J67c0Ou6NxLTjiE1toCMzClnxVx0vue2nV\n0nydHxHJLyC3SEi1Ld5gphhTS51Azcx4wQEuPHg67XvAhRf41WOM1k/65SX3xrEl\nP1dHAFsJHs5Ldk9wywatA7qoewYAVuxkeJpySpZHGo5E424FpaMHW588GaQE3kUS\nSr/XRvbxlQ5JUazgfUTVKzJ1BgvBIOGtI8LBL/GBm1C1DRI4fT9hR7XrtoUXUzhJ\nsBi/fQnPUFABa0Keuks2cVmI+44GT60dHPX0Hdtnf0HuOFb5/mevcqcj7TfI7fvn\nntJprebrw1goepYaOKcZ\n=9O2t\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d3de6bfa960b35e41354272a4abfb16d3caa25b8\nparent e303ce986a3595f0cf458e796d857f7c8f5f8b5c\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782191784 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782191784 -0400\n\nfeat(code): allow dependency updates without requiring release (#4157)\n\n`/update --deps` (and a prompt on `/update` when already current)\nrefreshes dependencies to their newest in-range versions without waiting\nfor a new release.\n\n---\n\nDependencies are range-pinned, so newer in-range releases (e.g. a fresh\n`langchain-openai`) are already permitted by a published\n`deepagents-code` — but `/update` only ever checked the dcode version on\nPyPI and dead-ended at \"Already on the latest version\", so users had to\ndrop to raw `uv` to pull them in.\n\nThis makes the refresh first-class in the TUI:\n- `/update --deps` re-resolves the tool environment via `uv tool install\n-U deepagents-code==<current>` (`perform_dependency_refresh`), so\ncompatible dependency releases are picked up without crossing to a newer\napp version. If a dcode update also happens to be available, `/update\n--deps` first asks (via `UpdateBeforeDependenciesConfirmScreen`) whether\nto take the app update instead; declining continues with the deps-only\nrefresh.\n- Plain `/update`, when dcode is already current, computes a preflight\ndry-run plan first and only then offers the refresh through a\nconfirmation modal (`RefreshDependenciesConfirmScreen`, which previews\nthe planned changes) instead of dead-ending.\n- Both paths parse uv's environment diff and report exactly which\ndependencies moved; a normal version bump also surfaces any dependency\nchanges that rode along.\n\nEditable (and other non-uv) installs are still refused, and a dep\nrefresh stays explicit/confirmed (it is not folded into silent\nbackground auto-update), consistent with the \"announce before running\nshell\" rule. `uv tool install`/`upgrade` has no `--dry-run`, so the\npreflight plan is computed against the running tool environment with `uv\npip install --dry-run --python <sys.executable>`\n(`perform_dependency_refresh_dry_run`), using the same pinned\nrequirement, extras, and preserved `--with` packages as the real\nrefresh.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/d64c7415-11cc-947f-f5f3-67aca0ec21ed)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-23T05:16:24Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7beb97a2b02e2fd238baf3b6f05d43a4accf3f42","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7beb97a2b02e2fd238baf3b6f05d43a4accf3f42","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7beb97a2b02e2fd238baf3b6f05d43a4accf3f42/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e303ce986a3595f0cf458e796d857f7c8f5f8b5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e303ce986a3595f0cf458e796d857f7c8f5f8b5c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e303ce986a3595f0cf458e796d857f7c8f5f8b5c"}]},{"sha":"e303ce986a3595f0cf458e796d857f7c8f5f8b5c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGUzMDNjZTk4NmEzNTk1ZjBjZjQ1OGU3OTZkODU3ZjdjOGY1ZjhiNWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-23T03:47:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T03:47:06Z"},"message":"fix(code): handle LangSmith project-not-found and default tracing project (#4153)\n\n`/trace` no longer shows a scary \"project not found\" error before the\nfirst run is traced, and the default `deepagents-code` tracing project\nis now actually used when tracing is enabled with no project configured.\n\n---\n\n`/trace` surfaced LangSmith's raw `Project deepagents-code not found`\n404 as an error, even though it only means no trace has been ingested\ninto that project yet (projects are auto-created lazily on first\ningest). We now classify that 404 as a dedicated\n`LangSmithProjectNotFoundError` and show a friendly \"created on first\ntrace\" hint instead. We also default `LANGSMITH_PROJECT` to\n`deepagents-code` at bootstrap when tracing is enabled but no project is\nconfigured, so ingestion matches the name `get_langsmith_project_name()`\ndisplays and looks up. We deliberately do **not** call `create_project`.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/f2a5f732-0697-777e-0bb2-7f2fb0704f00)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a13f86eaf127f43137c5c9b45051e141f175c9cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a13f86eaf127f43137c5c9b45051e141f175c9cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/e303ce986a3595f0cf458e796d857f7c8f5f8b5c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOgG6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUjcQAJ5wmn0g76/nDVG8Le61MNuZ\nXW1Pbkcy7hrcaha3swDvA+4xKIbneYeDmnkOM0HrKFuPj5al3tPJ7SWD3u61d6LP\nU8+ptt5xoVzFqUyxzT8G7+Upq0TLO9emMxMGLyTopdVMrAqCLMIxg9f0MLi7n28I\n0klH83shZof26O9DRb6CmGS+3E5IvjkDJx+mv3EsU7bqVyElR6aKp3zHBWl2ekHd\nYOuSsgfWAvwF9CfzPzTaTyXcX29DunZVaFT0laHYH5aAzYeKPm0b/U0D5Kxp02Px\n7ZQ+2kizEiudQXtGJmRF38i6hcHRSuZIpllkWW6uXGphVLW8eRSZYUWMDutICy1P\nCBDO4bsyj8pvL7jsxDxUg3bKmD9bHn0Z2EIv11X1ZfFgfVFwspnP+K/pRLnMXRmK\nC+KqdXLiVgV8deNR5GGxxNUkNZ/iA2/CZJaIxvnlAUA0rT4H0TUjBlIDwpSlIypV\n1h5T6pGzJlXbCJvMcMFMvZRRQoGyAG6L1P0VNX/+QS6mQJPSK4GoHrbG3xBrW+od\nsjsX4cgkC7flrhzbPe+yBejQLj7POc9oYR4W/bCLus8EcjvAaH3+vriRJ6QGP8MM\nBp4mX+Qq4b8c8m044uM4zbqEyfdlmAC8Gt+3FlN5dApH+8/00nTzaSXSvYQj4xev\ndoOuh6/GpxtGeNg9OiqP\n=95gN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a13f86eaf127f43137c5c9b45051e141f175c9cb\nparent 91c0dae3fe0253f02a5926fcd3c6f796cd8d11fe\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782186426 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782186426 -0400\n\nfix(code): handle LangSmith project-not-found and default tracing project (#4153)\n\n`/trace` no longer shows a scary \"project not found\" error before the\nfirst run is traced, and the default `deepagents-code` tracing project\nis now actually used when tracing is enabled with no project configured.\n\n---\n\n`/trace` surfaced LangSmith's raw `Project deepagents-code not found`\n404 as an error, even though it only means no trace has been ingested\ninto that project yet (projects are auto-created lazily on first\ningest). We now classify that 404 as a dedicated\n`LangSmithProjectNotFoundError` and show a friendly \"created on first\ntrace\" hint instead. We also default `LANGSMITH_PROJECT` to\n`deepagents-code` at bootstrap when tracing is enabled but no project is\nconfigured, so ingestion matches the name `get_langsmith_project_name()`\ndisplays and looks up. We deliberately do **not** call `create_project`.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/f2a5f732-0697-777e-0bb2-7f2fb0704f00)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-23T03:47:07Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e303ce986a3595f0cf458e796d857f7c8f5f8b5c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e303ce986a3595f0cf458e796d857f7c8f5f8b5c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e303ce986a3595f0cf458e796d857f7c8f5f8b5c/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"91c0dae3fe0253f02a5926fcd3c6f796cd8d11fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/91c0dae3fe0253f02a5926fcd3c6f796cd8d11fe","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/91c0dae3fe0253f02a5926fcd3c6f796cd8d11fe"}]},{"sha":"91c0dae3fe0253f02a5926fcd3c6f796cd8d11fe","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDkxYzBkYWUzZmUwMjUzZjAyYTU5MjZmY2QzYzZmNzk2Y2Q4ZDExZmU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Hunter Lovell","email":"40191806+hntrl@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-23T03:07:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T03:07:29Z"},"message":"feat(code): add structured TUI display for `js_eval` (#4151)\n\nCleans up how the `js_eval` interpreter tool (enabled via\n`--interpreter`) renders in the `dcode` TUI. Previously it dumped its\nraw XML-ish wire format (`<stdout>`/`<result>`/`<error>` blocks) and a\nraw `code=` kwarg line, which read poorly.\n\n- Add a `js_eval` output formatter that parses the stdout/result/error\nblocks, unescapes XML entities, and styles them (stdout dim, result\nsuccess-colored, error error-colored). A single short scalar result\nrenders inline as `result: value` instead of a misplaced badge.\n- Suppress the raw `code=` args line and show only the first code line\n(with an ellipsis when multiline) in the tool header.\n- Make the code a collapsible block — plain, left-aligned, with\ntop/bottom padding — toggled via click or Ctrl+O.\n- Fix toggle routing so Ctrl+O falls through to the code block when the\noutput itself is not expandable.\n\n**Before**:\n<img width=\"876\" height=\"164\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-22 at 3 28 34 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6665961f-7b5f-459f-b667-5e283281f892\"\n/>\n\n**After**:\n<img width=\"876\" height=\"397\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-22 at 3 28 48 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e5a940df-5e87-4599-a7e4-05ab837243ee\"\n/>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"08b0f3cf1d01cfa642b585dc0dda8147b2e20e34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/08b0f3cf1d01cfa642b585dc0dda8147b2e20e34"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/91c0dae3fe0253f02a5926fcd3c6f796cd8d11fe","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOfhxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6ZUQAK7H6wvv1KEvT3LC60iWWb4G\netJYr0ZkPbR1MPfPZVawQGDsuoEFnstpgRPk0lXP+QZOx+FgruSR70ZYau64Gd0O\n6ViUtrwg1SGHpFflFnWcftQAkTZ4oP2eEUQ159W+Y3geIJ2ibIcT2nHg4zXm+8PV\nDLMEFSYXHHG+7qllE5G/+BoJloKf6B7rfdeGxcZiq0wTPYp0Yxzm2wf+WKj4o4X1\nU87vSgUjc7fTu6tIZx81VmfVue0s+TK44wF7t8AuPHqpyZE+vbi++7K6nJA18f09\nLH9g7B5jDR6IGLKqARXE8O1ordQMfAwQiGGatxUI2f2uxW1zd0jvSeVhn5KBgN6x\n3dtdYNpMdDwzTZJYVZsO5PlFxO7PaW2MFugH8vgdTH8cjYw7erOmevumB6no8HPj\nTawJ5GfaYQb7ybZGKZziX59e6UE583zTd7dF491nmv2hmgD5iK70FTqQbEQ9OTU1\nZC53SKeTY7pWrYLnJND2caUwKiBXx1/k9oA81F+wMQBDurJO07Mp+m1teTGNRI+j\n6E1lGG72g0783GoWy8FNDhURArbjUvdLOUSvT4vV41dviixlh1pB83mM1Rf3jjqV\nTK2TI0xhLlGq1owwK699py1BlCdn/calq/pSGyDzSCEhn9vNdnIhGwosBmP3zPvO\nNOVLAUO1/heiO1x3esju\n=P13K\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 08b0f3cf1d01cfa642b585dc0dda8147b2e20e34\nparent d79cd74cb8a44c300c3bbad712fe77e709f9221a\nauthor Hunter Lovell <40191806+hntrl@users.noreply.github.com> 1782184049 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782184049 -0400\n\nfeat(code): add structured TUI display for `js_eval` (#4151)\n\nCleans up how the `js_eval` interpreter tool (enabled via\n`--interpreter`) renders in the `dcode` TUI. Previously it dumped its\nraw XML-ish wire format (`<stdout>`/`<result>`/`<error>` blocks) and a\nraw `code=` kwarg line, which read poorly.\n\n- Add a `js_eval` output formatter that parses the stdout/result/error\nblocks, unescapes XML entities, and styles them (stdout dim, result\nsuccess-colored, error error-colored). A single short scalar result\nrenders inline as `result: value` instead of a misplaced badge.\n- Suppress the raw `code=` args line and show only the first code line\n(with an ellipsis when multiline) in the tool header.\n- Make the code a collapsible block — plain, left-aligned, with\ntop/bottom padding — toggled via click or Ctrl+O.\n- Fix toggle routing so Ctrl+O falls through to the code block when the\noutput itself is not expandable.\n\n**Before**:\n<img width=\"876\" height=\"164\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-22 at 3 28 34 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6665961f-7b5f-459f-b667-5e283281f892\"\n/>\n\n**After**:\n<img width=\"876\" height=\"397\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-22 at 3 28 48 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e5a940df-5e87-4599-a7e4-05ab837243ee\"\n/>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-23T03:07:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/91c0dae3fe0253f02a5926fcd3c6f796cd8d11fe","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/91c0dae3fe0253f02a5926fcd3c6f796cd8d11fe","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/91c0dae3fe0253f02a5926fcd3c6f796cd8d11fe/comments","author":{"login":"hntrl","id":40191806,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMTkxODA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40191806?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl","html_url":"https://github.com/hntrl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d79cd74cb8a44c300c3bbad712fe77e709f9221a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d79cd74cb8a44c300c3bbad712fe77e709f9221a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d79cd74cb8a44c300c3bbad712fe77e709f9221a"}]},{"sha":"d79cd74cb8a44c300c3bbad712fe77e709f9221a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQ3OWNkNzRjYjhhNDRjMzAwYzNiYmFkNzEyZmU3N2U3MDlmOTIyMWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-23T02:40:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T02:40:42Z"},"message":"fix(code): refocus `/mcp` filter input after in-place refresh (#4080)\n\nFix the `/mcp` viewer swallowing keystrokes after the server finishes\n(re)connecting while the modal is open.\n\n---\n\nOpening `/mcp` while the LangGraph server is still connecting (or\nreconnecting after `Ctrl+R`) shows a placeholder with no filter input.\nWhen tools finish loading, `refresh_server_info` tears down the modal\nbody and re-mounts the filter `Input` — but Textual only auto-focuses a\nwidget on its *first* mount, so the rebuilt input was left unfocused.\nThe result: keystrokes were silently swallowed and the text input\nappeared \"blocked completely.\" This restores focus to the filter input\nexplicitly after the in-place rebuild (which also covers the F2\ndisable-toggle fallback path that routes through `refresh_server_info`).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/be0a0d4f-56b7-cfa3-302c-57a13d694e9a)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"48f7c8423253d351a6656d4baae1628cea1428df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/48f7c8423253d351a6656d4baae1628cea1428df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d79cd74cb8a44c300c3bbad712fe77e709f9221a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOfIqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADq0QAEtRpyCg9YxTg9y/H+a6nOt9\n5NQuqZaeEOodB/e5E2JgNsFD7Pqq4nin0VWfUnQhXEqhs9T+doff12WZgt1UfavB\ntZQOQ1GAJ6iQdEXY9dlInJezZ7TyhNg/8BCYALWjebJ5jwolRO6T8aIhfEJ6pN/R\nNMrrJQ3oe+E3uIDc0viHLdSNx/5rDL60Q1VgNjdH4k6inoSqpf9+gPQXswh+4sFB\nsiq5M+NEFQXrvUF8pm5ZZACfbwtcnOPYXOQe7jEwI4L0EsTR/11ttrINVJTn6FrC\ncKiYKg3Je/3LsqBoVtrbeXLT1fgaDnaLj27zEG3tVJGNOIPmeQK11JkWkDt2gkup\nByygamwodefr70wd894xtNth+QBfcSYjkYvGJJ1QI+/Cn4sZQqBgB/oian2hLJUb\nQhg/SCRnS0OlPABm1tcckVaHzCaY430IOfH4tyiEFR9L2SEleaGZAz7ErB/4guL9\nZM7P+UfJy6ERkri1E/f626aUIno3dafYzbzfeZPZNaFZv0mSaITuKRAfP4DicoL7\nkE/m0OCgiyRk49oba10uz2jE+KO25UVYk/DbIu50IwhQoyjG08JRoIm8wgC0QMw/\n+I6eZEwOCnMUyi8h9w6IgSlAxXSZ0RGvREU89tqQazsc8PQdi8kFHsYTGZ8MlOKU\nEarWz13oj/DC2RnoGEC5\n=983U\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 48f7c8423253d351a6656d4baae1628cea1428df\nparent c20546feac7876786e6816776d1ccfa5fcd4b2c8\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782182442 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782182442 -0400\n\nfix(code): refocus `/mcp` filter input after in-place refresh (#4080)\n\nFix the `/mcp` viewer swallowing keystrokes after the server finishes\n(re)connecting while the modal is open.\n\n---\n\nOpening `/mcp` while the LangGraph server is still connecting (or\nreconnecting after `Ctrl+R`) shows a placeholder with no filter input.\nWhen tools finish loading, `refresh_server_info` tears down the modal\nbody and re-mounts the filter `Input` — but Textual only auto-focuses a\nwidget on its *first* mount, so the rebuilt input was left unfocused.\nThe result: keystrokes were silently swallowed and the text input\nappeared \"blocked completely.\" This restores focus to the filter input\nexplicitly after the in-place rebuild (which also covers the F2\ndisable-toggle fallback path that routes through `refresh_server_info`).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/be0a0d4f-56b7-cfa3-302c-57a13d694e9a)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-23T02:40:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d79cd74cb8a44c300c3bbad712fe77e709f9221a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d79cd74cb8a44c300c3bbad712fe77e709f9221a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d79cd74cb8a44c300c3bbad712fe77e709f9221a/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c20546feac7876786e6816776d1ccfa5fcd4b2c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c20546feac7876786e6816776d1ccfa5fcd4b2c8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c20546feac7876786e6816776d1ccfa5fcd4b2c8"}]},{"sha":"c20546feac7876786e6816776d1ccfa5fcd4b2c8","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGMyMDU0NmZlYWM3ODc2Nzg2ZTY4MTY3NzZkMWNjZmE1ZmNkNGIyYzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-23T02:25:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T02:25:33Z"},"message":"feat(code): clear chat input via `esc+esc`, add `[ X ]/[ COPY ]` buttons (#4000)\n\nClear the chat input with <kbd>esc</kbd>+<kbd>esc</kbd> (undoable via\n<kbd>ctrl+z</kbd>) or the new on-screen `[ X ]`/`[ COPY ]` buttons.\n\n---\n\nAdds quick ways to discard or copy a chat-input draft when you change\nyour mind, instead of selecting all and deleting.\n\n- <kbd>esc + esc</kbd> clears the draft: the first <kbd>Esc</kbd> (when\nthere is nothing else to interrupt) arms a pending clear and shows a\nhint; a second <kbd>Esc</kbd> within the window clears it.\n- <kbd>ctrl+z</kbd> to undo: the clear is an undoable `TextArea` edit\n(via `discard_text`), so a mistaken clear can be restored.\n- **`[ X ]` and `[ COPY ]` buttons** on the right of the input row\nprovide discoverable mouse alternatives — `[ X ]` clears (undoable), `[\nCOPY ]` copies the draft to the clipboard. This addresses the request\nfor buttons so these operations don't require memorizing shortcuts.\n\nThe buttons use fixed widths because `width: auto` collapsed to 0 next\nto the `1fr` text area.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"1f4d23c5c3e466f3bcd7b3972d5427d32b68e8c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/1f4d23c5c3e466f3bcd7b3972d5427d32b68e8c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/c20546feac7876786e6816776d1ccfa5fcd4b2c8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOe6dCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATtwQAHt8gfGqnwuIDCd4cA53ASfR\nSZOzoU4Oapr2v6Q9ERae/EYlniuopgsihtWPOfQTpQUIUbYmsFGxEb7v2MOGmLbg\nWQnOT39jLp+Lfe+kW8VDxLRcvfDhgilfbxqvYlkqK3Gp60+7nROzk1FpqPd0V305\n/1jmn/WbZKfdmTCSLPdnRkLGaZWmO9uqCTGZhG/c1r2igzQCeAiYgkro9z/A5R6P\nnu9u/4LmG8rwcba+eY842CQlbwt9DZRjj/4PQc6o1JG2lHwimdzGoExE1ob4MRQ6\nWd9Sn9/bZIGyvRKsANcWongeAGlL2afSylv6ZMnNQYxNcdjG+VE5xLohfaqcalPQ\nJFigaB7WBv1c07PxSFhD4JSe9fRRd/NIfnbv/Xx4q30GtfcidztGSdRXur07OZjT\n+wnXokwhf8BVlHDoBr5Q5zE7WGpD2gocJ1JVsWZAWy6RuscuCg60kBMcdO/6XoFP\nE90QeX/ItN+wSxpY1DvN4EWensdKugbW1ReUpBjBkBzbEcxk6JVMoiwaYnaE5APC\ndNuEZUrXbDgJwIbnzOO2zyZD1WFYGzZ15HaBi4i4h20bN7gjxqGeSCrMvbBqNKyr\neZjomT0lOfZpnbXbbLZsBKZ74/7U5q9CC+KFTCWk7UXqHOPtbNO77QBEcXb939e0\n4DEY3KstOeXpS/sNndJy\n=bC5A\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1f4d23c5c3e466f3bcd7b3972d5427d32b68e8c5\nparent 1b461a0d6c6a7a6d323db18505596fcce4326b92\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782181533 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782181533 -0400\n\nfeat(code): clear chat input via `esc+esc`, add `[ X ]/[ COPY ]` buttons (#4000)\n\nClear the chat input with <kbd>esc</kbd>+<kbd>esc</kbd> (undoable via\n<kbd>ctrl+z</kbd>) or the new on-screen `[ X ]`/`[ COPY ]` buttons.\n\n---\n\nAdds quick ways to discard or copy a chat-input draft when you change\nyour mind, instead of selecting all and deleting.\n\n- <kbd>esc + esc</kbd> clears the draft: the first <kbd>Esc</kbd> (when\nthere is nothing else to interrupt) arms a pending clear and shows a\nhint; a second <kbd>Esc</kbd> within the window clears it.\n- <kbd>ctrl+z</kbd> to undo: the clear is an undoable `TextArea` edit\n(via `discard_text`), so a mistaken clear can be restored.\n- **`[ X ]` and `[ COPY ]` buttons** on the right of the input row\nprovide discoverable mouse alternatives — `[ X ]` clears (undoable), `[\nCOPY ]` copies the draft to the clipboard. This addresses the request\nfor buttons so these operations don't require memorizing shortcuts.\n\nThe buttons use fixed widths because `width: auto` collapsed to 0 next\nto the `1fr` text area.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-23T02:25:33Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c20546feac7876786e6816776d1ccfa5fcd4b2c8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c20546feac7876786e6816776d1ccfa5fcd4b2c8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c20546feac7876786e6816776d1ccfa5fcd4b2c8/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1b461a0d6c6a7a6d323db18505596fcce4326b92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1b461a0d6c6a7a6d323db18505596fcce4326b92","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1b461a0d6c6a7a6d323db18505596fcce4326b92"}]},{"sha":"1b461a0d6c6a7a6d323db18505596fcce4326b92","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDFiNDYxYTBkNmM2YTdhNmQzMjNkYjE4NTA1NTk2ZmNjZTQzMjZiOTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-23T02:15:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T02:15:17Z"},"message":"fix(quickjs): normalize nested `undefined` tool args (#3935)\n\nCloses #3926\n\n---\n\nIn programmatic tool calling, a JS call like `await tools.myTool({ name:\nundefined })` marshaled the property value through to Pydantic as the\nQuickJS `Undefined` sentinel, raising a validation error instead of\nletting the tool's schema default apply.\n\n`_normalize_tool_input` already mapped a top-level `undefined`/`null`\npayload to `{}`, but nested object properties were untouched. This\nrecursively omits dict keys whose value is `undefined` (so JS \"absent\"\nsemantics map to schema defaults) and converts `undefined` array entries\nto `None` rather than dropping them, preserving array indices. Identity\ncomparison against the `UNDEFINED` singleton was also unreliable since\nmarshaling yields fresh `Undefined` instances, so detection now uses an\n`isinstance` check.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"7fc83b2bc4167e5c62731da6fcc3588636b01f4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/7fc83b2bc4167e5c62731da6fcc3588636b01f4d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/1b461a0d6c6a7a6d323db18505596fcce4326b92","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOew1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtvUQAJiQgAQFHM8x4qB9j6o5yFsS\nTDCOX6WysjjiUvQc1BKHHxL0ynSwa6tsO8+SLEbcLpsLPXxGH8aBl03kkIvVRYZq\n41QEQVpLvmpl30XFle/4AV/cArQWar3Qq5C9DgEgKa5709tsTgH4mt1ggHlyrOF1\nmXHuHw0E2wDoKAcqFtj9SGxvOLPsHE907u/KmOfM59RuBCIQO77DEmiDMWPMvwzR\nvxEAva8ZGhYKCdRSK55BCmouUsiTaUBsn86pFRbBYJh9x+/9LivMa/q3ZhuIFkX8\nsHZMRRg6ZQIyqXhdz+fSXPZYZpJdvB7AVX/4P+GP03IxsOxs6gSRTdRMx6RmDLJm\nrk4pu9K5KdcratNNeoyD9DSQfGqitNzHFgkEqCh3zdB78ICGr5ADEyR5xH0EG/2P\ni0SE7hGGZMfbOGWnXyrPNrGKD2rWq7F2duBAGITTbONsPUDNSOC/MRulQiWcfrIo\nMVEO65s+dNKdyL9B6FiMZBBaxEqTg0kBbmNzqyaa3JifLqUOOhC8rlrykol6gXsK\n9ghb+xXzeHZtwjYN+39/FCoXcXb4HOGDPmuQFO0BVDlWHd0oI/usnkGO+de4Vo53\nj66r+pwjoLDtskUxHCl8wZ436lsMHBP0AC0p414EikJBiM5TbZF+tRax7gS7y626\ncU6BNnUSHiegOxrdAaKu\n=hQsA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7fc83b2bc4167e5c62731da6fcc3588636b01f4d\nparent 09f1e6a8a0188db7817423fcef0093d326318dbd\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782180917 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782180917 -0400\n\nfix(quickjs): normalize nested `undefined` tool args (#3935)\n\nCloses #3926\n\n---\n\nIn programmatic tool calling, a JS call like `await tools.myTool({ name:\nundefined })` marshaled the property value through to Pydantic as the\nQuickJS `Undefined` sentinel, raising a validation error instead of\nletting the tool's schema default apply.\n\n`_normalize_tool_input` already mapped a top-level `undefined`/`null`\npayload to `{}`, but nested object properties were untouched. This\nrecursively omits dict keys whose value is `undefined` (so JS \"absent\"\nsemantics map to schema defaults) and converts `undefined` array entries\nto `None` rather than dropping them, preserving array indices. Identity\ncomparison against the `UNDEFINED` singleton was also unreliable since\nmarshaling yields fresh `Undefined` instances, so detection now uses an\n`isinstance` check.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-23T02:15:18Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1b461a0d6c6a7a6d323db18505596fcce4326b92","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1b461a0d6c6a7a6d323db18505596fcce4326b92","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1b461a0d6c6a7a6d323db18505596fcce4326b92/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"09f1e6a8a0188db7817423fcef0093d326318dbd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/09f1e6a8a0188db7817423fcef0093d326318dbd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/09f1e6a8a0188db7817423fcef0093d326318dbd"}]},{"sha":"09f1e6a8a0188db7817423fcef0093d326318dbd","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDA5ZjFlNmE4YTAxODhkYjc4MTc0MjNmY2VmMDA5M2QzMjYzMThkYmQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-23T00:44:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T00:44:51Z"},"message":"ci(infra): credit releaser in release notes (#4154)\n\nRelease notes did not say who shipped a release, which makes it harder\nto see who handled the final release step. This resolves the releaser\nfrom the release PR merge, falls back to the actor who triggered the\nworkflow when the release commit has no associated merged PR, and skips\nbot accounts.\n\nThe footer always adds `Released by: @username` when a human releaser is\nresolved. This is intentionally independent of the community-contributor\nand internal-maintainer lists — releasing is a distinct role from\ncontributing the changes — so a user who both authored changes and\nmerged the release is credited in both places.\n\nWhen the release-PR lookup hits a real API failure (as opposed to the\ncommit genuinely having no merged PR), the step emits a `::warning::`\nand falls back to the actor rather than failing silently, so a\nmis-credit leaves a breadcrumb in the run log. This mirrors the existing\nlabel-resolution lookup elsewhere in the workflow.","tree":{"sha":"0247bfea6035908e8f27b86856f2d58d088d7253","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/0247bfea6035908e8f27b86856f2d58d088d7253"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/09f1e6a8a0188db7817423fcef0093d326318dbd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOdcDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJYEQABPgBaSY95gkjSsype5Ow8HH\n+XqWUYnXsFPQLD+BrWxb8hFQKlU17QsTytXpBHl4WJkLbuYYFLgwV+Nk9cLoGni9\nU/mEjh80DrHAbjGFVrJWO5ssKe3eaA/hGHHc5+lobU5DoyNJkopxgovaxScRIcs0\n4XCk1xCNfALamDTbVzwCszHob+rqBp4aQNY7WVyJFiFE8SfEGpX2f+iKHh5cDldx\nQ8ZNiguWMVk23Og/+JEQLhqH6V1CYyl0p/rQH5U518lZaM0Ilot6ogt8h3x/PUOo\nK//sv35Sd7Czk7Ck3Z86tcX+hzverKL4VAuDBoqgYz2hB/JK78kpbLQkakn4Yk0r\nUads/SKjMm8oH3ackOmNqly9wxerQ/M9wYxedKw2N1SzL7HATq1EmIJcfPJDGVMY\nBriUauLoB46O8uI/3LLJqXNWKoW8xHPi+Y0zaqX/a8JnYpq/sQCpqF5g4aP/Gr2V\nhnCPRod2W4TRe6tY55P8xP3ObhuuAnMHLZxAql98f2Ze9q8Ld1dxfneLTXXdtMDO\nD0A03GAj2CdXN8tqm9EYsv7m4Qa+DLNzRDx7SsTJmJgV+vRpGOakt/B2rfhCOuWz\nY9jAsMvxAZgbbTPB+HnLdlvpgleSCUsRuo/x3CkCN5XYmyEaMdOtPy7NhFSYgGVA\n8n30LZZ/zEWAykgCMl2k\n=E1T8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0247bfea6035908e8f27b86856f2d58d088d7253\nparent eb9de75b17a8c95fda8f9ea4e5b127c5f6e44d5d\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782175491 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782175491 -0400\n\nci(infra): credit releaser in release notes (#4154)\n\nRelease notes did not say who shipped a release, which makes it harder\nto see who handled the final release step. This resolves the releaser\nfrom the release PR merge, falls back to the actor who triggered the\nworkflow when the release commit has no associated merged PR, and skips\nbot accounts.\n\nThe footer always adds `Released by: @username` when a human releaser is\nresolved. This is intentionally independent of the community-contributor\nand internal-maintainer lists — releasing is a distinct role from\ncontributing the changes — so a user who both authored changes and\nmerged the release is credited in both places.\n\nWhen the release-PR lookup hits a real API failure (as opposed to the\ncommit genuinely having no merged PR), the step emits a `::warning::`\nand falls back to the actor rather than failing silently, so a\nmis-credit leaves a breadcrumb in the run log. This mirrors the existing\nlabel-resolution lookup elsewhere in the workflow.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T00:44:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/09f1e6a8a0188db7817423fcef0093d326318dbd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/09f1e6a8a0188db7817423fcef0093d326318dbd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/09f1e6a8a0188db7817423fcef0093d326318dbd/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"eb9de75b17a8c95fda8f9ea4e5b127c5f6e44d5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/eb9de75b17a8c95fda8f9ea4e5b127c5f6e44d5d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/eb9de75b17a8c95fda8f9ea4e5b127c5f6e44d5d"}]},{"sha":"eb9de75b17a8c95fda8f9ea4e5b127c5f6e44d5d","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGViOWRlNzViMTdhOGM5NWZkYThmOWVhNGU1YjEyN2M1ZjZlNDRkNWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Hunter Lovell","email":"40191806+hntrl@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-22T22:59:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T22:59:56Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump `langchain-quickjs` in dcode and evals (#4150)\n\n## Summary\n\nBumps the `langchain-quickjs` dependency constraints to the current\n`0.3.x` line in `libs/code` and `libs/evals`.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`libs/code/pyproject.toml`**: bump the `test` dependency group\nconstraint from `>=0.2.0,<0.3.0` to `>=0.3.0,<0.4.0`, matching the\n`quickjs` optional extra (which was already `>=0.3.0,<0.4.0`).\n- **`libs/code/deepagents_code/agent.py`**: update a stale docstring\nversion reference (`>=0.1.2,<0.2.0` -> `>=0.3.0,<0.4.0`).\n- **`libs/evals/pyproject.toml`**: bump `>=0.1.4` -> `>=0.3.0,<0.4.0`\n(adds an upper bound, consistent with the rest of the repo).\n- **Lockfiles**: re-ran `uv lock` in both libs. This also pulled\n`quickjs-rs` `0.2.0` -> `0.2.3` transitively.\n\n## Notes\n\n`0.3.0` is the latest published version on PyPI. In both libs the\ndependency resolves through the editable `../partners/quickjs` path\nlocally.","tree":{"sha":"e315f36c133b6d6de423e4d9fa438e47d000e19c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e315f36c133b6d6de423e4d9fa438e47d000e19c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/eb9de75b17a8c95fda8f9ea4e5b127c5f6e44d5d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOb5sCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcUIQAGVqW/tVKbbjFc3X8XFOPk1p\nLZDJqq810ZQa2Ef6Eeh2awWVs+guXaWi91RyGHnPLBEOmvHT6yyn9JvJ3B6DAe/h\nk8Pbz6BJHtVucdz3WaHXc34StkNwQ91DdbZolnbvbN1BQzk45eL9V+wxZoqon0+H\niSZlfLNd4UutFaoKWTGY+LDCxqGvLw2xX9YHyFJsxbfEU/RrSdroYxp6ycz4jfZh\n7Z0CVP3JztaQCFyZPNe0WM/NDggYcu8LutkTG4YnF3OIQczgqNSjm4NMjTb4AdWM\n0xTCv13Gq56N0wSM753pRFXe31FfdX5XzqxCKDUk4mSCjSfzzHkBp5LGRxCcwN5a\n8+KlV3K2smxUEN97hmSfz4UBzKaTibTGsoioSp3NLdqHIkUShP8UpEwSoL2qVAO/\nGHQ0aEUnMLWrBki4E1CjPlEWfGSrXHHiST0yhw78AuyNoddkY98kY8OhoTy60vdh\nNXIG30apvpSUqj74zvQAnKpmsM/fBrXDTjSu15+k+PgW0o71fnpRUzZwUh7fAf0K\n7GqSYPQXG/RKcdX16LQ11aF0GLonnIMl6Kx1XW4iAUiTFXGzqVqBsOCY5xAq/xQA\nXhuIdt2GrIfr1gaskBOzk8izDVkSqnW2juzQ7EHW9bs1BLx61aACXw2L6Kt1ai/Q\n9SaXlNrcniT4sGeVnm0M\n=CDrE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e315f36c133b6d6de423e4d9fa438e47d000e19c\nparent 2eb5f1252fd0a817b41299631d676b3618493966\nauthor Hunter Lovell <40191806+hntrl@users.noreply.github.com> 1782169196 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782169196 -0700\n\nchore(deps): bump `langchain-quickjs` in dcode and evals (#4150)\n\n## Summary\n\nBumps the `langchain-quickjs` dependency constraints to the current\n`0.3.x` line in `libs/code` and `libs/evals`.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`libs/code/pyproject.toml`**: bump the `test` dependency group\nconstraint from `>=0.2.0,<0.3.0` to `>=0.3.0,<0.4.0`, matching the\n`quickjs` optional extra (which was already `>=0.3.0,<0.4.0`).\n- **`libs/code/deepagents_code/agent.py`**: update a stale docstring\nversion reference (`>=0.1.2,<0.2.0` -> `>=0.3.0,<0.4.0`).\n- **`libs/evals/pyproject.toml`**: bump `>=0.1.4` -> `>=0.3.0,<0.4.0`\n(adds an upper bound, consistent with the rest of the repo).\n- **Lockfiles**: re-ran `uv lock` in both libs. This also pulled\n`quickjs-rs` `0.2.0` -> `0.2.3` transitively.\n\n## Notes\n\n`0.3.0` is the latest published version on PyPI. In both libs the\ndependency resolves through the editable `../partners/quickjs` path\nlocally.","verified_at":"2026-06-22T22:59:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/eb9de75b17a8c95fda8f9ea4e5b127c5f6e44d5d","html_url":"https://github.com/l