"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2eb5f1252fd0a817b41299631d676b3618493966","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2eb5f1252fd0a817b41299631d676b3618493966","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2eb5f1252fd0a817b41299631d676b3618493966"}]},{"sha":"2eb5f1252fd0a817b41299631d676b3618493966","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDJlYjVmMTI1MmZkMGE4MTdiNDEyOTk2MzFkNjc2YjM2MTg0OTM5NjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-22T22:51:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T22:51:58Z"},"message":"fix(infra): expand PR labeler scope aliases to all package components (#4152)\n\nExtends the scope-rewrite step in `pr_labeler.yml` so non-release PR\ntitles get every package-component scope normalized to its canonical\nshort scope, not just `deepagents`. Previously the renamer only handled\n`deepagents → sdk`; titles using `deepagents-acp`, `deepagents-cli`,\n`deepagents-code`, or `deepagents-talon` passed through unrewritten, so\nthe downstream title-based labels (and matching against the lint\nconfig's allowed scopes) saw a scope the labeler wasn't mapping.","tree":{"sha":"d0c23b26d474cb3793286c9b39b01f598c114be3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/d0c23b26d474cb3793286c9b39b01f598c114be3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/2eb5f1252fd0a817b41299631d676b3618493966","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqObyOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3tcQAGejKMwznR0J6Qy3hbtGxWMv\ng7gHVrK7eNCDSiH0jPBm+UWtnWJ5VFRC0bnLwfpcIK32yZJtqzpUNF/NYAyzSzhS\nXQmB6MDOnacIWXd2ryf53vy+naDz3hM/F+sQcNloZcAyiGYN/2A1bsdxF6Wtjgqv\ncuqgdSyaaK9CCCAsefbF0PLsebiYBoDz7AaPcmvv6KzuTL7F6s1owBM7/aqmbvzt\njACnAN091eKYErvv2yuIqsXn5exb+StRkmx8nzT7oUj8XTG1aaNa3ohqpiFwP8qQ\nFHdVO+EsfzZB4U4QI010Gtg1puFGNHMF5uPGyS3ZZwrxDLz7sDyb+/qOZBpGP/4X\nCTVDXVPqvBMLbLL9xD0ID1c8YT1VM/jS3rRRaeWLX5Qtu8x5aeBM9KakfywZCG9T\noUo2yXJzQ780J1gpLPdN1zAzdhxUZrVMwi1D+hRW4VR8FmfbXA9jBXOhArmzOfIV\nDNW7jhjiIAuU7PZ//Xbj9VMltSbOoJWH1E3qwONdTA0g2KL7nSqwyW5rNmg/oUw3\nCzP8CIj6usIqezc3PBqEhqVqM5Kj0WZbk7fYo1a9weZDW7yyPKqIf/Dd4ZeN65Oz\nA1c/5rPh0SFf5SC4iPL4Yi7A6HtNYPGabK2QLUuFzyNrfGVMuHNhv75DhsKPnMdl\nbxwBWscmlSYYD4IvWsKx\n=+Nbf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d0c23b26d474cb3793286c9b39b01f598c114be3\nparent 81797312c7d857e7d94d03c9c695cd3c8d88799a\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782168718 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782168718 -0400\n\nfix(infra): expand PR labeler scope aliases to all package components (#4152)\n\nExtends the scope-rewrite step in `pr_labeler.yml` so non-release PR\ntitles get every package-component scope normalized to its canonical\nshort scope, not just `deepagents`. Previously the renamer only handled\n`deepagents → sdk`; titles using `deepagents-acp`, `deepagents-cli`,\n`deepagents-code`, or `deepagents-talon` passed through unrewritten, so\nthe downstream title-based labels (and matching against the lint\nconfig's allowed scopes) saw a scope the labeler wasn't mapping.","verified_at":"2026-06-22T22:51:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2eb5f1252fd0a817b41299631d676b3618493966","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2eb5f1252fd0a817b41299631d676b3618493966","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2eb5f1252fd0a817b41299631d676b3618493966/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"81797312c7d857e7d94d03c9c695cd3c8d88799a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/81797312c7d857e7d94d03c9c695cd3c8d88799a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/81797312c7d857e7d94d03c9c695cd3c8d88799a"}]},{"sha":"81797312c7d857e7d94d03c9c695cd3c8d88799a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDgxNzk3MzEyYzdkODU3ZTdkOTRkMDNjOWM2OTVjZDNjOGQ4ODc5OWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-22T22:51:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T22:51:41Z"},"message":"feat(code): `dcode doctor` diagnostics command (#4148)\n\nAdd a `dcode doctor` command that prints install diagnostics (versions,\nplatform, update status, config locations), with `--json` support.\n\n---\n\nAdds a `dcode doctor` subcommand to `deepagents-code`, inspired by\n`claude doctor`. It prints a grouped, tree-style summary of the install\n(versions, platform, install method, path), update status, and on-disk\nconfig locations, with a `--json` mode for machine-readable output.\n\nIt deliberately runs offline — the update section reads only the local\ncache via `get_cached_update_available` and never contacts PyPI — and\nreuses existing helpers (`detect_install_method`,\n`is_auto_update_enabled`, editable-install detection, config paths) so\nthe output stays consistent with `dcode --version` and `dcode update`.\nAll rendered values go through `rich.markup.escape` with\n`highlight=False`.\n\nThe new command is a leaf subcommand (like `update`), so it is\nintentionally not registered in `_HELP_SPECS`. `ui.show_doctor_help`\nbacks `dcode doctor -h`, and the command is listed in the top-level help\nusage.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/74c251d7-548f-ee57-6e48-c76e1bd66a1a)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ff27ad4933014e21022e5d7a5853785affb5334d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/ff27ad4933014e21022e5d7a5853785affb5334d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/81797312c7d857e7d94d03c9c695cd3c8d88799a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqObx9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7FYQAKPEXRIaLjKBP8kz+Oza7pjP\n/a7wwakiRlcwO6LJGlw2oTKUUA0lUjjgOOxlfs+F4oIbgMRFifaNzzDXl6yHazbE\nRgiMPcmbcYLO++N958NmayJhzQSCgoOxKMyO1X4hFjgGfG6aeenywVUzNkPqs5kT\n0S42rwHKMp3ZQ22W1eEDpb8hhoQcdHXmzUyPHNA524VFP86TxcY30vp6Tr9qajS7\nB5tsMhN7TNB75iXb1nOODNihKfO4b0FzV0+eXLn8WDjNe6cC4T3nfmttAb7qQy66\n3+kYZj0ZmOLDoiSmQ5lttRzDKn7uvrD3a2tM5VY80lZo9LtjFQJO0UPnC8peF2oV\nVhZdNUiGO6nwf8v97cCnjkrKX9++seJlpp/hase1Yx2Wa5J1jdQ6LWaqQ1rDMTgD\nnmDbDEK7fMDD5BKH5VFVKzDfMRJnxScizf500dldt2JszOw1nZ0bwR6P2Wzte8LJ\nHEfk76H+lN5LBWcTJpks58BQVMCDAqQWGLht8Ansmk74ZBXl9S8QfM2h0ASHczgD\nvAT4IyuXofd3qDQMPa8xYZNNIWkIYDkaIsAboB+SPTonHlHtTWo1khC7ByeURbnp\nnUKnMrhUGSmT3dS9vZFyh8a4S8uGEdG8U9/QfHuCHIqrl9/7chDUMm+hBueYfWt2\n1NeiHNf0aoQlXDlepyc5\n=kzi8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ff27ad4933014e21022e5d7a5853785affb5334d\nparent a795988061816179df702b0deed710df996307da\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782168701 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782168701 -0400\n\nfeat(code): `dcode doctor` diagnostics command (#4148)\n\nAdd a `dcode doctor` command that prints install diagnostics (versions,\nplatform, update status, config locations), with `--json` support.\n\n---\n\nAdds a `dcode doctor` subcommand to `deepagents-code`, inspired by\n`claude doctor`. It prints a grouped, tree-style summary of the install\n(versions, platform, install method, path), update status, and on-disk\nconfig locations, with a `--json` mode for machine-readable output.\n\nIt deliberately runs offline — the update section reads only the local\ncache via `get_cached_update_available` and never contacts PyPI — and\nreuses existing helpers (`detect_install_method`,\n`is_auto_update_enabled`, editable-install detection, config paths) so\nthe output stays consistent with `dcode --version` and `dcode update`.\nAll rendered values go through `rich.markup.escape` with\n`highlight=False`.\n\nThe new command is a leaf subcommand (like `update`), so it is\nintentionally not registered in `_HELP_SPECS`. `ui.show_doctor_help`\nbacks `dcode doctor -h`, and the command is listed in the top-level help\nusage.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/74c251d7-548f-ee57-6e48-c76e1bd66a1a)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-22T22:51:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/81797312c7d857e7d94d03c9c695cd3c8d88799a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/81797312c7d857e7d94d03c9c695cd3c8d88799a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/81797312c7d857e7d94d03c9c695cd3c8d88799a/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a795988061816179df702b0deed710df996307da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a795988061816179df702b0deed710df996307da","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a795988061816179df702b0deed710df996307da"}]},{"sha":"a795988061816179df702b0deed710df996307da","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGE3OTU5ODgwNjE4MTYxNzlkZjcwMmIwZGVlZDcxMGRmOTk2MzA3ZGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"github-actions[bot]","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-22T22:46:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T22:46:42Z"},"message":"release(langchain-quickjs): 0.3.1 (#4085)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Everything below this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.3.1](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/langchain-quickjs==0.3.0...langchain-quickjs==0.3.1)\n(2026-06-22)\n\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* **quickjs:** persist top-level JS declarations across evals\n([#4147](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4147))\n([7574fea](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7574fea88b51c77f7afa8279c4f561d6ecb47e3f))\n* **quickjs:** ptc tools in tools namespace are rendered without\nprepended `tools.` in system prompt and task as ptc duplicated task\nglobal ([#4075](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4075))\n([014a903](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/014a9033af70b5b8b08ad2eb36f98590f5f1cca8))\n\n---\n\n_Everything above this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"7ce30cd23ee253afd2f80ac3022d147e79786014","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/7ce30cd23ee253afd2f80ac3022d147e79786014"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/a795988061816179df702b0deed710df996307da","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqObtSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAACMQAFuUvOmDyj5Ny9ZjF7yUANfQ\nvDNbYQDmh72NWD0NhOcTkmXsGgWoNulCwAqNQDL1hppvy2NOJ1xTMxUp7XVqktAd\n6fZAUdLrOiGgXOO95a95s9KdaTwDaL7cqsydpZLbMGm4fXwcvofrgEIutFEpRtgt\nuh66f27ToB0inwP7GqcMIqywXTYcwvf6GfbBN608sIEus+k/MVLo9isi4FkAD5RR\nqDje624+6I1OacxX6EbgP2vg8ATKx1QdQLkfTyQQw3WIB+Q8fwLM/eFuogllbgnv\n1nDIRFxnMQm544wRiwwhR4YZ2veyKXBCneXksfFjNvkjo4CzuoaJvQGazQzsyVSx\nYdQI0XrhtXEwz5tOraMrG1UfxkCkiA+Wrc+H/TanYEFpPHejJHJtmrZocOR+SYdm\nEEJs/+/JFej11hh0KWzLYBr3aWmxiQswCjIhznEHI8eiNDn4V0jLesHDBPVpDYI6\nJycuer4pWpRPqNctKYC0lZ+794itvIt1gjW4c4eFZvbCKAmMVVRKrffjcYO7AMLq\n8YxDzu+EfLQhXXoaHxTtM/5GyQqcsScIRo35LdkZ9qSmn4HjozqYY9lAoQrvfa1L\n0YBSKv61KMX3mekozkWVNR1Xxv2lC5jN31xqHWCSJ921kYAnysIg3GRrSox65wDn\nRRQJ2vc717qv7TLvrcmC\n=Emdk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7ce30cd23ee253afd2f80ac3022d147e79786014\nparent f02a8b82187e55c821a6e75e612c1f859de24cf8\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1782168402 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782168402 -0700\n\nrelease(langchain-quickjs): 0.3.1 (#4085)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Everything below this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.3.1](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/langchain-quickjs==0.3.0...langchain-quickjs==0.3.1)\n(2026-06-22)\n\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* **quickjs:** persist top-level JS declarations across evals\n([#4147](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4147))\n([7574fea](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7574fea88b51c77f7afa8279c4f561d6ecb47e3f))\n* **quickjs:** ptc tools in tools namespace are rendered without\nprepended `tools.` in system prompt and task as ptc duplicated task\nglobal ([#4075](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4075))\n([014a903](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/014a9033af70b5b8b08ad2eb36f98590f5f1cca8))\n\n---\n\n_Everything above this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-22T22:46:43Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a795988061816179df702b0deed710df996307da","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a795988061816179df702b0deed710df996307da","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a795988061816179df702b0deed710df996307da/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f02a8b82187e55c821a6e75e612c1f859de24cf8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f02a8b82187e55c821a6e75e612c1f859de24cf8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f02a8b82187e55c821a6e75e612c1f859de24cf8"}]},{"sha":"f02a8b82187e55c821a6e75e612c1f859de24cf8","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGYwMmE4YjgyMTg3ZTU1YzgyMWE2ZTc1ZTYxMmMxZjg1OWRlMjRjZjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Hunter Lovell","email":"40191806+hntrl@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-22T22:09:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T22:09:39Z"},"message":"refactor(quickjs): remove deprecated `snapshot_between_turns` flag (#4149)\n\nRemove the deprecated `snapshot_between_turns` compatibility option from\n`CodeInterpreterMiddleware` now that persistence is controlled entirely\nby `mode`.\n\nThis keeps REPL persistence configuration to one public knob and one\ninternal normalized value. `thread` remains the default, `turn` skips\ncross-turn snapshot restore/save, and `call` resets after each eval.\n\nChanges:\n- delete the deprecated constructor parameter and deprecation shim\n- collapse persistence state to the normalized `_mode`\n- update unit tests and QuickJS benchmarks to use `mode` directly","tree":{"sha":"6e0597268260ade011e8f9b5912e9269cc5fb551","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/6e0597268260ade011e8f9b5912e9269cc5fb551"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f02a8b82187e55c821a6e75e612c1f859de24cf8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqObKjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9loQAKU6KAqyDjqPZNLa0F+FyWJd\nW2sOgHu58LUvO5kLwMnd6eSp9mY10v7JOHJ3xJKen6Uh9qoaeQFvgcQMLBdyhc8x\n7qD9Yd0/f0upd+gE9RCu4e1b9oIZOJCBnIT5n7gHLn5KdahPybaYbiyAlCo+MM9J\n7zZ7nUzEiNOcWCCE8qN2hSNaDPyC+A1+3t1Y9rsviS0Z/W2Pwfmhg0icnvXpKluA\n4vqo0XytHe0H5r2QGguUlwgODMcM9yATSYaez3X9aEBbab1FFkJrzNz9v7VdmpUg\nWEgmVBsVPf3ksPc/xUmC1Ap1R1In3d32XndOdXifASj2/xPuKTlUAr/TIi5BGvlS\ng1mUIM9eLnSliJRQ1Y/dh7abxHD+PtBKaJUBLhPu06R2OcqWqM7Ko3fjxbQFFikL\nSTly2ipSzlWcNVfZEP4qLMLRe6jzbIKiZJzXgiKQ82K81DUrBzFlts1//0izMEZx\nLzP/qUctE9y1oeKMC3pbTB47CNMNCOBSHNpqx6thgLhN3jU3fZs5jDHMmeTfpCtz\nsZt8tEIXtosdVoizHy2gcEBkVGpKG9P3hOC++9AX5jubJ6A08gxQXuSYLJuo6IKP\ne4vEpXD9AHH4N36pLTjPVHfznnMCjKK7dY/k9O4f65Y1gl5LQ0KB9KazY3W08CLO\nHajFGqSd0cO5rITXC0vT\n=14bK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6e0597268260ade011e8f9b5912e9269cc5fb551\nparent 156e1185242a19746f8c268904637c73f07b9a10\nauthor Hunter Lovell <40191806+hntrl@users.noreply.github.com> 1782166179 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782166179 -0700\n\nrefactor(quickjs): remove deprecated `snapshot_between_turns` flag (#4149)\n\nRemove the deprecated `snapshot_between_turns` compatibility option from\n`CodeInterpreterMiddleware` now that persistence is controlled entirely\nby `mode`.\n\nThis keeps REPL persistence configuration to one public knob and one\ninternal normalized value. `thread` remains the default, `turn` skips\ncross-turn snapshot restore/save, and `call` resets after each eval.\n\nChanges:\n- delete the deprecated constructor parameter and deprecation shim\n- collapse persistence state to the normalized `_mode`\n- update unit tests and QuickJS benchmarks to use `mode` directly","verified_at":"2026-06-22T22:09:39Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f02a8b82187e55c821a6e75e612c1f859de24cf8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f02a8b82187e55c821a6e75e612c1f859de24cf8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f02a8b82187e55c821a6e75e612c1f859de24cf8/comments","author":{"login":"hntrl","id":40191806,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMTkxODA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40191806?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl","html_url":"https://github.com/hntrl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"156e1185242a19746f8c268904637c73f07b9a10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/156e1185242a19746f8c268904637c73f07b9a10","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/156e1185242a19746f8c268904637c73f07b9a10"}]},{"sha":"156e1185242a19746f8c268904637c73f07b9a10","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDE1NmUxMTg1MjQyYTE5NzQ2ZjhjMjY4OTA0NjM3YzczZjA3YjlhMTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-22T21:34:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T21:34:04Z"},"message":"fix(code): report same-version dependency updates (#4146)\n\nThe installer now distinguishes a true no-op reinstall from a\nsame-version reinstall that still moves transitive packages. When `uv`\nreports dependency changes, the final status and footer say dependencies\nwere updated, and the raw install output is saved so users can inspect\nthe full details after abbreviated terminal output.","tree":{"sha":"3c9c7e9ba06f0085bcad3afe1e91f2ac1a582da5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/3c9c7e9ba06f0085bcad3afe1e91f2ac1a582da5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/156e1185242a19746f8c268904637c73f07b9a10","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOapNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOtAQAIK8QOlSerPAej731zRw/ZxX\nl18R8SsFe8Gb7tDadwQvRmzouRpB60rZHT+5gkZZ8sjAsde5MRzTh5q9ve9OvzA3\nF6fpWdZ6jzsj3JQl+INu9OfhCrV4L7nr30xNvFCHxvC7NkeBJm7ye2BCp7//tMoy\nh2Q2uFOVAYZOMDqVQx7x4Ug0drBAL2kgcd5IfFZV0KVgh3GadAwK1uGjl+yxAF8m\nTFcTeqHhDj+wtVX9Tc01+c9178cedzrqXCrT4mg1bxccCT1oF3Cco3qtnxKJo84t\ngt8AEobtLyvYO1sw8sGmw5wk9zzMA2iUEEKt4EJ/MgG3CBJMZzeGoohQcPPUvg2r\nXPtv9Czy+ondJIP4V8eMxn/GhxKt6uOvhqqRtbwiBlME5i3+8BQT0tofsGdO5sqp\nhavJwtv4ZbVdohbA4EPhz4D3V/D27o6cp5zO8fBMKI8k5XxwyDAHV66pm5XrnIz0\nX9AJVxgrbycfrARnAJGMuCILCUkQ7sNZ2OVw91vIrrxjKodcu2COzeXTYQeA/GqK\nRuDpyTWpJTBDafQjlPxEqw0NRXnNuv24Q98OktTi+hm9L/HyZ6sJJPS7z04VJ7RM\npSDAd9Ua/sbokxMkpXwrfHMrxllCQP4kkWoi9eeWkpF1x0dMoGWfbCe3b3vp/UkU\nXtCDtJTgSxXy7SefpMyI\n=Rn7X\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3c9c7e9ba06f0085bcad3afe1e91f2ac1a582da5\nparent 7574fea88b51c77f7afa8279c4f561d6ecb47e3f\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782164044 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782164044 -0400\n\nfix(code): report same-version dependency updates (#4146)\n\nThe installer now distinguishes a true no-op reinstall from a\nsame-version reinstall that still moves transitive packages. When `uv`\nreports dependency changes, the final status and footer say dependencies\nwere updated, and the raw install output is saved so users can inspect\nthe full details after abbreviated terminal output.","verified_at":"2026-06-22T21:34:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/156e1185242a19746f8c268904637c73f07b9a10","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/156e1185242a19746f8c268904637c73f07b9a10","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/156e1185242a19746f8c268904637c73f07b9a10/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7574fea88b51c77f7afa8279c4f561d6ecb47e3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7574fea88b51c77f7afa8279c4f561d6ecb47e3f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7574fea88b51c77f7afa8279c4f561d6ecb47e3f"}]},{"sha":"7574fea88b51c77f7afa8279c4f561d6ecb47e3f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDc1NzRmZWE4OGI1MWM3N2Y3YWZhODI3OWM0ZjU2MWQ2ZWNiNDdlM2Y","commit":{"author":{"name":"Hunter Lovell","email":"40191806+hntrl@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-22T21:23:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T21:23:01Z"},"message":"fix(quickjs): persist top-level JS declarations across evals (#4147)\n\nUpdates `langchain-quickjs` to require `quickjs-rs` 0.2.3 so the REPL\ncan use the upstream runtime-level source transform for top-level\ndeclarations. The QuickJS runtime now enables\n`SourceTransform.TOP_LEVEL_CONST_TO_VAR`, keeping top-level `const` and\n`let` bindings visible across consecutive eval calls and matching the\npersistence behavior promised to agents.\n\nChanges:\n- Bumps `quickjs-rs` to 0.2.3 in `langchain-quickjs` and refreshes\ndependent lockfiles for the code and evals packages.\n- Configures `_Registry`-owned `Runtime` instances with\n`SourceTransform.TOP_LEVEL_CONST_TO_VAR`.\n- Adds sync and async regression coverage for same-turn eval persistence\nof top-level declarations.","tree":{"sha":"87bfd04b8eeccdf19f647baeed3261808a73a152","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/87bfd04b8eeccdf19f647baeed3261808a73a152"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/7574fea88b51c77f7afa8279c4f561d6ecb47e3f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOae1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARbIQAGP6rzrM8e9lINwB3PBNfehw\nSKXlZwJdAOigQg36B2YIFHxq4pn0b8w5vF0MgiDeN7nF26Fae+GwOEJD3bVo/iYz\nTEVHF2MVHhbohcxSKwjTKon/+bnPeucqVxtpjGlolewYl/3CufQNYdGiC/6yPa0W\nLLyx6ILPi/AW6t8bL7yzfDOwm97714sU+o5O4W9i80yB9q55Tgl3uGOkHRm5ukeN\nyiTRsMhdq1Rok5r7MaxV40L6K8Wxh/NnKqWZCl8E2+B9Pggs29Fa4EcsCbghEUP0\nAKdEHFGWeqVqWokbwOKxAFWEhISGUL2j2VVuDzyLLPQtgdWOqTvXbwXXQco7BCoG\nchs21worI74HArn9ZTBM+wR95a8Zf56XoJC8DJCEHWWS7eUHv/4g7XxJIFDYZmrP\n0hdS5jvTaUjvLmntvmvyF1He/fUffpt4SG813+9aM2Ul/W6AjbLvxnvqk0GcsCJp\nKT9uBez9rEvuMFFSStsXjVDiBnMpzJH95G4EyVr7idchb6W7cOO/gBHvgst1PJ/p\nzS5zQxZsty4Z58VIYjO9v881EUzY4ih7KS3J3cbm0k819Fy6PouEfSAd3Z0iHRDN\nPvY3ycQ5SRx7exJ2+S8PdszPohnH/3t0qC04AqoA28nNK0JralaEWW9wpT9gichp\nNMO2ClhMmJS4OziqpMWw\n=NnMH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 87bfd04b8eeccdf19f647baeed3261808a73a152\nparent 151beaef2e7fac8afda578e4304163ecb9821c0b\nauthor Hunter Lovell <40191806+hntrl@users.noreply.github.com> 1782163381 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782163381 -0700\n\nfix(quickjs): persist top-level JS declarations across evals (#4147)\n\nUpdates `langchain-quickjs` to require `quickjs-rs` 0.2.3 so the REPL\ncan use the upstream runtime-level source transform for top-level\ndeclarations. The QuickJS runtime now enables\n`SourceTransform.TOP_LEVEL_CONST_TO_VAR`, keeping top-level `const` and\n`let` bindings visible across consecutive eval calls and matching the\npersistence behavior promised to agents.\n\nChanges:\n- Bumps `quickjs-rs` to 0.2.3 in `langchain-quickjs` and refreshes\ndependent lockfiles for the code and evals packages.\n- Configures `_Registry`-owned `Runtime` instances with\n`SourceTransform.TOP_LEVEL_CONST_TO_VAR`.\n- Adds sync and async regression coverage for same-turn eval persistence\nof top-level declarations.","verified_at":"2026-06-22T21:23:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7574fea88b51c77f7afa8279c4f561d6ecb47e3f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7574fea88b51c77f7afa8279c4f561d6ecb47e3f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7574fea88b51c77f7afa8279c4f561d6ecb47e3f/comments","author":{"login":"hntrl","id":40191806,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMTkxODA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40191806?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl","html_url":"https://github.com/hntrl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"151beaef2e7fac8afda578e4304163ecb9821c0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/151beaef2e7fac8afda578e4304163ecb9821c0b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/151beaef2e7fac8afda578e4304163ecb9821c0b"}]},{"sha":"151beaef2e7fac8afda578e4304163ecb9821c0b","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDE1MWJlYWVmMmU3ZmFjOGFmZGE1NzhlNDMwNDE2M2VjYjk4MjFjMGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Hunter Lovell","email":"40191806+hntrl@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-22T19:58:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T19:58:50Z"},"message":"refactor(quickjs): delta-encode REPL snapshot as a bsdiff patch chain (#4077)\n\n## Summary\n\n`CodeInterpreterMiddleware` keeps the QuickJS REPL heap alive across\nturns by serializing the **entire** heap into the\n`_quickjs_snapshot_payload` state key on every `after_agent`. Under the\ndefault `LastValue` channel, that full snapshot (~1.4 MB in practice) is\nre-serialized into the checkpoint **blob store** of every subsequent\ncheckpoint version, so checkpoint storage grows linearly with\nconversation length.\n\nEmpirically the QuickJS heap is ~98-100% byte-stable between consecutive\nturns, so a binary diff (`bsdiff4`) between successive snapshots is tiny\n(~200 B-1 KB vs 1.4 MB). This PR moves the snapshot key onto a\n[`DeltaChannel`](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/pregel#deltachannel)\nholding a **patch chain**: each turn writes only the delta from the\nprevious snapshot, and a pure bulk reducer replays the chain back into\nthe full snapshot on reconstruction.\n\n<img width=\"1307\" height=\"441\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-18 at 11 58\n01 AM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4cf2c4b6-6e0e-4312-8e4e-09659b0f6806\"\n/>\n\n## How it works\n\nEach `after_agent` writes one record to the channel:\n\n- `(\"snap\", full_bytes)` — an anchor; emitted on the first turn, when\nthere is no usable prior, or when a patch would not be smaller than\nre-anchoring.\n- `(\"patch\", bsdiff_bytes)` — a delta against the materialized prior\nsnapshot.\n- `(\"clear\", b\"\")` — resets the chain (used when a snapshot is\ndropped/cleared).\n\nThe bulk reducer `_replay_snapshot_chain(base, writes)` folds these\nrecords left-to-right back into the full snapshot bytes. It is **pure\nand associative**, so LangGraph may batch/replay records in any grouping\nand re-run it on every checkpoint load — including time travel across\n`snapshot_frequency` boundaries and forks — without changing the result.\nIt also accepts legacy bare-`bytes` writes (treated as anchors) for\nbackward compatibility.\n\n`after_agent` computes the delta by diffing the new snapshot against the\n**materialized prior snapshot read back from state** (`b\"\"` when none\nexists). This makes snapshotting **stateless** — no in-process cache —\nso it stays correct across forks, restores, and fresh processes.\n`before_agent` reads the already-materialized full bytes (the reducer\ncoalesced the chain), so restore is unchanged.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Add `_replay_snapshot_chain` (bulk reducer) and `_coerce_record`\n(record normalization, incl. tuple/list/bytes/None and legacy forms).\n- Annotate `REPLState._quickjs_snapshot_payload` as `Annotated[bytes,\nDeltaChannel(_replay_snapshot_chain), PrivateStateAttr]`.\n- Rework `_snapshot_update` to emit anchor/patch records, fall back to\nan anchor when a patch is not smaller, and still drop snapshots over\n`max_snapshot_bytes`.\n- `after_agent` / `aafter_agent` diff against the prior snapshot from\nstate.\n- Keep the `if not payload` restore guard in `before_agent` /\n`abefore_agent`.\n- Add `bsdiff4` dependency.\n- Tests: reducer associativity, replay of a patch subset on a\nmaterialized anchor base, anchor/clear resets, record-coercion edge\ncases, anchor-fallback when a patch isn't smaller, plus compiled-graph\nintegration tests asserting zero blob-store growth and correct\nfork/time-travel reconstruction.\n\n## Why the value type is `bytes`, not `bytes | None`\n\n`DeltaChannel` seeds a never-written channel by calling `typ()`, so the\nvalue type must be a zero-arg callable. When a `DeltaChannel` appears\ninside `Annotated[...]`, LangGraph forces `typ` to the bare annotated\ntype (`langgraph.graph.state._is_field_channel`). A `bytes | None` union\nis a `types.UnionType` and is **not callable**, which raises `TypeError:\n'types.UnionType' object is not callable` on reconstruction.\n\nUsing `bytes` gives a valid empty seed (`b\"\"`). Writes are records\n(tuples) or `None` and flow through the reducer. Because the empty seed\nis `b\"\"`, `before_agent` / `abefore_agent` guard with `if not payload`\nso they never call `restore_snapshot(b\"\")` (which fails with \"snapshot\nshorter than header\").","tree":{"sha":"f1397375f7400642b9ce2df164b31d2fa438a63e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/f1397375f7400642b9ce2df164b31d2fa438a63e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/151beaef2e7fac8afda578e4304163ecb9821c0b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOZP6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArWMQAFJ7uDEoZSjpHZb0j7mmGXLt\n0KiSLhAMeY3jbYOAiDONUhwSg++BFfIcHhCbg2wmsmfj/NVuCBOas/iSM1Bu80mQ\nZA55kF3lS8pTzoCU0aFR519NupvT9Tezpj9vRxkd75YByX3luC1quWGXlStukvU1\nEZBqxFIg+Hi+JIbTg1baLueW/1rGSAkMX4WzXJGvqMzi+Y5enjTV52jumQgfY4qy\nxCQdYnT28V/NQkw6UvJZbyjNpXEpoMaL8CMdMmDmemw+YRHZIQyj0+GOX1Zmmwz/\njheKDIxawr453dz3VaorEwUHpKdOUHF1F/ZVL1zr9sYXv6AhGXQUNtYintQOQD/R\nnc/vV5qmQQlVBb1K846UzwkBw24BknhOY+Udb7mIU7XWk2KRLVPQ2SKdCV8zfK92\nr8W/YlOqt6tgePRjwvqZRTClCnVdDzf7Lru/Sv8nI20RNYm2L1AIBokXfcD73zuH\nEzHl/0q9ox7epPPrTnmHKeG7jC8JP/1MNwKh7HVy1E98mi9vCSgvdvtNLsEv8MaN\nUgcrcbF1babdTZvVL8X/FcgT2/DDVwNNNRTXN7dVxCm8CiN0KCFI0zgMH6cQg08Q\n554jgBsFyJzeHmgjecKrcA9XxNzfSv7zvwWDn1ELb63VOu0L4hjriEbFtKEKLJgU\n5xP33EYJawPJhMTJF4SS\n=rGYz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f1397375f7400642b9ce2df164b31d2fa438a63e\nparent 018844d6cafc278f07185b7fafa7ef6ecd48089c\nauthor Hunter Lovell <40191806+hntrl@users.noreply.github.com> 1782158330 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782158330 -0700\n\nrefactor(quickjs): delta-encode REPL snapshot as a bsdiff patch chain (#4077)\n\n## Summary\n\n`CodeInterpreterMiddleware` keeps the QuickJS REPL heap alive across\nturns by serializing the **entire** heap into the\n`_quickjs_snapshot_payload` state key on every `after_agent`. Under the\ndefault `LastValue` channel, that full snapshot (~1.4 MB in practice) is\nre-serialized into the checkpoint **blob store** of every subsequent\ncheckpoint version, so checkpoint storage grows linearly with\nconversation length.\n\nEmpirically the QuickJS heap is ~98-100% byte-stable between consecutive\nturns, so a binary diff (`bsdiff4`) between successive snapshots is tiny\n(~200 B-1 KB vs 1.4 MB). This PR moves the snapshot key onto a\n[`DeltaChannel`](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/pregel#deltachannel)\nholding a **patch chain**: each turn writes only the delta from the\nprevious snapshot, and a pure bulk reducer replays the chain back into\nthe full snapshot on reconstruction.\n\n<img width=\"1307\" height=\"441\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-18 at 11 58\n01 AM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4cf2c4b6-6e0e-4312-8e4e-09659b0f6806\"\n/>\n\n## How it works\n\nEach `after_agent` writes one record to the channel:\n\n- `(\"snap\", full_bytes)` — an anchor; emitted on the first turn, when\nthere is no usable prior, or when a patch would not be smaller than\nre-anchoring.\n- `(\"patch\", bsdiff_bytes)` — a delta against the materialized prior\nsnapshot.\n- `(\"clear\", b\"\")` — resets the chain (used when a snapshot is\ndropped/cleared).\n\nThe bulk reducer `_replay_snapshot_chain(base, writes)` folds these\nrecords left-to-right back into the full snapshot bytes. It is **pure\nand associative**, so LangGraph may batch/replay records in any grouping\nand re-run it on every checkpoint load — including time travel across\n`snapshot_frequency` boundaries and forks — without changing the result.\nIt also accepts legacy bare-`bytes` writes (treated as anchors) for\nbackward compatibility.\n\n`after_agent` computes the delta by diffing the new snapshot against the\n**materialized prior snapshot read back from state** (`b\"\"` when none\nexists). This makes snapshotting **stateless** — no in-process cache —\nso it stays correct across forks, restores, and fresh processes.\n`before_agent` reads the already-materialized full bytes (the reducer\ncoalesced the chain), so restore is unchanged.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Add `_replay_snapshot_chain` (bulk reducer) and `_coerce_record`\n(record normalization, incl. tuple/list/bytes/None and legacy forms).\n- Annotate `REPLState._quickjs_snapshot_payload` as `Annotated[bytes,\nDeltaChannel(_replay_snapshot_chain), PrivateStateAttr]`.\n- Rework `_snapshot_update` to emit anchor/patch records, fall back to\nan anchor when a patch is not smaller, and still drop snapshots over\n`max_snapshot_bytes`.\n- `after_agent` / `aafter_agent` diff against the prior snapshot from\nstate.\n- Keep the `if not payload` restore guard in `before_agent` /\n`abefore_agent`.\n- Add `bsdiff4` dependency.\n- Tests: reducer associativity, replay of a patch subset on a\nmaterialized anchor base, anchor/clear resets, record-coercion edge\ncases, anchor-fallback when a patch isn't smaller, plus compiled-graph\nintegration tests asserting zero blob-store growth and correct\nfork/time-travel reconstruction.\n\n## Why the value type is `bytes`, not `bytes | None`\n\n`DeltaChannel` seeds a never-written channel by calling `typ()`, so the\nvalue type must be a zero-arg callable. When a `DeltaChannel` appears\ninside `Annotated[...]`, LangGraph forces `typ` to the bare annotated\ntype (`langgraph.graph.state._is_field_channel`). A `bytes | None` union\nis a `types.UnionType` and is **not callable**, which raises `TypeError:\n'types.UnionType' object is not callable` on reconstruction.\n\nUsing `bytes` gives a valid empty seed (`b\"\"`). Writes are records\n(tuples) or `None` and flow through the reducer. Because the empty seed\nis `b\"\"`, `before_agent` / `abefore_agent` guard with `if not payload`\nso they never call `restore_snapshot(b\"\")` (which fails with \"snapshot\nshorter than header\").","verified_at":"2026-06-22T19:58:50Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/151beaef2e7fac8afda578e4304163ecb9821c0b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/151beaef2e7fac8afda578e4304163ecb9821c0b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/151beaef2e7fac8afda578e4304163ecb9821c0b/comments","author":{"login":"hntrl","id":40191806,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMTkxODA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40191806?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl","html_url":"https://github.com/hntrl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"018844d6cafc278f07185b7fafa7ef6ecd48089c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/018844d6cafc278f07185b7fafa7ef6ecd48089c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/018844d6cafc278f07185b7fafa7ef6ecd48089c"}]},{"sha":"018844d6cafc278f07185b7fafa7ef6ecd48089c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDAxODg0NGQ2Y2FmYzI3OGYwNzE4NWI3ZmFmYTdlZjZlY2Q0ODA4OWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-22T18:53:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T18:53:02Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump langsmith from 0.8.18 to 0.9.0 in /libs/evals (#4144)\n\nBumps [langsmith](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk) from\n0.8.18 to 0.9.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/releases\">langsmith's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v0.9.0</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>feat(sandbox): send mount_config for mounts by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DanielKneipp\"><code>@​DanielKneipp</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3051\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3051</a></li>\n<li>feat(anonymizer): curated secret-detection preset\n(createSecretAnonymizer) by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/paarth-a\"><code>@​paarth-a</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3059\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3059</a></li>\n<li>chore: sync langsmith_api by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langtions-bot\"><code>@​langtions-bot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3033\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3033</a></li>\n<li>fix(python): allow-list fields accepted from baggage replica updates\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/QuentinBrosse\"><code>@​QuentinBrosse</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3067\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3067</a></li>\n<li>release(py): 0.9.0 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/QuentinBrosse\"><code>@​QuentinBrosse</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3068\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3068</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>New Contributors</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paarth-a\"><code>@​paarth-a</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3059\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3059</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/compare/v0.8.18...v0.9.0\">https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/compare/v0.8.18...v0.9.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/commit/3759b21739e2b80133cd8