/github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/commit/5b2bd8db3c50d3f19e98f41288c87d9c0ac0b136\"><code>5b2bd8d</code></a>\nchore(deps): bump the npm_and_yarn group across 2 directories with 2\nupdates ...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/commit/d8642f9099a48025d00c7283ad3cd2ce56fec775\"><code>d8642f9</code></a>\nchore(deps): bump the npm_and_yarn group across 4 directories with 4\nupdates ...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/commit/953c2e5e25e41ecb4dba428adbac1c446c0a0071\"><code>953c2e5</code></a>\nchore(deps-dev): bump langchain-anthropic from 1.4.4 to 1.4.6 in /python\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/issues/3044\">#3044</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/commit/5513699e2d25c2147e02c296bc3b90f7d0923d8a\"><code>5513699</code></a>\nchore(deps): bump starlette from 1.0.1 to 1.3.1 in /python (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/issues/3039\">#3039</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/commit/8becdefdf422a02e03f78cf3ebb4c62c136b7cf3\"><code>8becdef</code></a>\nchore(deps): bump cryptography from 46.0.7 to 48.0.1 in /python (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/issues/3038\">#3038</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/commit/1a9c522febbf313bbe649ca75c39158fec048934\"><code>1a9c522</code></a>\nchore(deps): bump aiohttp from 3.14.0 to 3.14.1 in /python (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/issues/3037\">#3037</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/compare/v0.8.11...v0.8.18\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `msgpack` from 1.1.2 to 1.2.1\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/releases\">msgpack's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v1.2.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Bump pypa/cibuildwheel from 4.0.0 to 4.1.0 in the all-dependencies\ngroup by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/694\">msgpack/msgpack-python#694</a></li>\n<li>release v1.2.1 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/methane\"><code>@​methane</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/698\">msgpack/msgpack-python#698</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/compare/v1.2.0...v1.2.1\">https://github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/compare/v1.2.0...v1.2.1</a></p>\n<h2>v1.2.0</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>relax setuptools version by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/methane\"><code>@​methane</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/652\">msgpack/msgpack-python#652</a></li>\n<li>update setuptools requirements to &gt;=78.1.1 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/methane\"><code>@​methane</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/653\">msgpack/msgpack-python#653</a></li>\n<li>cython: freethreading_compatible by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/methane\"><code>@​methane</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/654\">msgpack/msgpack-python#654</a></li>\n<li>drop Python 3.9 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/methane\"><code>@​methane</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/656\">msgpack/msgpack-python#656</a></li>\n<li>update cython and cibuildwheel by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/methane\"><code>@​methane</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/658\">msgpack/msgpack-python#658</a></li>\n<li>ci: add riscv64 manylinux/musllinux wheels by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/justeph\"><code>@​justeph</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/664\">msgpack/msgpack-python#664</a></li>\n<li>fix: check <code>unpack_callback_uint32</code> result by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/KowalskiThomas\"><code>@​KowalskiThomas</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/666\">msgpack/msgpack-python#666</a></li>\n<li>fix: re-raise existing exception when available by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/KowalskiThomas\"><code>@​KowalskiThomas</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/667\">msgpack/msgpack-python#667</a></li>\n<li>fix: check return code in <code>unpack_callback_int64</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/KowalskiThomas\"><code>@​KowalskiThomas</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/665\">msgpack/msgpack-python#665</a></li>\n<li>Fixed README example by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/vallsv\"><code>@​vallsv</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/668\">msgpack/msgpack-python#668</a></li>\n<li>Bump the all-dependencies group with 6 updates by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/669\">msgpack/msgpack-python#669</a></li>\n<li>ci: use ubuntu-slim for lint by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/methane\"><code>@​methane</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/670\">msgpack/msgpack-python#670</a></li>\n<li>fix: enforce <code>strict_map_key</code> with\n<code>object_pairs_hook</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/KowalskiThomas\"><code>@​KowalskiThomas</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/673\">msgpack/msgpack-python#673</a></li>\n<li>Raise DEFAULT_RECURSE_LIMIT from 511 to 1024 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Copilot\"><code>@​Copilot</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/676\">msgpack/msgpack-python#676</a></li>\n<li>fix: properly handle return codes in <code>pack_timestamp</code> by\n<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/KowalskiThomas\"><code>@​KowalskiThomas</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/672\">msgpack/msgpack-python#672</a></li>\n<li>fix: avoid memory leak when decoding invalid nested arrays by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/KowalskiThomas\"><code>@​KowalskiThomas</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/671\">msgpack/msgpack-python#671</a></li>\n<li>Add missing autoreset in Packer.pack_ext_type by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/bysiber\"><code>@​bysiber</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/663\">msgpack/msgpack-python#663</a></li>\n<li>Add no-GIL interpreter support by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/clin1234\"><code>@​clin1234</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/641\">msgpack/msgpack-python#641</a></li>\n<li>skip recursion limit test on free-threaded CPython builds by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/methane\"><code>@​methane</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/679\">msgpack/msgpack-python#679</a></li>\n<li>Fix Timestamp.from_datetime returning wrong value for pre-epoch\ndatetimes by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/bysiber\"><code>@​bysiber</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/662\">msgpack/msgpack-python#662</a></li>\n<li>Add 3.15 to CI by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/clin1234\"><code>@​clin1234</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/678\">msgpack/msgpack-python#678</a></li>\n<li>fix: use-after-free in <code>get_data_from_buffer</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/KowalskiThomas\"><code>@​KowalskiThomas</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/677\">msgpack/msgpack-python#677</a></li>\n<li>change changelog format to markdown by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/methane\"><code>@​methane</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/680\">msgpack/msgpack-python#680</a></li>\n<li>Bump the all-dependencies group with 2 updates by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/684\">msgpack/msgpack-python#684</a></li>\n<li>Bump sys.setrecursionlimit within test_nest_limit_1024 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/clin1234\"><code>@​clin1234</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/682\">msgpack/msgpack-python#682</a></li>\n<li>Guard <code>Packer</code> buffer protocol hooks with Cython critical\nsections by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Copilot\"><code>@​Copilot</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/686\">msgpack/msgpack-python#686</a></li>\n<li>Harden <code>Unpacker.__init__</code> re-entry cleanup to prevent\nbuffer/context leaks by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Copilot\"><code>@​Copilot</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/687\">msgpack/msgpack-python#687</a></li>\n<li>release v1.2.0rc1 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/methane\"><code>@​methane</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/681\">msgpack/msgpack-python#681</a></li>\n<li>Wheels CI hangs for MacOS Intel by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/crusaderky\"><code>@​crusaderky</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/689\">msgpack/msgpack-python#689</a></li>\n<li>Bump pypa/cibuildwheel from 3.4.1 to 4.0.0 in the all-dependencies\ngroup by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/691\">msgpack/msgpack-python#691</a></li>\n<li>release v1.2.0 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/methane\"><code>@​methane</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/692\">msgpack/msgpack-python#692</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>New Contributors</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/justeph\"><code>@​justeph</code></a> made\ntheir first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/664\">msgpack/msgpack-python#664</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/KowalskiThomas\"><code>@​KowalskiThomas</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/666\">msgpack/msgpack-python#666</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/vallsv\"><code>@​vallsv</code></a> made\ntheir first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/668\">msgpack/msgpack-python#668</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a>[bot]\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/669\">msgpack/msgpack-python#669</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/Copilot\"><code>@​Copilot</code></a> made\ntheir first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/676\">msgpack/msgpack-python#676</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/bysiber\"><code>@​bysiber</code></a> made\ntheir first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/663\">msgpack/msgpack-python#663</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/clin1234\"><code>@​clin1234</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/pull/641\">msgpack/msgpack-python#641</a></li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">msgpack's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>1.2.1</h1>\n<p>Release Date: 2026-06-19</p>\n<p>Fix a segfault when calling <code>Unpacker.unpack()</code> or\n<code>Unpacker.skip()</code> after an unpacking failure.\nBut note that reusing the same <code>Unpacker</code> instance after an\nunpacking failure is not supported.\nPlease create a new <code>Unpacker</code> instance instead.\nGHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964</p>\n<h1>1.2.0</h1>\n<p>Release Date: 2026-06-11</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Support free threaded Python. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/issues/654\">#654</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/issues/686\">#686</a></li>\n<li>Dropped support for Python 3.9. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/issues/656\">#656</a></li>\n<li>Fix missing error checks in C code. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/issues/665\">#665</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/issues/666\">#666</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/issues/667\">#667</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/issues/672\">#672</a></li>\n<li>Fix <code>strict_map_key</code> option didn't work for\n<code>object_pairs_hook</code>. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/issues/673\">#673</a></li>\n<li>Increase DEFAULT_RECURSE_LIMIT of Unpacker to 1024. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/issues/676\">#676</a></li>\n<li>Fix memory leak when Unpacker returns error for invalid input. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/issues/671\">#671</a></li>\n<li>Fix <code>Packer.pack_ext_type()</code> ignored\n<code>autoreset</code> option. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/issues/663\">#663</a></li>\n<li>Fix <code>Timestamp.from_datetime()</code> returning wrong value for\npre-epoch datetimes. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/issues/662\">#662</a></li>\n<li>Fix use-after-free in <code>unpackb()</code> and\n<code>Unpacker.unpack()</code> for non-contiguous input. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/issues/677\">#677</a></li>\n<li>Fix possible memory leak when calling\n<code>Unpacker.__init__()</code> several times. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/issues/687\">#687</a></li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/commit/448d43f5dcca7b3a2b0810e161af0a6431d90071\"><code>448d43f</code></a>\nrelease v1.2.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/issues/698\">#698</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/commit/2c56ddb5d0025ed481d962c0f5d62d19dec7476d\"><code>2c56ddb</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/commit/0f4f350b6f3e80f24750422673424cce5d96e15d\"><code>0f4f350</code></a>\nBump pypa/cibuildwheel from 4.0.0 to 4.1.0 in the all-dependencies group\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/issues/694\">#694</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/commit/11ed0a5110c1920b85b7d24d9414f480983e0f16\"><code>11ed0a5</code></a>\nrelease v1.2.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/issues/692\">#692</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/commit/c410a388c58d55091736e510cad064977a12cb8b\"><code>c410a38</code></a>\nBump pypa/cibuildwheel from 3.4.1 to 4.0.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/issues/691\">#691</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/commit/97ba6ca0d29c1e8a5b30112f13f37a4d6b3c4492\"><code>97ba6ca</code></a>\nskip ci: remove unneeded CIBW_SKIP option</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/commit/cdde1b0d6336caff4e82310c3c7d2b4c73f22d59\"><code>cdde1b0</code></a>\nWheels CI hangs for MacOS Intel (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/issues/689\">#689</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/commit/5eb57e15455f5dd25001e97a7ef1170911dee104\"><code>5eb57e1</code></a>\nrelease v1.2.0rc1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/issues/681\">#681</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/commit/77395c19a50061238306df5ea10e67c5312ceff0\"><code>77395c1</code></a>\nHarden <code>Unpacker.__init__</code> re-entry cleanup to prevent\nbuffer/context leaks (...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/commit/7df7136e20933fd3a498bd58bff7975a24790516\"><code>7df7136</code></a>\nGuard <code>Packer</code> buffer protocol hooks with Cython critical\nsections (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/issues/686\">#686</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/compare/v1.1.2...v1.2.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `pydantic-settings` from 2.14.1 to 2.14.2\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/releases\">pydantic-settings's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v2.14.2</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<p>This is a security patch release.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Prevent <code>NestedSecretsSettingsSource</code> from following\nsymlinks outside <code>secrets_dir</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hramezani\"><code>@​hramezani</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/889\">pydantic/pydantic-settings#889</a></li>\n<li>Prepare release 2.14.2 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hramezani\"><code>@​hramezani</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/890\">pydantic/pydantic-settings#890</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Security</h3>\n<p>Fixes <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/security/advisories/GHSA-4xgf-cpjx-pc3j\">GHSA-4xgf-cpjx-pc3j</a>:\n<code>NestedSecretsSettingsSource</code> with\n<code>secrets_nested_subdir=True</code> could follow a symbolic link\ninside <code>secrets_dir</code> pointing outside it, reading out-of-tree\nfiles into settings values and bypassing the\n<code>secrets_dir_max_size</code> cap. Affected versions: <code>&gt;=\n2.12.0, &lt; 2.14.2</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/compare/v2.14.1...v2.14.2\">https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/compare/v2.14.1...v2.14.2</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/commit/d703bd717e5e07439fa89da2245eee6139413e9e\"><code>d703bd7</code></a>\nPrepare release 2.14.2 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/issues/890\">#890</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/compare/v2.14.1...v2.14.2\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> major version` will close this\ngroup update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific\ndependency's major version (unless you unignore this specific\ndependency's major version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> minor version` will close this\ngroup update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific\ndependency's minor version (unless you unignore this specific\ndependency's minor version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name>` will close this group update PR\nand stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific dependency\n(unless you unignore this specific dependency or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name>` will remove all of the ignore\nconditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name> <ignore condition>` will\nremove the ignore condition of the specified dependency and ignore\nconditions\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-22T18:32:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9f222a1981ceeafc0b6f99633b2f9c95ffa0268b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9f222a1981ceeafc0b6f99633b2f9c95ffa0268b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9f222a1981ceeafc0b6f99633b2f9c95ffa0268b/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8605560f45a33f3bd25cffc529ca3854d4f15fef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8605560f45a33f3bd25cffc529ca3854d4f15fef","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8605560f45a33f3bd25cffc529ca3854d4f15fef"}]},{"sha":"8605560f45a33f3bd25cffc529ca3854d4f15fef","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDg2MDU1NjBmNDVhMzNmM2JkMjVjZmZjNTI5Y2EzODU0ZDRmMTVmZWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-22T18:31:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T18:31:58Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump vcrpy from 8.1.1 to 8.2.1 in /libs/partners/vercel (#4113)\n\nBumps [vcrpy](https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy) from 8.1.1 to 8.2.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/releases\">vcrpy's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v8.2.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SECURITY:</strong> Cassettes are now loaded with a safe YAML\nloader, preventing arbitrary code execution when a cassette from an\nuntrusted source is loaded. Previously a crafted cassette containing a\nPython object tag (e.g. <code>!!python/object/apply:os.system</code>)\nwould execute code on load, including via the normal\n<code>vcr.use_cassette()</code> path. Existing cassettes (including\nfile-upload/streaming bodies) continue to load. Advisory:\nGHSA-rpj2-4hq8-938g — thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/RamiAltai\"><code>@​RamiAltai</code></a> and <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/EQSTLab\"><code>@​EQSTLab</code></a> for the\nreports.</li>\n<li>Validate <code>record_mode</code> and raise a clear error on an\ninvalid value (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/208\">#208</a>)</li>\n<li>Recommend pytest-recording over the unmaintained pytest-vcr in the\ndocs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/986\">#986</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.2.0...v8.2.1\">https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.2.0...v8.2.1</a></p>\n<h2>v8.2.0</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Add support for httpx 2.x (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/993\">#993</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Patch httpx transports instead of httpcore (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/972\">#972</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix aiohttp 3.14 compatibility: <code>AsyncStreamReaderMixin</code>\nremoved and <code>ClientResponse</code> now requires\n<code>stream_writer</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/995\">#995</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Account for modified requests when storing played cassettes, so\n<code>drop_unused_requests</code> honours\n<code>before_record_request</code> filtering (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/962\">#962</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jamesbraza\"><code>@​jamesbraza</code></a></li>\n<li>Make the request URL available on <code>VCRHTTPResponse</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/976\">#976</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dAnjou\"><code>@​dAnjou</code></a></li>\n<li>Improve error message when a matching request has already been\nconsumed (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/985\">#985</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix body check in <code>convert_body_to_unicode</code> to use an\nexplicit type check (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/982\">#982</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Add env proxy cassette regression test (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/994\">#994</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tine1117\"><code>@​tine1117</code></a></li>\n<li>Remove milestone references from docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/984\">#984</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump sphinx-rtd-theme from 3.0.2 to 3.1.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/973\">#973</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.1.1...v8.2.0\">https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.1.1...v8.2.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/blob/master/docs/changelog.rst\">vcrpy's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Changelog</h2>\n<p>All help in providing PRs to close out bug issues is appreciated.\nEven if that is providing a repo that fully replicates issues. We have\nvery generous contributors that have added these to bug issues which\nmeant another contributor picked up the bug and closed it out.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>8.2.1</p>\n<ul>\n<li>SECURITY: Load cassettes with a safe YAML loader, preventing\narbitrary code execution when a cassette from an untrusted source is\nloaded (GHSA-rpj2-4hq8-938g) - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/RamiAltai\"><code>@​RamiAltai</code></a> and <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/EQSTLab\"><code>@​EQSTLab</code></a></li>\n<li>Validate <code>record_mode</code> and raise a clear error on an\ninvalid value (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/208\">#208</a>)</li>\n<li>Recommend pytest-recording over the unmaintained pytest-vcr in the\ndocs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/986\">#986</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.2.0</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Add support for httpx 2.x (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/993\">#993</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Patch httpx transports instead of httpcore (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/972\">#972</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix aiohttp 3.14 compatibility: <code>AsyncStreamReaderMixin</code>\nremoved and <code>ClientResponse</code> now requires\n<code>stream_writer</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/995\">#995</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Account for modified requests when storing played cassettes, so\n<code>drop_unused_requests</code> honours\n<code>before_record_request</code> filtering (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/962\">#962</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jamesbraza\"><code>@​jamesbraza</code></a></li>\n<li>Make the request URL available on <code>VCRHTTPResponse</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/976\">#976</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dAnjou\"><code>@​dAnjou</code></a></li>\n<li>Improve error message when a matching request has already been\nconsumed (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/985\">#985</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix body check in <code>convert_body_to_unicode</code> to use an\nexplicit type check (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/982\">#982</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Add env proxy cassette regression test (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/994\">#994</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tine1117\"><code>@​tine1117</code></a></li>\n<li>Remove milestone references from docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/984\">#984</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump sphinx-rtd-theme from 3.0.2 to 3.1.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/973\">#973</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.1.1</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix sync requests in async contexts for HTTPX (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/965\">#965</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump peter-evans/create-pull-request from 7 to 8 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/969\">#969</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.1.0</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Enable brotli decompression if available (via <code>brotli</code>,\n<code>brotlipy</code> or <code>brotlicffi</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/620\">#620</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/immerrr\"><code>@​immerrr</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix aiohttp allowing both <code>data</code> and <code>json</code>\narguments when one is None (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/624\">#624</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/leorochael\"><code>@​leorochael</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix usage of io-like interface with VCR.py (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/906\">#906</a>)\n- thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/tito\"><code>@​tito</code></a> and\n<a href=\"https://github.com/kevdevg\"><code>@​kevdevg</code></a></li>\n<li>Migrate to declarative Python package config (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/767\">#767</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/deronnax\"><code>@​deronnax</code></a></li>\n<li>Various linting fixes - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump actions/checkout from 5 to 6 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/955\">#955</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.0.0</p>\n<ul>\n<li>BREAKING: Drop support for Python 3.9 (major version bump) - thanks\n<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>BREAKING: Drop support for urllib3 &lt; 2 - fixes CVE warnings from\nurllib3 1.x (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/926\">#926</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/880\">#880</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>New feature: <code>drop_unused_requests</code> option to remove\nunused interactions from cassettes (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/763\">#763</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/danielnsilva\"><code>@​danielnsilva</code></a></li>\n<li>Rewrite httpx support to patch httpcore instead of httpx (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/943\">#943</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a>\n<ul>\n<li>Fixes <code>httpx.ResponseNotRead</code> exceptions (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/832\">#832</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/834\">#834</a>)</li>\n<li>Fixes <code>KeyError: 'follow_redirects'</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/945\">#945</a>)</li>\n<li>Adds support for custom httpx transports</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Fix HTTPS proxy handling - proxy address no longer ends up in\ncassette URIs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/809\">#809</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/914\">#914</a>)\n- thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/alga\"><code>@​alga</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix <code>iscoroutinefunction</code> deprecation warning on Python\n3.14 - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kloczek\"><code>@​kloczek</code></a></li>\n<li>Only log message if response is appended - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/talfus-laddus\"><code>@​talfus-laddus</code></a></li>\n<li>Optimize urllib.parse calls - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Martin-Brunthaler\"><code>@​Martin-Brunthaler</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix CI for Ubuntu 24.04 - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hartwork\"><code>@​hartwork</code></a></li>\n<li>Various CI improvements: migrate to uv, update GitHub Actions -\nthanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>Various linting and test improvements - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a>\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hartwork\"><code>@​hartwork</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/85312039e9ade8f1290f7e556b18d2889cf9f6e0\"><code>8531203</code></a>\nRelease v8.2.1</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/045acb1b5f8940f82adbb3faafd13e43e46289d6\"><code>045acb1</code></a>\nUse a safe YAML loader for cassettes to prevent code execution</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/de43f46247e763c2e36dc8dd9c36173be3069f81\"><code>de43f46</code></a>\nFix lint failures from merged PRs (codespell + ruff UP032)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/514c374796ba8b53402d3cad86682a7d3f0c34cc\"><code>514c374</code></a>\nValidate record_mode and raise a clear error on invalid values</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/b736cadd58d3f4088c0e440a1196e4b14d369dd2\"><code>b736cad</code></a>\ndocs: recommend pytest-recording over unmaintained pytest-vcr</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/06758c9879f18a46b24b450591a295ae9443d097\"><code>06758c9</code></a>\nRelease v8.2.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/6554837e023f97aee5edcc7cd8359408686cca98\"><code>6554837</code></a>\nAdd env proxy cassette regression test (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/994\">#994</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/62cf5e127201c050b6b8f8c8a20910eb7eab753a\"><code>62cf5e1</code></a>\nAccounting for modified requests when storing played cassettes, with a\ntest (...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/13f201a820b71288829df9470d629bfd0b4183de\"><code>13f201a</code></a>\nmake url available in VCRHTTPResponse (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/976\">#976</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/d57b55339e1bd386fed791621bb0094de2a8a4b2\"><code>d57b553</code></a>\nimprove error message on repeated requestt (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/985\">#985</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.1.1...v8.2.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=vcrpy&package-manager=uv&previous-version=8.1.1&new-version=8.2.1)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"48fdcba48095b7bfb78306594950f6bbcb3db866","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/48fdcba48095b7bfb78306594950f6bbcb3db866"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/8605560f45a33f3bd25cffc529ca3854d4f15fef","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOX+eCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAk/4QAGCHhWOAu2xBhe/EEUgad4/t\nVHvlXyLow0btViKuKjj2JaTQkC6mJmUpiOKwObIs9vcQaisVQdiE2Cpk7aaoWWTx\nW/eNUldL/2VmIQxUUlalr5rQVROROk7EfYoM6DW0UkB95sllVjHKm7PgR3yZcHBd\nZXCe7fJbU8w66uBI+CK2CCkKfiQp7v+hRxfnSy0rLa0VdqzjkxecFJBTGw02yNnB\nonrUhpEzluW/8mCaZkNobpnXm1e87uvFDJ+KBmp3A2jkIFA/4Q33rrSo0CEROuqv\nUdK/alGuOT1TajaE/r6CCq4pfvp1dyQ+v27+LaQOlNNxJB8y33k37AP1S+37DaAn\nUpzhCuNGbQ2ZjnzNFSOwWiwiwnkYdIz0CtbVGLEhFjsGDYUk2S2B3KT/EYjLePXR\nctvpyuK0RjowoHjBCXrtfn2i8Zs27Ac/m9IIyBv+/pM/sJvi4ITpQxTOUtWvoQTC\nm7/vbNg42t7q/ZvsNPVfO9HTlytOVSjYtCAKntH1T9cWjAa9wqMqidpcyU+65s4y\nj0mnXJB9RbCFCqOB6L25sjt7kNSOkqpewWpWRumFOyIFY5F7+df4LpnrlHa+eqF8\nI+HTE6UE+7Ab5JprwKX+6Qa+1kUiHSnesECdL7js5AMPPCEfo/BbbHQOfCuZ55Ym\n752MdD7/hbpMuSHD/Nb8\n=0oft\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 48fdcba48095b7bfb78306594950f6bbcb3db866\nparent 9ecefa468e093998e883d076b88c5930599a69af\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1782153118 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782153118 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump vcrpy from 8.1.1 to 8.2.1 in /libs/partners/vercel (#4113)\n\nBumps [vcrpy](https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy) from 8.1.1 to 8.2.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/releases\">vcrpy's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v8.2.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SECURITY:</strong> Cassettes are now loaded with a safe YAML\nloader, preventing arbitrary code execution when a cassette from an\nuntrusted source is loaded. Previously a crafted cassette containing a\nPython object tag (e.g. <code>!!python/object/apply:os.system</code>)\nwould execute code on load, including via the normal\n<code>vcr.use_cassette()</code> path. Existing cassettes (including\nfile-upload/streaming bodies) continue to load. Advisory:\nGHSA-rpj2-4hq8-938g — thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/RamiAltai\"><code>@​RamiAltai</code></a> and <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/EQSTLab\"><code>@​EQSTLab</code></a> for the\nreports.</li>\n<li>Validate <code>record_mode</code> and raise a clear error on an\ninvalid value (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/208\">#208</a>)</li>\n<li>Recommend pytest-recording over the unmaintained pytest-vcr in the\ndocs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/986\">#986</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.2.0...v8.2.1\">https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.2.0...v8.2.1</a></p>\n<h2>v8.2.0</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Add support for httpx 2.x (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/993\">#993</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Patch httpx transports instead of httpcore (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/972\">#972</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix aiohttp 3.14 compatibility: <code>AsyncStreamReaderMixin</code>\nremoved and <code>ClientResponse</code> now requires\n<code>stream_writer</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/995\">#995</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Account for modified requests when storing played cassettes, so\n<code>drop_unused_requests</code> honours\n<code>before_record_request</code> filtering (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/962\">#962</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jamesbraza\"><code>@​jamesbraza</code></a></li>\n<li>Make the request URL available on <code>VCRHTTPResponse</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/976\">#976</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dAnjou\"><code>@​dAnjou</code></a></li>\n<li>Improve error message when a matching request has already been\nconsumed (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/985\">#985</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix body check in <code>convert_body_to_unicode</code> to use an\nexplicit type check (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/982\">#982</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Add env proxy cassette regression test (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/994\">#994</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tine1117\"><code>@​tine1117</code></a></li>\n<li>Remove milestone references from docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/984\">#984</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump sphinx-rtd-theme from 3.0.2 to 3.1.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/973\">#973</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.1.1...v8.2.0\">https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.1.1...v8.2.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/blob/master/docs/changelog.rst\">vcrpy's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Changelog</h2>\n<p>All help in providing PRs to close out bug issues is appreciated.\nEven if that is providing a repo that fully replicates issues. We have\nvery generous contributors that have added these to bug issues which\nmeant another contributor picked up the bug and closed it out.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>8.2.1</p>\n<ul>\n<li>SECURITY: Load cassettes with a safe YAML loader, preventing\narbitrary code execution when a cassette from an untrusted source is\nloaded (GHSA-rpj2-4hq8-938g) - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/RamiAltai\"><code>@​RamiAltai</code></a> and <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/EQSTLab\"><code>@​EQSTLab</code></a></li>\n<li>Validate <code>record_mode</code> and raise a clear error on an\ninvalid value (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/208\">#208</a>)</li>\n<li>Recommend pytest-recording over the unmaintained pytest-vcr in the\ndocs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/986\">#986</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.2.0</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Add support for httpx 2.x (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/993\">#993</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Patch httpx transports instead of httpcore (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/972\">#972</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix aiohttp 3.14 compatibility: <code>AsyncStreamReaderMixin</code>\nremoved and <code>ClientResponse</code> now requires\n<code>stream_writer</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/995\">#995</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Account for modified requests when storing played cassettes, so\n<code>drop_unused_requests</code> honours\n<code>before_record_request</code> filtering (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/962\">#962</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jamesbraza\"><code>@​jamesbraza</code></a></li>\n<li>Make the request URL available on <code>VCRHTTPResponse</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/976\">#976</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dAnjou\"><code>@​dAnjou</code></a></li>\n<li>Improve error message when a matching request has already been\nconsumed (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/985\">#985</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix body check in <code>convert_body_to_unicode</code> to use an\nexplicit type check (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/982\">#982</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Add env proxy cassette regression test (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/994\">#994</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tine1117\"><code>@​tine1117</code></a></li>\n<li>Remove milestone references from docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/984\">#984</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump sphinx-rtd-theme from 3.0.2 to 3.1.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/973\">#973</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.1.1</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix sync requests in async contexts for HTTPX (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/965\">#965</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump peter-evans/create-pull-request from 7 to 8 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/969\">#969</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.1.0</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Enable brotli decompression if available (via <code>brotli</code>,\n<code>brotlipy</code> or <code>brotlicffi</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/620\">#620</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/immerrr\"><code>@​immerrr</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix aiohttp allowing both <code>data</code> and <code>json</code>\narguments when one is None (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/624\">#624</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/leorochael\"><code>@​leorochael</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix usage of io-like interface with VCR.py (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/906\">#906</a>)\n- thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/tito\"><code>@​tito</code></a> and\n<a href=\"https://github.com/kevdevg\"><code>@​kevdevg</code></a></li>\n<li>Migrate to declarative Python package config (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/767\">#767</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/deronnax\"><code>@​deronnax</code></a></li>\n<li>Various linting fixes - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump actions/checkout from 5 to 6 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/955\">#955</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.0.0</p>\n<ul>\n<li>BREAKING: Drop support for Python 3.9 (major version bump) - thanks\n<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>BREAKING: Drop support for urllib3 &lt; 2 - fixes CVE warnings from\nurllib3 1.x (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/926\">#926</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/880\">#880</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>New feature: <code>drop_unused_requests</code> option to remove\nunused interactions from cassettes (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/763\">#763</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/danielnsilva\"><code>@​danielnsilva</code></a></li>\n<li>Rewrite httpx support to patch httpcore instead of httpx (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/943\">#943</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a>\n<ul>\n<li>Fixes <code>httpx.ResponseNotRead</code> exceptions (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/832\">#832</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/834\">#834</a>)</li>\n<li>Fixes <code>KeyError: 'follow_redirects'</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/945\">#945</a>)</li>\n<li>Adds support for custom httpx transports</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Fix HTTPS proxy handling - proxy address no longer ends up in\ncassette URIs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/809\">#809</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/914\">#914</a>)\n- thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/alga\"><code>@​alga</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix <code>iscoroutinefunction</code> deprecation warning on Python\n3.14 - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kloczek\"><code>@​kloczek</code></a></li>\n<li>Only log message if response is appended - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/talfus-laddus\"><code>@​talfus-laddus</code></a></li>\n<li>Optimize urllib.parse calls - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Martin-Brunthaler\"><code>@​Martin-Brunthaler</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix CI for Ubuntu 24.04 - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hartwork\"><code>@​hartwork</code></a></li>\n<li>Various CI improvements: migrate to uv, update GitHub Actions -\nthanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>Various linting and test improvements - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a>\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hartwork\"><code>@​hartwork</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/85312039e9ade8f1290f7e556b18d2889cf9f6e0\"><code>8531203</code></a>\nRelease v8.2.1</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/045acb1b5f8940f82adbb3faafd13e43e46289d6\"><code>045acb1</code></a>\nUse a safe YAML loader for cassettes to prevent code execution</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/de43f46247e763c2e36dc8dd9c36173be3069f81\"><code>de43f46</code></a>\nFix lint failures from merged PRs (codespell + ruff UP032)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/514c374796ba8b53402d3cad86682a7d3f0c34cc\"><code>514c374</code></a>\nValidate record_mode and raise a clear error on invalid values</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/b736cadd58d3f4088c0e440a1196e4b14d369dd2\"><code>b736cad</code></a>\ndocs: recommend pytest-recording over unmaintained pytest-vcr</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/06758c9879f18a46b24b450591a295ae9443d097\"><code>06758c9</code></a>\nRelease v8.2.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/6554837e023f97aee5edcc7cd8359408686cca98\"><code>6554837</code></a>\nAdd env proxy cassette regression test (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/994\">#994</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/62cf5e127201c050b6b8f8c8a20910eb7eab753a\"><code>62cf5e1</code></a>\nAccounting for modified requests when storing played cassettes, with a\ntest (...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/13f201a820b71288829df9470d629bfd0b4183de\"><code>13f201a</code></a>\nmake url available in VCRHTTPResponse (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/976\">#976</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/d57b55339e1bd386fed791621bb0094de2a8a4b2\"><code>d57b553</code></a>\nimprove error message on repeated requestt (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/985\">#985</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.1.1...v8.2.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=vcrpy&package-manager=uv&previous-version=8.1.1&new-version=8.2.1)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-22T18:31:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8605560f45a33f3bd25cffc529ca3854d4f15fef","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8605560f45a33f3bd25cffc529ca3854d4f15fef","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8605560f45a33f3bd25cffc529ca3854d4f15fef/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9ecefa468e093998e883d076b88c5930599a69af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9ecefa468e093998e883d076b88c5930599a69af","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9ecefa468e093998e883d076b88c5930599a69af"}]},{"sha":"9ecefa468e093998e883d076b88c5930599a69af","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDllY2VmYTQ2OGUwOTM5OThlODgzZDA3NmI4OGM1OTMwNTk5YTY5YWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-22T18:31:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T18:31:54Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump vcrpy from 8.1.1 to 8.2.1 in /libs/partners/runloop (#4114)\n\nBumps [vcrpy](https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy) from 8.1.1 to 8.2.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/releases\">vcrpy's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v8.2.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SECURITY:</strong> Cassettes are now loaded with a safe YAML\nloader, preventing arbitrary code execution when a cassette from an\nuntrusted source is loaded. Previously a crafted cassette containing a\nPython object tag (e.g. <code>!!python/object/apply:os.system</code>)\nwould execute code on load, including via the normal\n<code>vcr.use_cassette()</code> path. Existing cassettes (including\nfile-upload/streaming bodies) continue to load. Advisory:\nGHSA-rpj2-4hq8-938g — thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/RamiAltai\"><code>@​RamiAltai</code></a> and <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/EQSTLab\"><code>@​EQSTLab</code></a> for the\nreports.</li>\n<li>Validate <code>record_mode</code> and raise a clear error on an\ninvalid value (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/208\">#208</a>)</li>\n<li>Recommend pytest-recording over the unmaintained pytest-vcr in the\ndocs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/986\">#986</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.2.0...v8.2.1\">https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.2.0...v8.2.1</a></p>\n<h2>v8.2.0</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Add support for httpx 2.x (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/993\">#993</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Patch httpx transports instead of httpcore (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/972\">#972</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix aiohttp 3.14 compatibility: <code>AsyncStreamReaderMixin</code>\nremoved and <code>ClientResponse</code> now requires\n<code>stream_writer</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/995\">#995</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Account for modified requests when storing played cassettes, so\n<code>drop_unused_requests</code> honours\n<code>before_record_request</code> filtering (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/962\">#962</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jamesbraza\"><code>@​jamesbraza</code></a></li>\n<li>Make the request URL available on <code>VCRHTTPResponse</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/976\">#976</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dAnjou\"><code>@​dAnjou</code></a></li>\n<li>Improve error message when a matching request has already been\nconsumed (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/985\">#985</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix body check in <code>convert_body_to_unicode</code> to use an\nexplicit type check (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/982\">#982</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Add env proxy cassette regression test (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/994\">#994</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tine1117\"><code>@​tine1117</code></a></li>\n<li>Remove milestone references from docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/984\">#984</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump sphinx-rtd-theme from 3.0.2 to 3.1.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/973\">#973</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.1.1...v8.2.0\">https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.1.1...v8.2.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/blob/master/docs/changelog.rst\">vcrpy's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Changelog</h2>\n<p>All help in providing PRs to close out bug issues is appreciated.\nEven if that is providing a repo that fully replicates issues. We have\nvery generous contributors that have added these to bug issues which\nmeant another contributor picked up the bug and closed it out.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>8.2.1</p>\n<ul>\n<li>SECURITY: Load cassettes with a safe YAML loader, preventing\narbitrary code execution when a cassette from an untrusted source is\nloaded (GHSA-rpj2-4hq8-938g) - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/RamiAltai\"><code>@​RamiAltai</code></a> and <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/EQSTLab\"><code>@​EQSTLab</code></a></li>\n<li>Validate <code>record_mode</code> and raise a clear error on an\ninvalid value (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/208\">#208</a>)</li>\n<li>Recommend pytest-recording over the unmaintained pytest-vcr in the\ndocs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/986\">#986</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.2.0</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Add support for httpx 2.x (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/993\">#993</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Patch httpx transports instead of httpcore (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/972\">#972</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix aiohttp 3.14 compatibility: <code>AsyncStreamReaderMixin</code>\nremoved and <code>ClientResponse</code> now requires\n<code>stream_writer</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/995\">#995</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Account for modified requests when storing played cassettes, so\n<code>drop_unused_requests</code> honours\n<code>before_record_request</code> filtering (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/962\">#962</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jamesbraza\"><code>@​jamesbraza</code></a></li>\n<li>Make the request URL available on <code>VCRHTTPResponse</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/976\">#976</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dAnjou\"><code>@​dAnjou</code></a></li>\n<li>Improve error message when a matching request has already been\nconsumed (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/985\">#985</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix body check in <code>convert_body_to_unicode</code> to use an\nexplicit type check (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/982\">#982</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Add env proxy cassette regression test (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/994\">#994</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tine1117\"><code>@​tine1117</code></a></li>\n<li>Remove milestone references from docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/984\">#984</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump sphinx-rtd-theme from 3.0.2 to 3.1.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/973\">#973</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.1.1</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix sync requests in async contexts for HTTPX (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/965\">#965</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump peter-evans/create-pull-request from 7 to 8 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/969\">#969</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.1.0</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Enable brotli decompression if available (via <code>brotli</code>,\n<code>brotlipy</code> or <code>brotlicffi</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/620\">#620</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/immerrr\"><code>@​immerrr</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix aiohttp allowing both <code>data</code> and <code>json</code>\narguments when one is None (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/624\">#624</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/leorochael\"><code>@​leorochael</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix usage of io-like interface with VCR.py (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/906\">#906</a>)\n- thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/tito\"><code>@​tito</code></a> and\n<a href=\"https://github.com/kevdevg\"><code>@​kevdevg</code></a></li>\n<li>Migrate to declarative Python package config (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/767\">#767</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/deronnax\"><code>@​deronnax</code></a></li>\n<li>Various linting fixes - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump actions/checkout from 5 to 6 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/955\">#955</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.0.0</p>\n<ul>\n<li>BREAKING: Drop support for Python 3.9 (major version bump) - thanks\n<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>BREAKING: Drop support for urllib3 &lt; 2 - fixes CVE warnings from\nurllib3 1.x (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/926\">#926</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/880\">#880</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>New feature: <code>drop_unused_requests</code> option to remove\nunused interactions from cassettes (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/763\">#763</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/danielnsilva\"><code>@​danielnsilva</code></a></li>\n<li>Rewrite httpx support to patch httpcore instead of httpx (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/943\">#943</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a>\n<ul>\n<li>Fixes <code>httpx.ResponseNotRead</code> exceptions (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/832\">#832</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/834\">#834</a>)</li>\n<li>Fixes <code>KeyError: 'follow_redirects'</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/945\">#945</a>)</li>\n<li>Adds support for custom httpx transports</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Fix HTTPS proxy handling - proxy address no longer ends up in\ncassette URIs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/809\">#809</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/914\">#914</a>)\n- thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/alga\"><code>@​alga</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix <code>iscoroutinefunction</code> deprecation warning on Python\n3.14 - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kloczek\"><code>@​kloczek</code></a></li>\n<li>Only log message if response is appended - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/talfus-laddus\"><code>@​talfus-laddus</code></a></li>\n<li>Optimize urllib.parse calls - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Martin-Brunthaler\"><code>@​Martin-Brunthaler</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix CI for Ubuntu 24.04 - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hartwork\"><code>@​hartwork</code></a></li>\n<li>Various CI improvements: migrate to uv, update GitHub Actions -\nthanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>Various linting and test improvements - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a>\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hartwork\"><code>@​hartwork</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/85312039e9ade8f1290f7e556b18d2889cf9f6e0\"><code>8531203</code></a>\nRelease v8.2.1</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/045acb1b5f8940f82adbb3faafd13e43e46289d6\"><code>045acb1</code></a>\nUse a safe YAML loader for cassettes to prevent code execution</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/de43f46247e763c2e36dc8dd9c36173be3069f81\"><code>de43f46</code></a>\nFix lint failures from merged PRs (codespell + ruff UP032)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/514c374796ba8b53402d3cad86682a7d3f0c34cc\"><code>514c374</code></a>\nValidate record_mode and raise a clear error on invalid values</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/b736cadd58d3f4088c0e440a1196e4b14d369dd2\"><code>b736cad</code></a>\ndocs: recommend pytest-recording over unmaintained pytest-vcr</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/06758c9879f18a46b24b450591a295ae9443d097\"><code>06758c9</code></a>\nRelease v8.2.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/6554837e023f97aee5edcc7cd8359408686cca98\"><code>6554837</code></a>\nAdd env proxy cassette regression test (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/994\">#994</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/62cf5e127201c050b6b8f8c8a20910eb7eab753a\"><code>62cf5e1</code></a>\nAccounting for modified requests when storing played cassettes, with a\ntest (...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/13f201a820b71288829df9470d629bfd0b4183de\"><code>13f201a</code></a>\nmake url available in VCRHTTPResponse (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/976\">#976</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/d57b55339e1bd386fed791621bb0094de2a8a4b2\"><code>d57b553</code></a>\nimprove error message on repeated requestt (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/985\">#985</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.1.1...v8.2.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=vcrpy&package-manager=uv&previous-version=8.1.1&new-version=8.2.1)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"500e32ef680794700c7ba6d903b9ce64c91c1fb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/500e32ef680794700c7ba6d903b9ce64c91c1fb7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/9ecefa468e093998e883d076b88c5930599a69af","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOX+aCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZGwQAKrJhRvWbZJgOtY3UjR1oVn8\nlbiH40eAR/Nk+gbNfQcxkNR5/MbIZemNg75VHSHn9BD2UqqxYuQvqFNBfWj5dT0I\nok2ZEdq4o45WTKmsbnrd4asNTjxJw2xjyYwODO6xl3EZP3JeIdNcOCy/4m4nD5Jx\nwq/OcE/6nnXRCcXXvuxoBahZ65CzAtZPondk+hGJPaukc04pqWy1q+lqVwRC/11Y\nJTD4TQeDJ99ZKFSxe+zIRDoKb0VxcskXHczbhPaxKSQdqU11Ma9+A7xkrcpB2lSR\nYms2LmRz3GGdkXGjZpu3XYqD+j++cLCh2BTTitLPjsB8ZpkPXH/wvMr2m5XE3+mX\n8nF5JpFnNzvVMbpcP8CxmAV3rOM3fUVWw+FP7XRYUFCCSboyLXjz1a7KgJo7qz9L\n2WedcRLamlS77N6V4fUdCh6Uf4UPQZB2qCLe87IF0GRNkUwK9z0kywpsDdGqijT/\n8vVubjkLM3jYseqm/HgZAFLlK3cmanZ8Vw9fHdL2jh1wlYPKIK/6oNG0TmQ7C07q\nUuY9rZ7BN33V3wUGval3iLiVLM9rur9Ec764wTkKc5Zj/OlwSbGy5lsq6OWY0hAY\ntdT9pIwW5t6cwNTrCMvPlSjKNqBgu4uFGUlUE0sKaMZ78wi21ThQ0wMjHXQWuUj0\nkWZmsinfbJJUrbKfcCtY\n=rPIx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 500e32ef680794700c7ba6d903b9ce64c91c1fb7\nparent dd3886979cff5f3732ae7e891c380938094cbb18\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1782153114 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782153114 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump vcrpy from 8.1.1 to 8.2.1 in /libs/partners/runloop (#4114)\n\nBumps [vcrpy](https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy) from 8.1.1 to 8.2.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/releases\">vcrpy's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v8.2.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SECURITY:</strong> Cassettes are now loaded with a safe YAML\nloader, preventing arbitrary code execution when a cassette from an\nuntrusted source is loaded. Previously a crafted cassette containing a\nPython object tag (e.g. <code>!!python/object/apply:os.system</code>)\nwould execute code on load, including via the normal\n<code>vcr.use_cassette()</code> path. Existing cassettes (including\nfile-upload/streaming bodies) continue to load. Advisory:\nGHSA-rpj2-4hq8-938g — thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/RamiAltai\"><code>@​RamiAltai</code></a> and <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/EQSTLab\"><code>@​EQSTLab</code></a> for the\nreports.</li>\n<li>Validate <code>record_mode</code> and raise a clear error on an\ninvalid value (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/208\">#208</a>)</li>\n<li>Recommend pytest-recording over the unmaintained pytest-vcr in the\ndocs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/986\">#986</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.2.0...v8.2.1\">https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.2.0...v8.2.1</a></p>\n<h2>v8.2.0</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Add support for httpx 2.x (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/993\">#993</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Patch httpx transports instead of httpcore (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/972\">#972</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix aiohttp 3.14 compatibility: <code>AsyncStreamReaderMixin</code>\nremoved and <code>ClientResponse</code> now requires\n<code>stream_writer</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/995\">#995</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Account for modified requests when storing played cassettes, so\n<code>drop_unused_requests</code> honours\n<code>before_record_request</code> filtering (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/962\">#962</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jamesbraza\"><code>@​jamesbraza</code></a></li>\n<li>Make the request URL available on <code>VCRHTTPResponse</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/976\">#976</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dAnjou\"><code>@​dAnjou</code></a></li>\n<li>Improve error message when a matching request has already been\nconsumed (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/985\">#985</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix body check in <code>convert_body_to_unicode</code> to use an\nexplicit type check (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/982\">#982</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Add env proxy cassette regression test (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/994\">#994</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tine1117\"><code>@​tine1117</code></a></li>\n<li>Remove milestone references from docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/984\">#984</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump sphinx-rtd-theme from 3.0.2 to 3.1.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/973\">#973</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.1.1...v8.2.0\">https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.1.1...v8.2.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/blob/master/docs/changelog.rst\">vcrpy's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Changelog</h2>\n<p>All help in providing PRs to close out bug issues is appreciated.\nEven if that is providing a repo that fully replicates issues. We have\nvery generous contributors that have added these to bug issues which\nmeant another contributor picked up the bug and closed it out.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>8.2.1</p>\n<ul>\n<li>SECURITY: Load cassettes with a safe YAML loader, preventing\narbitrary code execution when a cassette from an untrusted source is\nloaded (GHSA-rpj2-4hq8-938g) - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/RamiAltai\"><code>@​RamiAltai</code></a> and <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/EQSTLab\"><code>@​EQSTLab</code></a></li>\n<li>Validate <code>record_mode</code> and raise a clear error on an\ninvalid value (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/208\">#208</a>)</li>\n<li>Recommend pytest-recording over the unmaintained pytest-vcr in the\ndocs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/986\">#986</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.2.0</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Add support for httpx 2.x (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/993\">#993</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Patch httpx transports instead of httpcore (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/972\">#972</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix aiohttp 3.14 compatibility: <code>AsyncStreamReaderMixin</code>\nremoved and <code>ClientResponse</code> now requires\n<code>stream_writer</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/995\">#995</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Account for modified requests when storing played cassettes, so\n<code>drop_unused_requests</code> honours\n<code>before_record_request</code> filtering (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/962\">#962</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jamesbraza\"><code>@​jamesbraza</code></a></li>\n<li>Make the request URL available on <code>VCRHTTPResponse</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/976\">#976</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dAnjou\"><code>@​dAnjou</code></a></li>\n<li>Improve error message when a matching request has already been\nconsumed (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/985\">#985</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix body check in <code>convert_body_to_unicode</code> to use an\nexplicit type check (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/982\">#982</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Add env proxy cassette regression test (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/994\">#994</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tine1117\"><code>@​tine1117</code></a></li>\n<li>Remove milestone references from docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/984\">#984</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump sphinx-rtd-theme from 3.0.2 to 3.1.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/973\">#973</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.1.1</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix sync requests in async contexts for HTTPX (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/965\">#965</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump peter-evans/create-pull-request from 7 to 8 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/969\">#969</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.1.0</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Enable brotli decompression if available (via <code>brotli</code>,\n<code>brotlipy</code> or <code>brotlicffi</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/620\">#620</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/immerrr\"><code>@​immerrr</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix aiohttp allowing both <code>data</code> and <code>json</code>\narguments when one is None (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/624\">#624</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/leorochael\"><code>@​leorochael</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix usage of io-like interface with VCR.py (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/906\">#906</a>)\n- thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/tito\"><code>@​tito</code></a> and\n<a href=\"https://github.com/kevdevg\"><code>@​kevdevg</code></a></li>\n<li>Migrate to declarative Python package config (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/767\">#767</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/deronnax\"><code>@​deronnax</code></a></li>\n<li>Various linting fixes - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump actions/checkout from 5 to 6 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/955\">#955</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.0.0</p>\n<ul>\n<li>BREAKING: Drop support for Python 3.9 (major version bump) - thanks\n<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>BREAKING: Drop support for urllib3 &lt; 2 - fixes CVE warnings from\nurllib3 1.x (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/926\">#926</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/880\">#880</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>New feature: <code>drop_unused_requests</code> option to remove\nunused interactions from cassettes (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/763\">#763</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/danielnsilva\"><code>@​danielnsilva</code></a></li>\n<li>Rewrite httpx support to patch httpcore instead of httpx (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/943\">#943</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a>\n<ul>\n<li>Fixes <code>httpx.ResponseNotRead</code> exceptions (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/832\">#832</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/834\">#834</a>)</li>\n<li>Fixes <code>KeyError: 'follow_redirects'</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/945\">#945</a>)</li>\n<li>Adds support for custom httpx transports</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Fix HTTPS proxy handling - proxy address no longer ends up in\ncassette URIs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/809\">#809</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/914\">#914</a>)\n- thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/alga\"><code>@​alga</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix <code>iscoroutinefunction</code> deprecation warning on Python\n3.14 - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kloczek\"><code>@​kloczek</code></a></li>\n<li>Only log message if response is appended - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/talfus-laddus\"><code>@​talfus-laddus</code></a></li>\n<li>Optimize urllib.parse calls - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Martin-Brunthaler\"><code>@​Martin-Brunthaler</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix CI for Ubuntu 24.04 - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hartwork\"><code>@​hartwork</code></a></li>\n<li>Various CI improvements: migrate to uv, update GitHub Actions -\nthanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>Various linting and test improvements - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a>\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hartwork\"><code>@​hartwork</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/85312039e9ade8f1290f7e556b18d2889cf9f6e0\"><code>8531203</code></a>\nRelease v8.2.1</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/045acb1b5f8940f82adbb3faafd13e43e46289d6\"><code>045acb1</code></a>\nUse a safe YAML loader for cassettes to prevent code execution</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/de43f46247e763c2e36dc8dd9c36173be3069f81\"><code>de43f46</code></a>\nFix lint failures from merged PRs (codespell + ruff UP032)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/514c374796ba8b53402d3cad86682a7d3f0c34cc\"><code>514c374</code></a>\nValidate record_mode and raise a clear error on invalid values</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/b736cadd58d3f4088c0e440a1196e4b14d369dd2\"><code>b736cad</code></a>\ndocs: recommend pytest-recording over unmaintained pytest-vcr</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/06758c9879f18a46b24b450591a295ae9443d097\"><code>06758c9</code></a>\nRelease v8.2.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/6554837e023f97aee5edcc7cd8359408686cca98\"><code>6554837</code></a>\nAdd env proxy cassette regression test (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/994\">#994</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/62cf5e127201c050b6b8f8c8a20910eb7eab753a\"><code>62cf5e1</code></a>\nAccounting for modified requests when storing played cassettes, with a\ntest (...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/13f201a820b71288829df9470d629bfd0b4183de\"><code>13f201a</code></a>\nmake url available in VCRHTTPResponse (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/976\">#976</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/d57b55339e1bd386fed791621bb0094de2a8a4b2\"><code>d57b553</code></a>\nimprove error message on repeated requestt (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/985\">#985</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.1.1...v8.2.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=vcrpy&package-manager=uv&previous-version=8.1.1&new-version=8.2.1)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-22T18:31:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9ecefa468e093998e883d076b88c5930599a69af","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9ecefa468e093998e883d076b88c5930599a69af","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9ecefa468e093998e883d076b88c5930599a69af/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"dd3886979cff5f3732ae7e891c380938094cbb18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/dd3886979cff5f3732ae7e891c380938094cbb18","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/dd3886979cff5f3732ae7e891c380938094cbb18"}]},{"sha":"dd3886979cff5f3732ae7e891c380938094cbb18","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGRkMzg4Njk3OWNmZjVmMzczMmFlN2U4OTFjMzgwOTM4MDk0Y2JiMTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-22T18:31:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T18:31:49Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump langsmith from 0.8.11 to 0.8.18 in /libs/partners/runloop (#4115)\n\nBumps [langsmith](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk) from\n0.8.11 to 0.8.18.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/releases\">langsmith's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v0.8.18</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>chore(deps-dev): bump vitest from 3.2.4 to 3.2.6 in /js by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3002\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3002</a></li>\n<li>chore(deps): bump pyjwt from 2.12.1 to 2.13.0 in /python by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3030\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3030</a></li>\n<li>chore(deps): bump python-multipart from 0.0.27 to 0.0.31 in /python\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3036\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3036</a></li>\n<li>chore(deps): bump aiohttp from 3.14.0 to 3.14.1 in /python by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3037\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3037</a></li>\n<li>chore(deps): bump cryptography from 46.0.7 to 48.0.1 in /python by\n<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3038\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3038</a></li>\n<li>chore(deps): bump starlette from 1.0.1 to 1.3.1 in /python by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3039\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3039</a></li>\n<li>chore(deps-dev): bump langchain-anthropic from 1.4.4 to 1.4.6 in\n/python by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3044\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3044</a></li>\n<li>chore(deps): bump the npm_and_yarn group across 4 directories with 4\nupdates by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3046\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3046</a></li>\n<li>chore(deps): bump the npm_and_yarn group across 2 directories with 2\nupdates by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3060\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3060</a></li>\n<li>test(python): fix integration assertions for updated attachment\nerror message by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/QuentinBrosse\"><code>@​QuentinBrosse</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3061\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3061</a></li>\n<li>chore: reconcile bumpversion config and mandate release process for\nagents by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/QuentinBrosse\"><code>@​QuentinBrosse</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3062\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3062</a></li>\n<li>release(py): 0.8.18 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/QuentinBrosse\"><code>@​QuentinBrosse</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3063\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3063</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/compare/v0.8.17...v0.8.18\">https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/compare/v0.8.17...v0.8.18</a></p>\n<h2>v0.8.17</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>feat: expose the resources from the generated openap