ct.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3048\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3048</a></li>\n<li>Add sandbox Git mount SDK helpers by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DanielKneipp\"><code>@​DanielKneipp</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3040\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3040</a></li>\n<li>fix: use insights tab in sdk report links [closes LSO-2936] by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/eric-langchain\"><code>@​eric-langchain</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3050\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3050</a></li>\n<li>feat(client): warn when backend version is below minimum required by\n<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/KiewanVillatel\"><code>@​KiewanVillatel</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3041\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3041</a></li>\n<li>chore: bump _MIN_BACKEND_VERSION to 0.16.5rc1 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langtions-bot\"><code>@​langtions-bot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3053\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3053</a></li>\n<li>fix(sandbox): use built-in gcp auth host matching by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DanielKneipp\"><code>@​DanielKneipp</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3055\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3055</a></li>\n<li>chore(python): py to 0.8.17 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sineha-mani\"><code>@​sineha-mani</code></a> in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3056\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3056</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>New Contributors</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sineha-mani\"><code>@​sineha-mani</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3018\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3018</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/eric-langchain\"><code>@​eric-langchain</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3050\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3050</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/compare/v0.8.16...v0.8.17\">https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/compare/v0.8.16...v0.8.17</a></p>\n<h2>v0.8.16</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>feat(py): add sync/async conversion for Sandbox and SandboxClient\n[INF-0000] by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ramon-langchain\"><code>@​ramon-langchain</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3019\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3019</a></li>\n<li>fix(experiments): extract keys from wrapped evaluator function by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/shamikkarkhanis\"><code>@​shamikkarkhanis</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3014\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3014</a></li>\n<li>chore: repoint <a\nhref=\"mailto:support@langchain.dev\">support@langchain.dev</a> mentions\nto the Support Portal by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lutan-langchain\"><code>@​lutan-langchain</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3024\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3024</a></li>\n<li>fix(python): derive create_child run id from start_time [LSDK-220]\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/harisaiharish\"><code>@​harisaiharish</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3027\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3027</a></li>\n<li>chore: sync langsmith_api by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langtions-bot\"><code>@​langtions-bot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3020\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3020</a></li>\n<li>chore: js to 0.7.8 and py to 0.8.16 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/shamikkarkhanis\"><code>@​shamikkarkhanis</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3029\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3029</a></li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/commit/31c2bf650b84a44577d8b4443298fb7e78025b8f\"><code>31c2bf6</code></a>\nrelease(py): 0.8.18 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/issues/3063\">#3063</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/commit/8955b688689fdf47871d44013787410a42ea13fd\"><code>8955b68</code></a>\nchore: reconcile bumpversion config and mandate release process for\nagents (#...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/commit/411401f6ca5ff401c29772ed097c9c9ed97f994c\"><code>411401f</code></a>\ntest(python): fix integration assertions for updated attachment error\nmessage...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/commit/9c5515620f9bfa2145fc65d6f4353c4c8a3e96b6\"><code>9c55156</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/commit/5b2bd8db3c50d3f19e98f41288c87d9c0ac0b136\"><code>5b2bd8d</code></a>\nchore(deps): bump the npm_and_yarn group across 2 directories with 2\nupdates ...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/commit/d8642f9099a48025d00c7283ad3cd2ce56fec775\"><code>d8642f9</code></a>\nchore(deps): bump the npm_and_yarn group across 4 directories with 4\nupdates ...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/commit/953c2e5e25e41ecb4dba428adbac1c446c0a0071\"><code>953c2e5</code></a>\nchore(deps-dev): bump langchain-anthropic from 1.4.4 to 1.4.6 in /python\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/issues/3044\">#3044</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/commit/5513699e2d25c2147e02c296bc3b90f7d0923d8a\"><code>5513699</code></a>\nchore(deps): bump starlette from 1.0.1 to 1.3.1 in /python (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/issues/3039\">#3039</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/commit/8becdefdf422a02e03f78cf3ebb4c62c136b7cf3\"><code>8becdef</code></a>\nchore(deps): bump cryptography from 46.0.7 to 48.0.1 in /python (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/issues/3038\">#3038</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/commit/1a9c522febbf313bbe649ca75c39158fec048934\"><code>1a9c522</code></a>\nchore(deps): bump aiohttp from 3.14.0 to 3.14.1 in /python (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/issues/3037\">#3037</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/compare/v0.8.11...v0.8.18\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-22T18:31:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/91b77e1bf61cd4ef9cca0f1fc6adeb10acbd337a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/91b77e1bf61cd4ef9cca0f1fc6adeb10acbd337a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/91b77e1bf61cd4ef9cca0f1fc6adeb10acbd337a/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ce36f6536c04e3e94ef463a3fb0f120645663ce6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ce36f6536c04e3e94ef463a3fb0f120645663ce6","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ce36f6536c04e3e94ef463a3fb0f120645663ce6"}]},{"sha":"ce36f6536c04e3e94ef463a3fb0f120645663ce6","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGNlMzZmNjUzNmMwNGUzZTk0ZWY0NjNhM2ZiMGYxMjA2NDU2NjNjZTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-22T18:31:25Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T18:31:25Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump vcrpy from 8.1.1 to 8.2.1 in /libs/partners/daytona (#4120)\n\nBumps [vcrpy](https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy) from 8.1.1 to 8.2.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/releases\">vcrpy's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v8.2.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SECURITY:</strong> Cassettes are now loaded with a safe YAML\nloader, preventing arbitrary code execution when a cassette from an\nuntrusted source is loaded. Previously a crafted cassette containing a\nPython object tag (e.g. <code>!!python/object/apply:os.system</code>)\nwould execute code on load, including via the normal\n<code>vcr.use_cassette()</code> path. Existing cassettes (including\nfile-upload/streaming bodies) continue to load. Advisory:\nGHSA-rpj2-4hq8-938g — thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/RamiAltai\"><code>@​RamiAltai</code></a> and <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/EQSTLab\"><code>@​EQSTLab</code></a> for the\nreports.</li>\n<li>Validate <code>record_mode</code> and raise a clear error on an\ninvalid value (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/208\">#208</a>)</li>\n<li>Recommend pytest-recording over the unmaintained pytest-vcr in the\ndocs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/986\">#986</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.2.0...v8.2.1\">https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.2.0...v8.2.1</a></p>\n<h2>v8.2.0</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Add support for httpx 2.x (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/993\">#993</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Patch httpx transports instead of httpcore (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/972\">#972</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix aiohttp 3.14 compatibility: <code>AsyncStreamReaderMixin</code>\nremoved and <code>ClientResponse</code> now requires\n<code>stream_writer</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/995\">#995</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Account for modified requests when storing played cassettes, so\n<code>drop_unused_requests</code> honours\n<code>before_record_request</code> filtering (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/962\">#962</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jamesbraza\"><code>@​jamesbraza</code></a></li>\n<li>Make the request URL available on <code>VCRHTTPResponse</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/976\">#976</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dAnjou\"><code>@​dAnjou</code></a></li>\n<li>Improve error message when a matching request has already been\nconsumed (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/985\">#985</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix body check in <code>convert_body_to_unicode</code> to use an\nexplicit type check (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/982\">#982</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Add env proxy cassette regression test (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/994\">#994</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tine1117\"><code>@​tine1117</code></a></li>\n<li>Remove milestone references from docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/984\">#984</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump sphinx-rtd-theme from 3.0.2 to 3.1.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/973\">#973</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.1.1...v8.2.0\">https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.1.1...v8.2.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/blob/master/docs/changelog.rst\">vcrpy's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Changelog</h2>\n<p>All help in providing PRs to close out bug issues is appreciated.\nEven if that is providing a repo that fully replicates issues. We have\nvery generous contributors that have added these to bug issues which\nmeant another contributor picked up the bug and closed it out.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>8.2.1</p>\n<ul>\n<li>SECURITY: Load cassettes with a safe YAML loader, preventing\narbitrary code execution when a cassette from an untrusted source is\nloaded (GHSA-rpj2-4hq8-938g) - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/RamiAltai\"><code>@​RamiAltai</code></a> and <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/EQSTLab\"><code>@​EQSTLab</code></a></li>\n<li>Validate <code>record_mode</code> and raise a clear error on an\ninvalid value (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/208\">#208</a>)</li>\n<li>Recommend pytest-recording over the unmaintained pytest-vcr in the\ndocs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/986\">#986</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.2.0</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Add support for httpx 2.x (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/993\">#993</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Patch httpx transports instead of httpcore (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/972\">#972</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix aiohttp 3.14 compatibility: <code>AsyncStreamReaderMixin</code>\nremoved and <code>ClientResponse</code> now requires\n<code>stream_writer</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/995\">#995</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Account for modified requests when storing played cassettes, so\n<code>drop_unused_requests</code> honours\n<code>before_record_request</code> filtering (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/962\">#962</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jamesbraza\"><code>@​jamesbraza</code></a></li>\n<li>Make the request URL available on <code>VCRHTTPResponse</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/976\">#976</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dAnjou\"><code>@​dAnjou</code></a></li>\n<li>Improve error message when a matching request has already been\nconsumed (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/985\">#985</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix body check in <code>convert_body_to_unicode</code> to use an\nexplicit type check (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/982\">#982</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Add env proxy cassette regression test (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/994\">#994</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tine1117\"><code>@​tine1117</code></a></li>\n<li>Remove milestone references from docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/984\">#984</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump sphinx-rtd-theme from 3.0.2 to 3.1.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/973\">#973</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.1.1</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix sync requests in async contexts for HTTPX (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/965\">#965</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump peter-evans/create-pull-request from 7 to 8 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/969\">#969</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.1.0</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Enable brotli decompression if available (via <code>brotli</code>,\n<code>brotlipy</code> or <code>brotlicffi</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/620\">#620</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/immerrr\"><code>@​immerrr</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix aiohttp allowing both <code>data</code> and <code>json</code>\narguments when one is None (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/624\">#624</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/leorochael\"><code>@​leorochael</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix usage of io-like interface with VCR.py (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/906\">#906</a>)\n- thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/tito\"><code>@​tito</code></a> and\n<a href=\"https://github.com/kevdevg\"><code>@​kevdevg</code></a></li>\n<li>Migrate to declarative Python package config (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/767\">#767</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/deronnax\"><code>@​deronnax</code></a></li>\n<li>Various linting fixes - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump actions/checkout from 5 to 6 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/955\">#955</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.0.0</p>\n<ul>\n<li>BREAKING: Drop support for Python 3.9 (major version bump) - thanks\n<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>BREAKING: Drop support for urllib3 &lt; 2 - fixes CVE warnings from\nurllib3 1.x (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/926\">#926</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/880\">#880</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>New feature: <code>drop_unused_requests</code> option to remove\nunused interactions from cassettes (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/763\">#763</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/danielnsilva\"><code>@​danielnsilva</code></a></li>\n<li>Rewrite httpx support to patch httpcore instead of httpx (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/943\">#943</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a>\n<ul>\n<li>Fixes <code>httpx.ResponseNotRead</code> exceptions (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/832\">#832</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/834\">#834</a>)</li>\n<li>Fixes <code>KeyError: 'follow_redirects'</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/945\">#945</a>)</li>\n<li>Adds support for custom httpx transports</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Fix HTTPS proxy handling - proxy address no longer ends up in\ncassette URIs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/809\">#809</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/914\">#914</a>)\n- thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/alga\"><code>@​alga</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix <code>iscoroutinefunction</code> deprecation warning on Python\n3.14 - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kloczek\"><code>@​kloczek</code></a></li>\n<li>Only log message if response is appended - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/talfus-laddus\"><code>@​talfus-laddus</code></a></li>\n<li>Optimize urllib.parse calls - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Martin-Brunthaler\"><code>@​Martin-Brunthaler</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix CI for Ubuntu 24.04 - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hartwork\"><code>@​hartwork</code></a></li>\n<li>Various CI improvements: migrate to uv, update GitHub Actions -\nthanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>Various linting and test improvements - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a>\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hartwork\"><code>@​hartwork</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/85312039e9ade8f1290f7e556b18d2889cf9f6e0\"><code>8531203</code></a>\nRelease v8.2.1</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/045acb1b5f8940f82adbb3faafd13e43e46289d6\"><code>045acb1</code></a>\nUse a safe YAML loader for cassettes to prevent code execution</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/de43f46247e763c2e36dc8dd9c36173be3069f81\"><code>de43f46</code></a>\nFix lint failures from merged PRs (codespell + ruff UP032)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/514c374796ba8b53402d3cad86682a7d3f0c34cc\"><code>514c374</code></a>\nValidate record_mode and raise a clear error on invalid values</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/b736cadd58d3f4088c0e440a1196e4b14d369dd2\"><code>b736cad</code></a>\ndocs: recommend pytest-recording over unmaintained pytest-vcr</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/06758c9879f18a46b24b450591a295ae9443d097\"><code>06758c9</code></a>\nRelease v8.2.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/6554837e023f97aee5edcc7cd8359408686cca98\"><code>6554837</code></a>\nAdd env proxy cassette regression test (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/994\">#994</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/62cf5e127201c050b6b8f8c8a20910eb7eab753a\"><code>62cf5e1</code></a>\nAccounting for modified requests when storing played cassettes, with a\ntest (...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/13f201a820b71288829df9470d629bfd0b4183de\"><code>13f201a</code></a>\nmake url available in VCRHTTPResponse (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/976\">#976</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/d57b55339e1bd386fed791621bb0094de2a8a4b2\"><code>d57b553</code></a>\nimprove error message on repeated requestt (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/985\">#985</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.1.1...v8.2.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=vcrpy&package-manager=uv&previous-version=8.1.1&new-version=8.2.1)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"81584eb8696b519b14eaf5ab0570650ba4e1efae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/81584eb8696b519b14eaf5ab0570650ba4e1efae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/ce36f6536c04e3e94ef463a3fb0f120645663ce6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOX9+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAChcQAD7e3Lza5CVViJ0XWru4Nc4o\n/S9BOXLucEsllNAkUPl4g5Zgj9fdLzZy8mU79Wx3adaBE6nuUu1scSpxvTrfkAXS\nrtiye05QLdjcaO1U0P10VejzXOsCoNcptG97JwCRK3mvsS05Px+E/V8NtPHb+XNM\nnGsyOKGqgWJKIxUi+IeTrVi4qQKCUFwmhFLL7GePK7LZC4sl+/LUy+o0gAkoXlzf\nLbWI1IS4s7ybxDGuLSjOpSdrtBNAUjoGW/X/jZctl/1Wntz98eyaJCBvV0mNL07z\ny88rZB8+v+5M09QvZ3Ix3wCVaL8KcAYkiEZTsQTBRHYxk+M82AgZDBMBLVrUVcVu\noJxfvVniz0N0+IDxT72ZQpPdo3rF6pXGDtkVBlSG3RBfYOXJnaNBV3ASbm/5C0wx\nmRArFueX6XnQQz44guv3xDEgsmwdHtde0CxmuGH8un2yU1ZZ8A3LXzt8utPA0CGf\nebc0x92zvnrmUeir88oE2cuMG08JfGX4ML84NkegAw/vGYQnVpBr6AjJKemkfS7Z\nlLgEMMk0wgJ2pvBvmZb55WB2k1K618x8q4GJ75C7Y3Q2YkSGjMjaDm3rAhc3kl+c\njs23DtLPIFVICPtalGZX9NIOdeodnNofCswCxGb/AwnV4+BQVwcJb/+nethknbfO\ne2J1Zj+90AsDyT+Yuz9r\n=pZlJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 81584eb8696b519b14eaf5ab0570650ba4e1efae\nparent 37d5e8cafa2435159c6281c3ddaa3e4dc9a2a507\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1782153085 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782153085 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump vcrpy from 8.1.1 to 8.2.1 in /libs/partners/daytona (#4120)\n\nBumps [vcrpy](https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy) from 8.1.1 to 8.2.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/releases\">vcrpy's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v8.2.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SECURITY:</strong> Cassettes are now loaded with a safe YAML\nloader, preventing arbitrary code execution when a cassette from an\nuntrusted source is loaded. Previously a crafted cassette containing a\nPython object tag (e.g. <code>!!python/object/apply:os.system</code>)\nwould execute code on load, including via the normal\n<code>vcr.use_cassette()</code> path. Existing cassettes (including\nfile-upload/streaming bodies) continue to load. Advisory:\nGHSA-rpj2-4hq8-938g — thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/RamiAltai\"><code>@​RamiAltai</code></a> and <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/EQSTLab\"><code>@​EQSTLab</code></a> for the\nreports.</li>\n<li>Validate <code>record_mode</code> and raise a clear error on an\ninvalid value (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/208\">#208</a>)</li>\n<li>Recommend pytest-recording over the unmaintained pytest-vcr in the\ndocs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/986\">#986</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.2.0...v8.2.1\">https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.2.0...v8.2.1</a></p>\n<h2>v8.2.0</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Add support for httpx 2.x (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/993\">#993</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Patch httpx transports instead of httpcore (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/972\">#972</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix aiohttp 3.14 compatibility: <code>AsyncStreamReaderMixin</code>\nremoved and <code>ClientResponse</code> now requires\n<code>stream_writer</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/995\">#995</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Account for modified requests when storing played cassettes, so\n<code>drop_unused_requests</code> honours\n<code>before_record_request</code> filtering (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/962\">#962</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jamesbraza\"><code>@​jamesbraza</code></a></li>\n<li>Make the request URL available on <code>VCRHTTPResponse</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/976\">#976</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dAnjou\"><code>@​dAnjou</code></a></li>\n<li>Improve error message when a matching request has already been\nconsumed (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/985\">#985</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix body check in <code>convert_body_to_unicode</code> to use an\nexplicit type check (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/982\">#982</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Add env proxy cassette regression test (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/994\">#994</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tine1117\"><code>@​tine1117</code></a></li>\n<li>Remove milestone references from docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/984\">#984</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump sphinx-rtd-theme from 3.0.2 to 3.1.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/973\">#973</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.1.1...v8.2.0\">https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.1.1...v8.2.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/blob/master/docs/changelog.rst\">vcrpy's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Changelog</h2>\n<p>All help in providing PRs to close out bug issues is appreciated.\nEven if that is providing a repo that fully replicates issues. We have\nvery generous contributors that have added these to bug issues which\nmeant another contributor picked up the bug and closed it out.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>8.2.1</p>\n<ul>\n<li>SECURITY: Load cassettes with a safe YAML loader, preventing\narbitrary code execution when a cassette from an untrusted source is\nloaded (GHSA-rpj2-4hq8-938g) - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/RamiAltai\"><code>@​RamiAltai</code></a> and <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/EQSTLab\"><code>@​EQSTLab</code></a></li>\n<li>Validate <code>record_mode</code> and raise a clear error on an\ninvalid value (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/208\">#208</a>)</li>\n<li>Recommend pytest-recording over the unmaintained pytest-vcr in the\ndocs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/986\">#986</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.2.0</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Add support for httpx 2.x (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/993\">#993</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Patch httpx transports instead of httpcore (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/972\">#972</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix aiohttp 3.14 compatibility: <code>AsyncStreamReaderMixin</code>\nremoved and <code>ClientResponse</code> now requires\n<code>stream_writer</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/995\">#995</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Account for modified requests when storing played cassettes, so\n<code>drop_unused_requests</code> honours\n<code>before_record_request</code> filtering (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/962\">#962</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jamesbraza\"><code>@​jamesbraza</code></a></li>\n<li>Make the request URL available on <code>VCRHTTPResponse</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/976\">#976</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dAnjou\"><code>@​dAnjou</code></a></li>\n<li>Improve error message when a matching request has already been\nconsumed (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/985\">#985</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix body check in <code>convert_body_to_unicode</code> to use an\nexplicit type check (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/982\">#982</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Add env proxy cassette regression test (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/994\">#994</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tine1117\"><code>@​tine1117</code></a></li>\n<li>Remove milestone references from docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/984\">#984</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump sphinx-rtd-theme from 3.0.2 to 3.1.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/973\">#973</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.1.1</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix sync requests in async contexts for HTTPX (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/965\">#965</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump peter-evans/create-pull-request from 7 to 8 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/969\">#969</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.1.0</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Enable brotli decompression if available (via <code>brotli</code>,\n<code>brotlipy</code> or <code>brotlicffi</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/620\">#620</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/immerrr\"><code>@​immerrr</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix aiohttp allowing both <code>data</code> and <code>json</code>\narguments when one is None (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/624\">#624</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/leorochael\"><code>@​leorochael</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix usage of io-like interface with VCR.py (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/906\">#906</a>)\n- thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/tito\"><code>@​tito</code></a> and\n<a href=\"https://github.com/kevdevg\"><code>@​kevdevg</code></a></li>\n<li>Migrate to declarative Python package config (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/767\">#767</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/deronnax\"><code>@​deronnax</code></a></li>\n<li>Various linting fixes - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump actions/checkout from 5 to 6 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/955\">#955</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.0.0</p>\n<ul>\n<li>BREAKING: Drop support for Python 3.9 (major version bump) - thanks\n<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>BREAKING: Drop support for urllib3 &lt; 2 - fixes CVE warnings from\nurllib3 1.x (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/926\">#926</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/880\">#880</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>New feature: <code>drop_unused_requests</code> option to remove\nunused interactions from cassettes (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/763\">#763</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/danielnsilva\"><code>@​danielnsilva</code></a></li>\n<li>Rewrite httpx support to patch httpcore instead of httpx (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/943\">#943</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a>\n<ul>\n<li>Fixes <code>httpx.ResponseNotRead</code> exceptions (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/832\">#832</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/834\">#834</a>)</li>\n<li>Fixes <code>KeyError: 'follow_redirects'</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/945\">#945</a>)</li>\n<li>Adds support for custom httpx transports</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Fix HTTPS proxy handling - proxy address no longer ends up in\ncassette URIs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/809\">#809</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/914\">#914</a>)\n- thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/alga\"><code>@​alga</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix <code>iscoroutinefunction</code> deprecation warning on Python\n3.14 - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kloczek\"><code>@​kloczek</code></a></li>\n<li>Only log message if response is appended - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/talfus-laddus\"><code>@​talfus-laddus</code></a></li>\n<li>Optimize urllib.parse calls - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Martin-Brunthaler\"><code>@​Martin-Brunthaler</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix CI for Ubuntu 24.04 - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hartwork\"><code>@​hartwork</code></a></li>\n<li>Various CI improvements: migrate to uv, update GitHub Actions -\nthanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>Various linting and test improvements - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a>\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hartwork\"><code>@​hartwork</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/85312039e9ade8f1290f7e556b18d2889cf9f6e0\"><code>8531203</code></a>\nRelease v8.2.1</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/045acb1b5f8940f82adbb3faafd13e43e46289d6\"><code>045acb1</code></a>\nUse a safe YAML loader for cassettes to prevent code execution</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/de43f46247e763c2e36dc8dd9c36173be3069f81\"><code>de43f46</code></a>\nFix lint failures from merged PRs (codespell + ruff UP032)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/514c374796ba8b53402d3cad86682a7d3f0c34cc\"><code>514c374</code></a>\nValidate record_mode and raise a clear error on invalid values</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/b736cadd58d3f4088c0e440a1196e4b14d369dd2\"><code>b736cad</code></a>\ndocs: recommend pytest-recording over unmaintained pytest-vcr</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/06758c9879f18a46b24b450591a295ae9443d097\"><code>06758c9</code></a>\nRelease v8.2.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/6554837e023f97aee5edcc7cd8359408686cca98\"><code>6554837</code></a>\nAdd env proxy cassette regression test (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/994\">#994</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/62cf5e127201c050b6b8f8c8a20910eb7eab753a\"><code>62cf5e1</code></a>\nAccounting for modified requests when storing played cassettes, with a\ntest (...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/13f201a820b71288829df9470d629bfd0b4183de\"><code>13f201a</code></a>\nmake url available in VCRHTTPResponse (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/976\">#976</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/d57b55339e1bd386fed791621bb0094de2a8a4b2\"><code>d57b553</code></a>\nimprove error message on repeated requestt (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/985\">#985</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.1.1...v8.2.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=vcrpy&package-manager=uv&previous-version=8.1.1&new-version=8.2.1)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-22T18:31:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ce36f6536c04e3e94ef463a3fb0f120645663ce6","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ce36f6536c04e3e94ef463a3fb0f120645663ce6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ce36f6536c04e3e94ef463a3fb0f120645663ce6/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"37d5e8cafa2435159c6281c3ddaa3e4dc9a2a507","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/37d5e8cafa2435159c6281c3ddaa3e4dc9a2a507","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/37d5e8cafa2435159c6281c3ddaa3e4dc9a2a507"}]},{"sha":"37d5e8cafa2435159c6281c3ddaa3e4dc9a2a507","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDM3ZDVlOGNhZmEyNDM1MTU5YzYyODFjM2RkYWEzZTRkYzlhMmE1MDc","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-22T18:31:21Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T18:31:21Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump vcrpy from 8.1.1 to 8.2.1 in /libs/deepagents (#4123)\n\nBumps [vcrpy](https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy) from 8.1.1 to 8.2.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/releases\">vcrpy's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v8.2.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SECURITY:</strong> Cassettes are now loaded with a safe YAML\nloader, preventing arbitrary code execution when a cassette from an\nuntrusted source is loaded. Previously a crafted cassette containing a\nPython object tag (e.g. <code>!!python/object/apply:os.system</code>)\nwould execute code on load, including via the normal\n<code>vcr.use_cassette()</code> path. Existing cassettes (including\nfile-upload/streaming bodies) continue to load. Advisory:\nGHSA-rpj2-4hq8-938g — thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/RamiAltai\"><code>@​RamiAltai</code></a> and <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/EQSTLab\"><code>@​EQSTLab</code></a> for the\nreports.</li>\n<li>Validate <code>record_mode</code> and raise a clear error on an\ninvalid value (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/208\">#208</a>)</li>\n<li>Recommend pytest-recording over the unmaintained pytest-vcr in the\ndocs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/986\">#986</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.2.0...v8.2.1\">https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.2.0...v8.2.1</a></p>\n<h2>v8.2.0</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Add support for httpx 2.x (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/993\">#993</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Patch httpx transports instead of httpcore (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/972\">#972</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix aiohttp 3.14 compatibility: <code>AsyncStreamReaderMixin</code>\nremoved and <code>ClientResponse</code> now requires\n<code>stream_writer</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/995\">#995</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Account for modified requests when storing played cassettes, so\n<code>drop_unused_requests</code> honours\n<code>before_record_request</code> filtering (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/962\">#962</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jamesbraza\"><code>@​jamesbraza</code></a></li>\n<li>Make the request URL available on <code>VCRHTTPResponse</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/976\">#976</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dAnjou\"><code>@​dAnjou</code></a></li>\n<li>Improve error message when a matching request has already been\nconsumed (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/985\">#985</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix body check in <code>convert_body_to_unicode</code> to use an\nexplicit type check (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/982\">#982</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Add env proxy cassette regression test (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/994\">#994</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tine1117\"><code>@​tine1117</code></a></li>\n<li>Remove milestone references from docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/984\">#984</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump sphinx-rtd-theme from 3.0.2 to 3.1.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/973\">#973</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.1.1...v8.2.0\">https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.1.1...v8.2.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/blob/master/docs/changelog.rst\">vcrpy's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Changelog</h2>\n<p>All help in providing PRs to close out bug issues is appreciated.\nEven if that is providing a repo that fully replicates issues. We have\nvery generous contributors that have added these to bug issues which\nmeant another contributor picked up the bug and closed it out.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>8.2.1</p>\n<ul>\n<li>SECURITY: Load cassettes with a safe YAML loader, preventing\narbitrary code execution when a cassette from an untrusted source is\nloaded (GHSA-rpj2-4hq8-938g) - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/RamiAltai\"><code>@​RamiAltai</code></a> and <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/EQSTLab\"><code>@​EQSTLab</code></a></li>\n<li>Validate <code>record_mode</code> and raise a clear error on an\ninvalid value (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/208\">#208</a>)</li>\n<li>Recommend pytest-recording over the unmaintained pytest-vcr in the\ndocs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/986\">#986</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.2.0</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Add support for httpx 2.x (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/993\">#993</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Patch httpx transports instead of httpcore (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/972\">#972</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix aiohttp 3.14 compatibility: <code>AsyncStreamReaderMixin</code>\nremoved and <code>ClientResponse</code> now requires\n<code>stream_writer</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/995\">#995</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Account for modified requests when storing played cassettes, so\n<code>drop_unused_requests</code> honours\n<code>before_record_request</code> filtering (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/962\">#962</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jamesbraza\"><code>@​jamesbraza</code></a></li>\n<li>Make the request URL available on <code>VCRHTTPResponse</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/976\">#976</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dAnjou\"><code>@​dAnjou</code></a></li>\n<li>Improve error message when a matching request has already been\nconsumed (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/985\">#985</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix body check in <code>convert_body_to_unicode</code> to use an\nexplicit type check (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/982\">#982</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Add env proxy cassette regression test (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/994\">#994</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tine1117\"><code>@​tine1117</code></a></li>\n<li>Remove milestone references from docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/984\">#984</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump sphinx-rtd-theme from 3.0.2 to 3.1.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/973\">#973</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.1.1</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix sync requests in async contexts for HTTPX (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/965\">#965</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump peter-evans/create-pull-request from 7 to 8 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/969\">#969</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.1.0</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Enable brotli decompression if available (via <code>brotli</code>,\n<code>brotlipy</code> or <code>brotlicffi</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/620\">#620</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/immerrr\"><code>@​immerrr</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix aiohttp allowing both <code>data</code> and <code>json</code>\narguments when one is None (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/624\">#624</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/leorochael\"><code>@​leorochael</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix usage of io-like interface with VCR.py (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/906\">#906</a>)\n- thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/tito\"><code>@​tito</code></a> and\n<a href=\"https://github.com/kevdevg\"><code>@​kevdevg</code></a></li>\n<li>Migrate to declarative Python package config (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/767\">#767</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/deronnax\"><code>@​deronnax</code></a></li>\n<li>Various linting fixes - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump actions/checkout from 5 to 6 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/955\">#955</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.0.0</p>\n<ul>\n<li>BREAKING: Drop support for Python 3.9 (major version bump) - thanks\n<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>BREAKING: Drop support for urllib3 &lt; 2 - fixes CVE warnings from\nurllib3 1.x (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/926\">#926</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/880\">#880</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>New feature: <code>drop_unused_requests</code> option to remove\nunused interactions from cassettes (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/763\">#763</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/danielnsilva\"><code>@​danielnsilva</code></a></li>\n<li>Rewrite httpx support to patch httpcore instead of httpx (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/943\">#943</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a>\n<ul>\n<li>Fixes <code>httpx.ResponseNotRead</code> exceptions (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/832\">#832</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/834\">#834</a>)</li>\n<li>Fixes <code>KeyError: 'follow_redirects'</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/945\">#945</a>)</li>\n<li>Adds support for custom httpx transports</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Fix HTTPS proxy handling - proxy address no longer ends up in\ncassette URIs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/809\">#809</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/914\">#914</a>)\n- thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/alga\"><code>@​alga</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix <code>iscoroutinefunction</code> deprecation warning on Python\n3.14 - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kloczek\"><code>@​kloczek</code></a></li>\n<li>Only log message if response is appended - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/talfus-laddus\"><code>@​talfus-laddus</code></a></li>\n<li>Optimize urllib.parse calls - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Martin-Brunthaler\"><code>@​Martin-Brunthaler</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix CI for Ubuntu 24.04 - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hartwork\"><code>@​hartwork</code></a></li>\n<li>Various CI improvements: migrate to uv, update GitHub Actions -\nthanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>Various linting and test improvements - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a>\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hartwork\"><code>@​hartwork</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/85312039e9ade8f1290f7e556b18d2889cf9f6e0\"><code>8531203</code></a>\nRelease v8.2.1</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/045acb1b5f8940f82adbb3faafd13e43e46289d6\"><code>045acb1</code></a>\nUse a safe YAML loader for cassettes to prevent code execution</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/de43f46247e763c2e36dc8dd9c36173be3069f81\"><code>de43f46</code></a>\nFix lint failures from merged PRs (codespell + ruff UP032)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/514c374796ba8b53402d3cad86682a7d3f0c34cc\"><code>514c374</code></a>\nValidate record_mode and raise a clear error on invalid values</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/b736cadd58d3f4088c0e440a1196e4b14d369dd2\"><code>b736cad</code></a>\ndocs: recommend pytest-recording over unmaintained pytest-vcr</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/06758c9879f18a46b24b450591a295ae9443d097\"><code>06758c9</code></a>\nRelease v8.2.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/6554837e023f97aee5edcc7cd8359408686cca98\"><code>6554837</code></a>\nAdd env proxy cassette regression test (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/994\">#994</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/62cf5e127201c050b6b8f8c8a20910eb7eab753a\"><code>62cf5e1</code></a>\nAccounting for modified requests when storing played cassettes, with a\ntest (...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/13f201a820b71288829df9470d629bfd0b4183de\"><code>13f201a</code></a>\nmake url available in VCRHTTPResponse (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/976\">#976</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/d57b55339e1bd386fed791621bb0094de2a8a4b2\"><code>d57b553</code></a>\nimprove error message on repeated requestt (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/985\">#985</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.1.1...v8.2.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=vcrpy&package-manager=uv&previous-version=8.1.1&new-version=8.2.1)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"e1d81bb74885034bbcfc32155edf7127ad44bc22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e1d81bb74885034bbcfc32155edf7127ad44bc22"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/37d5e8cafa2435159c6281c3ddaa3e4dc9a2a507","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOX95CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHfMQAJp5zUOXiFuzF7dgJLvoT7RH\nasax17EU+rjLr6NQghRaN0ZxkTQhaUHp7dmbHbuT/3A3GBqF4spie5O2TJiy+crQ\nkqnSvY8uIqb+JLjK18bKdl8eODEYypE5ichiHmf0AbLsrQ7bpqm2opJMxPO2sS0m\n2c1t5aybtLIRDX9EmJN2QPji4x5pykL6sbue7lKZHTxW/nDtG62i88Dgo4JF85pz\nN1y2Sd3EK9J3wpUiucJqJ26fuB4zTf9Kd3VP/pwsCYJR0on4Yar8CmEBeF0aKN5q\nGnzaHrweRZCBiu3mgRaNQ7SuEiACM/ulGCbPY16CXr5LG9d1M2s7aKUaGI01xcel\nUVpjBypGS+4qmk6dKp5efNIZ/+x5jMmGreIirr+K/KcboXfjts/mhxoamQ4WviGZ\ns270pWU2skG9CBT7OniPLCsMVQlYPwr5J+bSYAdvJEGMG3FuFNScVdcn+zsJekeX\nrHG6LkzZjfKbSjE+fof/7Gt1IjJ2tf4tvkrSufhovatk+Eekj1y4XfueOJa8mqGd\nfZJFvqc4YJOYDf0+X9VqhIWsumi61X5l7+u61D22jCJXD92ILz6YVEg8MuxhjAeA\nHre0zeq0g+a/3Bvwqj2FHuDWAAyLe0Z1AdSbHjgxwa5EM7WO9A09IEkiy6/Q29ic\nHFbYZdBFuWhPrMLlhnp8\n=be/W\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e1d81bb74885034bbcfc32155edf7127ad44bc22\nparent c120a2f31613dd448c3d78994aacbb5a34dd62e3\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1782153081 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782153081 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump vcrpy from 8.1.1 to 8.2.1 in /libs/deepagents (#4123)\n\nBumps [vcrpy](https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy) from 8.1.1 to 8.2.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/releases\">vcrpy's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v8.2.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SECURITY:</strong> Cassettes are now loaded with a safe YAML\nloader, preventing arbitrary code execution when a cassette from an\nuntrusted source is loaded. Previously a crafted cassette containing a\nPython object tag (e.g. <code>!!python/object/apply:os.system</code>)\nwould execute code on load, including via the normal\n<code>vcr.use_cassette()</code> path. Existing cassettes (including\nfile-upload/streaming bodies) continue to load. Advisory:\nGHSA-rpj2-4hq8-938g — thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/RamiAltai\"><code>@​RamiAltai</code></a> and <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/EQSTLab\"><code>@​EQSTLab</code></a> for the\nreports.</li>\n<li>Validate <code>record_mode</code> and raise a clear error on an\ninvalid value (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/208\">#208</a>)</li>\n<li>Recommend pytest-recording over the unmaintained pytest-vcr in the\ndocs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/986\">#986</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.2.0...v8.2.1\">https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.2.0...v8.2.1</a></p>\n<h2>v8.2.0</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Add support for httpx 2.x (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/993\">#993</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Patch httpx transports instead of httpcore (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/972\">#972</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix aiohttp 3.14 compatibility: <code>AsyncStreamReaderMixin</code>\nremoved and <code>ClientResponse</code> now requires\n<code>stream_writer</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/995\">#995</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Account for modified requests when storing played cassettes, so\n<code>drop_unused_requests</code> honours\n<code>before_record_request</code> filtering (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/962\">#962</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jamesbraza\"><code>@​jamesbraza</code></a></li>\n<li>Make the request URL available on <code>VCRHTTPResponse</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/976\">#976</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dAnjou\"><code>@​dAnjou</code></a></li>\n<li>Improve error message when a matching request has already been\nconsumed (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/985\">#985</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix body check in <code>convert_body_to_unicode</code> to use an\nexplicit type check (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/982\">#982</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Add env proxy cassette regression test (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/994\">#994</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tine1117\"><code>@​tine1117</code></a></li>\n<li>Remove milestone references from docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/984\">#984</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump sphinx-rtd-theme from 3.0.2 to 3.1.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/973\">#973</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.1.1...v8.2.0\">https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.1.1...v8.2.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/blob/master/docs/changelog.rst\">vcrpy's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Changelog</h2>\n<p>All help in providing PRs to close out bug issues is appreciated.\nEven if that is providing a repo that fully replicates issues. We have\nvery generous contributors that have added these to bug issues which\nmeant another contributor picked up the bug and closed it out.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>8.2.1</p>\n<ul>\n<li>SECURITY: Load cassettes with a safe YAML loader, preventing\narbitrary code execution when a cassette from an untrusted source is\nloaded (GHSA-rpj2-4hq8-938g) - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/RamiAltai\"><code>@​RamiAltai</code></a> and <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/EQSTLab\"><code>@​EQSTLab</code></a></li>\n<li>Validate <code>record_mode</code> and raise a clear error on an\ninvalid value (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/208\">#208</a>)</li>\n<li>Recommend pytest-recording over the unmaintained pytest-vcr in the\ndocs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/986\">#986</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.2.0</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Add support for httpx 2.x (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/993\">#993</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Patch httpx transports instead of httpcore (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/972\">#972</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix aiohttp 3.14 compatibility: <code>AsyncStreamReaderMixin</code>\nremoved and <code>ClientResponse</code> now requires\n<code>stream_writer</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/995\">#995</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dsfaccini\"><code>@​dsfaccini</code></a></li>\n<li>Account for modified requests when storing played cassettes, so\n<code>drop_unused_requests</code> honours\n<code>before_record_request</code> filtering (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/962\">#962</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jamesbraza\"><code>@​jamesbraza</code></a></li>\n<li>Make the request URL available on <code>VCRHTTPResponse</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/976\">#976</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dAnjou\"><code>@​dAnjou</code></a></li>\n<li>Improve error message when a matching request has already been\nconsumed (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/985\">#985</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix body check in <code>convert_body_to_unicode</code> to use an\nexplicit type check (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/982\">#982</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>Add env proxy cassette regression test (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/994\">#994</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tine1117\"><code>@​tine1117</code></a></li>\n<li>Remove milestone references from docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/984\">#984</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Polandia94\"><code>@​Polandia94</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump sphinx-rtd-theme from 3.0.2 to 3.1.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/973\">#973</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.1.1</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix sync requests in async contexts for HTTPX (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/965\">#965</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump peter-evans/create-pull-request from 7 to 8 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/969\">#969</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.1.0</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Enable brotli decompression if available (via <code>brotli</code>,\n<code>brotlipy</code> or <code>brotlicffi</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/620\">#620</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/immerrr\"><code>@​immerrr</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix aiohttp allowing both <code>data</code> and <code>json</code>\narguments when one is None (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/624\">#624</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/leorochael\"><code>@​leorochael</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix usage of io-like interface with VCR.py (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/906\">#906</a>)\n- thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/tito\"><code>@​tito</code></a> and\n<a href=\"https://github.com/kevdevg\"><code>@​kevdevg</code></a></li>\n<li>Migrate to declarative Python package config (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/767\">#767</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/deronnax\"><code>@​deronnax</code></a></li>\n<li>Various linting fixes - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>CI: bump actions/checkout from 5 to 6 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/955\">#955</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>8.0.0</p>\n<ul>\n<li>BREAKING: Drop support for Python 3.9 (major version bump) - thanks\n<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>BREAKING: Drop support for urllib3 &lt; 2 - fixes CVE warnings from\nurllib3 1.x (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/926\">#926</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/880\">#880</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>New feature: <code>drop_unused_requests</code> option to remove\nunused interactions from cassettes (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/763\">#763</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/danielnsilva\"><code>@​danielnsilva</code></a></li>\n<li>Rewrite httpx support to patch httpcore instead of httpx (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/943\">#943</a>)\n- thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/seowalex\"><code>@​seowalex</code></a>\n<ul>\n<li>Fixes <code>httpx.ResponseNotRead</code> exceptions (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/832\">#832</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/834\">#834</a>)</li>\n<li>Fixes <code>KeyError: 'follow_redirects'</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/945\">#945</a>)</li>\n<li>Adds support for custom httpx transports</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Fix HTTPS proxy handling - proxy address no longer ends up in\ncassette URIs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/809\">#809</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/914\">#914</a>)\n- thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/alga\"><code>@​alga</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix <code>iscoroutinefunction</code> deprecation warning on Python\n3.14 - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kloczek\"><code>@​kloczek</code></a></li>\n<li>Only log message if response is appended - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/talfus-laddus\"><code>@​talfus-laddus</code></a></li>\n<li>Optimize urllib.parse calls - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Martin-Brunthaler\"><code>@​Martin-Brunthaler</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix CI for Ubuntu 24.04 - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hartwork\"><code>@​hartwork</code></a></li>\n<li>Various CI improvements: migrate to uv, update GitHub Actions -\nthanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a></li>\n<li>Various linting and test improvements - thanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jairhenrique\"><code>@​jairhenrique</code></a>\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hartwork\"><code>@​hartwork</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/85312039e9ade8f1290f7e556b18d2889cf9f6e0\"><code>8531203</code></a>\nRelease v8.2.1</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/045acb1b5f8940f82adbb3faafd13e43e46289d6\"><code>045acb1</code></a>\nUse a safe YAML loader for cassettes to prevent code execution</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/de43f46247e763c2e36dc8dd9c36173be3069f81\"><code>de43f46</code></a>\nFix lint failures from merged PRs (codespell + ruff UP032)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/514c374796ba8b53402d3cad86682a7d3f0c34cc\"><code>514c374</code></a>\nValidate record_mode and raise a clear error on invalid values</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/b736cadd58d3f4088c0e440a1196e4b14d369dd2\"><code>b736cad</code></a>\ndocs: recommend pytest-recording over unmaintained pytest-vcr</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/06758c9879f18a46b24b450591a295ae9443d097\"><code>06758c9</code></a>\nRelease v8.2.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/6554837e023f97aee5edcc7cd8359408686cca98\"><code>6554837</code></a>\nAdd env proxy cassette regression test (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/994\">#994</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/62cf5e127201c050b6b8f8c8a20910eb7eab753a\"><code>62cf5e1</code></a>\nAccounting for modified requests when storing played cassettes, with a\ntest (...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/13f201a820b71288829df9470d629bfd0b4183de\"><code>13f201a</code></a>\nmake url available in VCRHTTPResponse (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/976\">#976</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/commit/d57b55339e1bd386fed791621bb0094de2a8a4b2\"><code>d57b553</code></a>\nimprove error message on repeated requestt (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/issues/985\">#985</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy/compare/v8.1.1...v8.2.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=vcrpy&package-manager=uv&previous-version=8.1.1&new-version=8.2.1)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-22T18:31:21Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/37d5e8cafa2435159c6281c3ddaa3e4dc9a2a507","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/37d5e8cafa2435159c6281c3ddaa3e4dc9a2a507","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/37d5e8cafa2435159c6281c3ddaa3e4dc9a2a507/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c120a2f31613dd448c3d78994aacbb5a34dd62e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c120a2f31613dd448c3d78994aacbb5a34dd62e3","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c120a2f31613dd448c3d78994aacbb5a34dd62e3"}]},{"sha":"c120a2f31613dd448c3d78994aacbb5a34dd62e3","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGMxMjBhMmYzMTYxM2RkNDQ4YzNkNzg5OTRhYWNiYjVhMzRkZDYyZTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-22T18:31:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T18:31:16Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump langsmith from 0.8.11 to 0.8.18 in /libs/deepagents (#4124)\n\nBumps [langsmith](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk) from\n0.8.11 to 0.8.18.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/releases\">langsmith's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v0.8.18</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>chore(deps-dev): bump vitest from 3.2.4 to 3.2.6 in /js by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3002\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3002</a></li>\n<li>chore(deps): bump pyjwt from 2.12.1 to 2.13.0 in /python by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3030\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3030</a></li>\n<li>chore(deps): bump python-multipart from 0.0.27 to 0.0.31 in /python\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3036\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3036</a></li>\n<li>chore(deps): bump aiohttp from 3.14.0 to 3.14.1 in /python by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3037\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3037</a></li>\n<li>chore(deps): bump cryptography from 46.0.7 to 48.0.1 in /python by\n<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3038\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3038</a></li>\n<li>chore(deps): bump starlette from 1.0.1 to 1.3.1 in /python by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3039\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3039</a></li>\n<li>chore(deps-dev): bump langchain-anthropic from 1.4.4 to 1.4.6 in\n/python by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3044\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3044</a></li>\n<li>chore(deps): bump the npm_and_yarn group across 4 directories with 4\nupdates by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3046\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3046</a></li>\n<li>chore(deps): bump the npm_and_yarn group across 2 directories with 2\nupdates by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3060\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3060</a></li>\n<li>test(python): fix integration assertions for updated attachment\nerror message by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/QuentinBrosse\"><code>@​QuentinBrosse</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3061\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3061</a></li>\n<li>chore: reconcile bumpversion config and mandate release process for\nagents by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/QuentinBrosse\"><code>@​QuentinBrosse</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3062\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3062</a></li>\n<li>release(py): 0.8.18 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/QuentinBrosse\"><code>@​QuentinBrosse</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3063\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3063</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/compare/v0.8.17...v0.8.18\">https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/compare/v0.8.17...v0.8.18</a></p>\n<h2>v0.8.17</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>feat: expose the resources from the generated openapi client in the\nlangsmith client by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sineha-mani\"><code>@​sineha-mani</code></a> in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3018\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3018</a></li>\n<li>feat(js): port <code>isTracingEnabled</code> utility from Python by\n<a href=\"https://github.com/dqbd\"><code>@​dqbd</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3032\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3032</a></li>\n<li>Add sandbox mount support to JS SDK by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DanielKneipp\"><code>@​DanielKneipp</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3010\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3010</a></li>\n<li>release(js): bump to 0.7.9 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dqbd\"><code>@​dqbd</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3035\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3035</a></li>\n<li>Add sandbox mount support to Python SDK by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DanielKneipp\"><code>@​DanielKneipp</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3009\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3009</a></li>\n<li>docs: note that _openapi_client directories are auto-generated by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/KiewanVillatel\"><code>@​KiewanVillatel</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3034\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3034</a></li>\n<li>fix: update JS SDK type declarations with skipLibCheck disabled by\n<a href=\"https://github.com/sineha-mani\"><code>@​sineha-mani</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3043\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3043</a></li>\n<li>release(js): 0.7.10 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dqbd\"><code>@​dqbd</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3045\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3045</a></li>\n<li>feat: adding python async for online evals by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sineha-mani\"><code>@​sineha-mani</code></a> in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3048\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3048</a></li>\n<li>Add sandbox Git mount SDK helpers by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DanielKneipp\"><code>@​DanielKneipp</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3040\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3040</a></li>\n<li>fix: use insights tab in sdk report links [closes LSO-2936] by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/eric-langchain\"><code>@​eric-langchain</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3050\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3050</a></li>\n<li>feat(client): warn when backend version is below minimum required by\n<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/KiewanVillatel\"><code>@​KiewanVillatel</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3041\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3041</a></li>\n<li>chore: bump _MIN_BACKEND_VERSION to 0.16.5rc1 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langtions-bot\"><code>@​langtions-bot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3053\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3053</a></li>\n<li>fix(sandbox): use built-in gcp auth host matching by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DanielKneipp\"><code>@​DanielKneipp</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3055\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3055</a></li>\n<li>chore(python): py to 0.8.17 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sineha-mani\"><code>@​sineha-mani</code></a> in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3056\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3056</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>New Contributors</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sineha-mani\"><code>@​sineha-mani</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3018\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3018</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/eric-langchain\"><code>@​eric-langchain</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3050\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3050</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/compare/v0.8.16...v0.8.17\">https://github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/compare/v0.8.16...v0.8.17</a></p>\n<h2>v0.8.16</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>feat(py): add sync/async conversion for Sandbox and SandboxClient\n[INF-0000] by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ramon-langchain\"><code>@​ramon-langchain</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3019\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3019</a></li>\n<li>fix(experiments): extract keys from wrapped evaluator function by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/shamikkarkhanis\"><code>@​shamikkarkhanis</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3014\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3014</a></li>\n<li>chore: repoint <a\nhref=\"mailto:support@langchain.dev\">support@langchain.dev</a> mentions\nto the Support Portal by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lutan-langchain\"><code>@​lutan-langchain</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3024\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3024</a></li>\n<li>fix(python): derive create_child run id from start_time [LSDK-220]\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/harisaiharish\"><code>@​harisaiharish</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3027\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3027</a></li>\n<li>chore: sync langsmith_api by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/langtions-bot\"><code>@​langtions-bot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk/pull/3020\">langchain-ai/langsmith-sdk#3020</a></li>\n<li>chore: js to 0.7.8 and py to 0.8.16 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/shamikkarkhanis\"><code>@​s